IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb3-nouns`
IMPORT `cb3-part11-insider-trading`
IMPORT `cb3-part12-meetings`
IMPORT `cb3-part12-proposals`
IMPORT `cb3-part12-voting`
IMPORT `cb3-part12-requisition-agreements`
IMPORT `cb3-part13-proxies`
IMPORT `cb3-part14-statements`
IMPORT `cb3-part14-auditor`
IMPORT `cb3-part14-1-diversity`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Parts XI to XIV.1 (ss 126 to 172.1) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice Canada
-- consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version, and nothing here has
-- been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds shares in a corporation under the Canada Business Corporations Act
-- (an incorporator, a director or officer, or a shareholder, including a minority shareholder), asking what the Act lets
-- them do, what it requires of them, what they may require of the corporation, and what can be done to them.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules of the modules imported above as the questions that person would ask, in the order of the
-- text. Nothing here is new law: each question takes plain inputs (yes/no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices), one
-- for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as that person would be asked, and calls the module's rule.
-- Where the text gives the person a claim, privilege, power or immunity, the facts about the other party on which the text
-- makes it depend are asked as inputs, and where the text also puts a duty or a liability on the person, the paired
-- question is asked in the person's own voice ("Must I ...?", "What can be done to me if ...?"). Where a relation is seen
-- from the other side (a director's duty, a shareholder's claim), both questions call the SAME module rule.
-- A figure the Act leaves to the regulations ("the prescribed period", "the prescribed percentage") is asked as a fact, because
-- the regulations are not among the sources; a judgment the Act leaves to a court or the Director is asked as a fact too
-- ("if the court is satisfied that ..."). A court's order or the Director's decision is never decided here.
-- Dates carry no time of day, and "forthwith" and "without delay" are the person's own judgment.

§ `Canada Business Corporations Act, Parts XI to XIV.1 -- the questions of an incorporator, director, officer or shareholder`


§§ `Who is an insider, and what the Act counts as mine (ss 126 and 131)`

-- Only if you are a director, officer, employee or large shareholder of a distributing corporation, or deal with one, or have received confidential information about one. A distributing corporation is a corporation whose securities have been distributed to the public.

-- s 126(1). "Insider", everywhere in the Act except section 131 (which has its own definition, asked below): a director or officer of a
-- distributing corporation, of its subsidiary, or of a body corporate that enters into a business combination with it; or a person employed or retained by it.
-- The first input of the rule ("the term is used in section 131") is fixed FALSE: this question is about every use of "insider" except
-- the one in section 131, which has its own question (s 131(1)).
@ref CBCA s 126(1) insider
@export Am I an insider of a distributing corporation (s 126(1))?
GIVEN `I am a director or officer of a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of a distributing corporation?
      `I am a director or officer of a subsidiary of a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of a subsidiary of a distributing corporation?
      `I am a director or officer of a body corporate that is entering into a business combination with a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of a body corporate that is entering into a business combination (an acquisition of all or substantially all of its property, an amalgamation, or a similar reorganization) with a distributing corporation?
      `I am employed or retained by a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed or retained by a distributing corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an insider of a distributing corporation` IF
    `insider within s 126(1)` FALSE `I am a director or officer of a distributing corporation` `I am a director or officer of a subsidiary of a distributing corporation` `I am a director or officer of a body corporate that is entering into a business combination with a distributing corporation` `I am employed or retained by a distributing corporation`

-- s 126(1). "Officer" for Part XI: the listed offices of an entity, or another individual performing similar functions. Unlike s 2(1),
-- an officer appointed under section 121 who holds none of the offices does not count here.
@ref CBCA s 126(1) officer
@export Am I an officer for the purposes of Part XI (s 126(1))?
GIVEN `the office I hold or the function I perform` IS AN Office @desc Which office do you hold, or what function do you perform, in the body (the chairperson of the board, the president, a vice-president, the secretary, the treasurer, the comptroller, the general counsel, the general manager, a managing director, another individual performing similar functions, or none of these)?
      `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an individual (a natural person)?
      `the kind of body that I hold the office in` IS A `Kind of person or entity` @desc What kind of body is it (an individual, a partnership, an association, a body corporate, a personal representative, a trust, a joint venture, or an unincorporated association or organization)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an officer for the purposes of Part XI` IF
    `officer within s 126(1)` `the office I hold or the function I perform` `I am an individual` `the kind of body that I hold the office in`

-- s 126(1). "Share" for Part XI: a share carrying voting rights always or because of an event that is continuing, and, included, a currently
-- convertible security or currently exercisable option or right to acquire one.
@ref CBCA s 126(1) share
@export Is what I hold a share for the purposes of Part XI (s 126(1))?
GIVEN `what I hold is a share carrying voting rights under all circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you hold a share that carries voting rights in all circumstances?
      `what I hold is a share carrying voting rights by reason of an event that is continuing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does what you hold carry voting rights because of an event that has occurred and is continuing?
      `what I hold is a security currently convertible into such a share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you hold a security that you can currently convert into such a share?
      `what I hold is a currently exercisable option or right to acquire such a share or such a security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you hold a currently exercisable option or right to acquire such a share, or such a convertible security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I hold a share for the purposes of Part XI` IF
    `share within s 126(1)` `what I hold is a share carrying voting rights under all circumstances` `what I hold is a share carrying voting rights by reason of an event that is continuing` `what I hold is a security currently convertible into such a share` `what I hold is a currently exercisable option or right to acquire such a share or such a security`

-- s 126(2)(a). A director or officer of a body corporate that owns, controls or directs more than the prescribed percentage of the voting rights of a
-- distributing corporation is deemed an insider of it. Exactly the prescribed percentage is not "more than".
@ref CBCA s 126(2)(a)
@export Am I deemed an insider because my body corporate holds a large block of voting shares (s 126(2)(a))?
GIVEN `I am a director or an officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of the body corporate that holds the shares?
      `the fraction of the voting rights that the body corporate owns, controls or directs` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the voting rights attached to all the outstanding shares of the distributing corporation does the body corporate own, control or direct (as a number between 0 and 1, not counting shares it holds as underwriter during a public distribution)?
      `the percentage that the regulations prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the regulations prescribe for this purpose (as a number between 0 and 1)? The Act leaves this figure to the regulations.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed an insider because my body corporate holds a large block of voting shares` IF
    `deemed insider within s 126(2)(a)` `I am a director or an officer of the body corporate` `the fraction of the voting rights that the body corporate owns, controls or directs` `the percentage that the regulations prescribe`

-- s 126(2)(b). A director or officer of a subsidiary is deemed an insider of its holding distributing corporation.
@ref CBCA s 126(2)(b)
@export Am I deemed an insider of the holding corporation because I run its subsidiary (s 126(2)(b))?
GIVEN `I am a director or an officer of a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of a body corporate?
      `the body corporate is a subsidiary of a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body corporate a subsidiary of a distributing corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed an insider of the holding corporation because I run its subsidiary` IF
    `deemed insider within s 126(2)(b)` `I am a director or an officer of a body corporate` `the body corporate is a subsidiary of a distributing corporation`

-- s 126(2)(c). A person is deemed to own beneficially the shares that a body corporate they control, directly or indirectly, owns beneficially.
@ref CBCA s 126(2)(c)
@export How many shares am I deemed to own beneficially (s 126(2)(c))?
GIVEN `the shares I beneficially own myself` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares do you yourself beneficially own?
      `the shares beneficially owned by each body corporate that I control` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each body corporate that you control, directly or indirectly, how many shares does it beneficially own? Give a list of numbers, one for each body corporate.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many shares am I deemed to own beneficially` IS
    `shares deemed beneficially owned by a person within s 126(2)(c)` `the shares I beneficially own myself` `the shares beneficially owned by each body corporate that I control`

-- s 126(2)(d). A body corporate is deemed to own beneficially the shares that each of its affiliates owns beneficially.
@ref CBCA s 126(2)(d)
@export How many shares is my body corporate deemed to own beneficially (s 126(2)(d))?
GIVEN `the shares my body corporate beneficially owns itself` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares does your body corporate beneficially own itself?
      `the shares beneficially owned by each affiliate of my body corporate` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each affiliate of your body corporate, how many shares does it beneficially own? Give a list of numbers, one for each affiliate.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many shares is my body corporate deemed to own beneficially` IS
    `shares deemed beneficially owned by a body corporate within s 126(2)(d)` `the shares my body corporate beneficially owns itself` `the shares beneficially owned by each affiliate of my body corporate`

-- s 126(2)(e). For an insider, an acquisition or disposition of an option or right to acquire a share is deemed a change in beneficial ownership.
@ref CBCA s 126(2)(e)
@export Is my acquisition or disposition of an option treated as a change in my beneficial ownership (s 126(2)(e))?
GIVEN `I am an insider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an insider?
      `the transaction is an acquisition or disposition of an option or right to acquire a share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the transaction an acquisition or a disposition of an option or right to acquire a share?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my acquisition or disposition of an option treated as a change in my beneficial ownership` IF
    `change in beneficial ownership deemed within s 126(2)(e)` `I am an insider` `the transaction is an acquisition or disposition of an option or right to acquire a share`


§§ `Selling short, puts and calls (s 130)`

-- Only if you are an insider of a distributing corporation and have sold, or are thinking of selling, its securities short, or of selling a call or buying a put.

-- s 130(1). No insider of a distributing corporation shall knowingly sell, directly or indirectly, a security of the corporation or of an affiliate
-- if the insider does not own it or has not fully paid for it.
@ref CBCA s 130(1)
@export Am I barred from selling a security short (s 130(1))?
GIVEN `I am an insider of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an insider of the corporation?
      `I knowingly sold the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly sell the security, directly or indirectly?
      `the security is one of a distributing corporation or of one of its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the security one issued by the distributing corporation or by one of its affiliates?
      `I did not own the security I sold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not own the security you sold?
      `I had not fully paid for the security I sold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had you not fully paid for the security you sold?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from selling a security short` IF
    `a short sale is prohibited within s 130(1)` `I am an insider of the corporation` `I knowingly sold the security` `the security is one of a distributing corporation or of one of its affiliates` `I did not own the security I sold` `I had not fully paid for the security I sold`

-- s 130(2). No insider shall knowingly, directly or indirectly, sell a call or buy a put in respect of a security of the corporation or an affiliate.
@ref CBCA s 130(2)
@export Am I barred from selling a call or buying a put (s 130(2))?
GIVEN `I am an insider of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an insider of the corporation?
      `I knowingly sold a call` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly sell a call (a right for the buyer to buy a security from you)?
      `I knowingly bought a put` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly buy a put (a right for you to sell a security to the other party)?
      `the call or put is in respect of a security of the corporation or of one of its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the call or put in respect of a security of the corporation or of one of its affiliates?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I barred from selling a call or buying a put` IF
    `selling a call or buying a put is prohibited within s 130(2)` `I am an insider of the corporation` `I knowingly sold a call` `I knowingly bought a put` `the call or put is in respect of a security of the corporation or of one of its affiliates`

-- s 130(3). An insider who owns a convertible security, option or right to acquire the security sold is not caught by s 130(1) if, within ten days after the sale, they
-- exercise it and deliver the security, or transfer it to the purchaser.
@ref CBCA s 130(3)
@export Does the exception for owners of a convertible security or option apply to my sale (s 130(3))?
GIVEN `I did not own the security I sold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not own the security you sold?
      `I own another security convertible into the security I sold, or an option or right to acquire it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you own another security that you can convert into the security you sold, or an option or right to acquire it?
      `the date of the sale` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the sale?
      `I exercised the conversion privilege, option or right and delivered the security to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you exercise the conversion privilege, option or right and deliver the security so acquired to the purchaser?
      `the date I exercised it and delivered the security to the purchaser` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you exercise it and deliver the security to the purchaser?
      `I transferred the convertible security, option or right to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you transfer the convertible security, option or right to the purchaser?
      `the date I transferred it to the purchaser` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you transfer it to the purchaser?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the exception for owners of a convertible security or option apply to my sale` IF
    `the exception to a short sale applies within s 130(3)` `I did not own the security I sold` `I own another security convertible into the security I sold, or an option or right to acquire it` `the date of the sale` (IF `I exercised the conversion privilege, option or right and delivered the security to the purchaser` THEN JUST `the date I exercised it and delivered the security to the purchaser` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `I transferred the convertible security, option or right to the purchaser` THEN JUST `the date I transferred it to the purchaser` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 130(4). An insider who contravenes s 130(1) or (2) is guilty of an offence. The rule works out the contravention from the three provisions above.
@ref CBCA s 130(4)
@export Am I guilty of an offence for a short sale, call or put (s 130(4))?
GIVEN `I am an insider of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an insider of the corporation?
      `I knowingly sold the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly sell the security, directly or indirectly?
      `the security is one of a distributing corporation or of one of its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the security one issued by the distributing corporation or by one of its affiliates?
      `I did not own the security I sold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not own the security you sold?
      `I had not fully paid for the security I sold` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had you not fully paid for the security you sold?
      `I own another security convertible into the security I sold, or an option or right to acquire it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you own another security that you can convert into the security you sold, or an option or right to acquire it?
      `the date of the sale` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the sale?
      `I exercised the conversion privilege, option or right and delivered the security to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you exercise the conversion privilege, option or right and deliver the security so acquired to the purchaser?
      `the date I exercised it and delivered the security to the purchaser` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you exercise it and deliver the security to the purchaser?
      `I transferred the convertible security, option or right to the purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you transfer the convertible security, option or right to the purchaser?
      `the date I transferred it to the purchaser` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you transfer it to the purchaser?
      `I knowingly sold a call` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly sell a call (a right for the buyer to buy a security from you)?
      `I knowingly bought a put` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly buy a put (a right for you to sell a security to the other party)?
      `the call or put is in respect of a security of the corporation or of one of its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the call or put in respect of a security of the corporation or of one of its affiliates?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence for a short sale, call or put` IF
    `the insider is guilty of an offence within s 130(4)`
        (`the insider contravenes s 130(1) or (2) within s 130(4)`
            (`a short sale is prohibited within s 130(1)` `I am an insider of the corporation` `I knowingly sold the security` `the security is one of a distributing corporation or of one of its affiliates` `I did not own the security I sold` `I had not fully paid for the security I sold`)
            (`the exception to a short sale applies within s 130(3)` `I did not own the security I sold` `I own another security convertible into the security I sold, or an option or right to acquire it` `the date of the sale` (IF `I exercised the conversion privilege, option or right and delivered the security to the purchaser` THEN JUST `the date I exercised it and delivered the security to the purchaser` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `I transferred the convertible security, option or right to the purchaser` THEN JUST `the date I transferred it to the purchaser` ELSE NOTHING))
            (`selling a call or buying a put is prohibited within s 130(2)` `I am an insider of the corporation` `I knowingly sold a call` `I knowingly bought a put` `the call or put is in respect of a security of the corporation or of one of its affiliates`))

-- s 130(4). On summary conviction the fine does not exceed the greater of $1,000,000 and three times the profit made; the ceiling is not the sentence.
@ref CBCA s 130(4) fine
@export What is the most I can be fined for a short sale, call or put (s 130(4))?
GIVEN `the profit I made, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What profit did you make from the contravention, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for a short sale, call or put` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 130(4)` `the profit I made, in dollars`)'s `maximum fine in dollars`

-- s 130(4). The offence is punishable on summary conviction by imprisonment for up to six months; the ceiling is not the sentence.
@ref CBCA s 130(4) imprisonment
@export What is the longest imprisonment I can face for a short sale, call or put, in months (s 130(4))?
GIVEN `the profit I made, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What profit did you make from the contravention, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment I can face for a short sale, call or put, in months` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 130(4)` `the profit I made, in dollars`)'s `maximum imprisonment in months`


§§ `Insiders under section 131, and trading or tipping on confidential information (s 131)`

-- Only if you hold, or have received, confidential information about a corporation, or have traded with someone who did.

-- s 131(1). "Insider" in section 131, with respect to a corporation: the corporation, an affiliate, its directors and officers, a holder of more than the prescribed
-- percentage of voting rights, its employees and those doing business with it, people who received material confidential information while one of these,
-- people who received it from an insider knowing so, and prescribed persons. One limb is enough.
@ref CBCA s 131(1)
@export Am I an insider of the corporation for section 131 (s 131(1))?
GIVEN `I am the corporation itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the corporation itself?
      `I am an affiliate of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an affiliate of the corporation?
      `I am a director or an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of the corporation?
      `I am a director or an officer of an affiliate of the corporation, of a person holding a large block of its shares, or of a person doing business with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of an affiliate of the corporation, of a person who holds more than the prescribed percentage of its voting shares, or of a person who engages in business or professional activity with it?
      `the fraction of the voting rights in the corporation that I own, control or direct` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the voting rights attached to all the outstanding shares of the corporation do you own, control or direct, alone or together (as a number between 0 and 1, not counting shares held as underwriter during a public distribution)?
      `I am employed or retained by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed or retained by the corporation?
      `I am employed or retained by a person doing business with the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed or retained by a person who engages in business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation?
      `I engage or propose to engage in business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you engage, or propose to engage, in any business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation?
      `I received material confidential information about the corporation while I was one of those persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive material confidential information about the corporation while you were the corporation, an affiliate, a director or officer, a large shareholder, an employee, or someone doing business with it?
      `I received material confidential information about the corporation from an insider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive material confidential information about the corporation from a person who is an insider under section 131 (including a person under subsection 131(3) or (3.1))?
      `I knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person who gave me the information about the corporation was an insider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know, or ought you reasonably to have known, that the person who gave you the information was such an insider?
      `I am a person the regulations prescribe as an insider of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person that the regulations prescribe as an insider of the corporation?
      `the percentage that the regulations prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the regulations prescribe for this purpose (as a number between 0 and 1)? The Act leaves this figure to the regulations.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an insider of the corporation for section 131` IF
    `insider within s 131(1)` myConnection `the percentage that the regulations prescribe`
    WHERE
        myConnection MEANS `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)` WITH
            `the corporation itself` IS `I am the corporation itself`
            `an affiliate of the corporation` IS `I am an affiliate of the corporation`
            `a director or an officer of the corporation` IS `I am a director or an officer of the corporation`
            `a director or an officer of a person described in paragraph (b), (d) or (f)` IS `I am a director or an officer of an affiliate of the corporation, of a person holding a large block of its shares, or of a person doing business with it`
            `fraction of the voting rights beneficially owned, controlled or directed, not counting shares held as underwriter in the course of a distribution to the public` IS `the fraction of the voting rights in the corporation that I own, control or direct`
            `employed or retained by the corporation` IS `I am employed or retained by the corporation`
            `employed or retained by a person described in paragraph (f)` IS `I am employed or retained by a person doing business with the corporation`
            `engages in or proposes to engage in any business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation` IS `I engage or propose to engage in business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation`
            `received material confidential information concerning the corporation while a person described in any of paragraphs (a) to (f)` IS `I received material confidential information about the corporation while I was one of those persons`
            `received material confidential information from a person described in subsection 131(1), (3) or (3.1)` IS `I received material confidential information about the corporation from an insider`
            `knows or ought reasonably to have known that the person giving the information is such a person` IS `I knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person who gave me the information about the corporation was an insider`
            `a prescribed person` IS `I am a person the regulations prescribe as an insider of the corporation`

-- s 131(2). For section 131, a put, call, option or other right to buy or sell a security of the corporation, and a security of another entity whose price
-- moves materially with the corporation's, are deemed securities of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 131(2)
@export Does section 131 treat what I hold or traded as a security of the corporation (s 131(2))?
GIVEN `it is a security of the corporation apart from this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a security of the corporation in the ordinary sense?
      `it is a put, call, option or other right or obligation to purchase or sell a security of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a put, call, option or other right or obligation to purchase or sell a security of the corporation?
      `it is a security of another entity whose market price varies materially with the market price of the corporation's securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a security of another entity whose market price varies materially with the market price of the corporation's securities?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 131 treat what I hold or traded as a security of the corporation` IF
    `security of the corporation within s 131(2)` `it is a security of the corporation apart from this subsection` `it is a put, call, option or other right or obligation to purchase or sell a security of the corporation` `it is a security of another entity whose market price varies materially with the market price of the corporation's securities`

-- s 131(3). A person who proposes to make a take-over bid for securities of a corporation, or to enter into a business combination with it, is an insider of it
-- with respect to material confidential information obtained from the corporation, and for the purposes of subsection (6).
@ref CBCA s 131(3)
@export Am I deemed an insider because I propose a take-over bid or a business combination (s 131(3))?
GIVEN `I propose to make a take-over bid for securities of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you propose to make a take-over bid (as the regulations define it) for securities of the corporation?
      `I propose to enter into a business combination with the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you propose to enter into a business combination with the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I deemed an insider because I propose a take-over bid or a business combination` IF
    `deemed insider within s 131(3)` `I propose to make a take-over bid for securities of the corporation` `I propose to enter into a business combination with the corporation`

-- s 131(3.1). An insider of a person described in subsection (3), and an affiliate or associate of that person, is an insider of the corporation.
-- Paragraphs (1)(b) to (i) apply, reading "person described in subsection (3)" for "corporation".
@ref CBCA s 131(3.1)
@export Am I an insider because I am connected to a person who proposes a take-over bid or a business combination (s 131(3.1))?
GIVEN `I am the bidder or party to the business combination itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination itself?
      `I am an affiliate of the bidder or party to the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an affiliate of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination?
      `I am a director or an officer of the bidder or party to the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination?
      `I am a director or an officer of an affiliate of the bidder or party to the business combination, of a person holding a large block of its shares, or of a person doing business with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of an affiliate of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination, of a person who holds more than the prescribed percentage of its voting shares, or of a person who engages in business or professional activity with it?
      `the fraction of the voting rights in the bidder or party to the business combination that I own, control or direct` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the voting rights attached to all the outstanding shares of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination do you own, control or direct, alone or together (as a number between 0 and 1, not counting shares held as underwriter during a public distribution)?
      `I am employed or retained by the bidder or party to the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed or retained by the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination?
      `I am employed or retained by a person doing business with the bidder or party to the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed or retained by a person who engages in business or professional activity with or on behalf of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination?
      `I engage or propose to engage in business or professional activity with or on behalf of the bidder or party to the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you engage, or propose to engage, in any business or professional activity with or on behalf of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination?
      `I received material confidential information about the bidder or party to the business combination while I was one of those persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive material confidential information about the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination while you were the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination, an affiliate, a director or officer, a large shareholder, an employee, or someone doing business with it?
      `I received material confidential information about the bidder or party to the business combination from an insider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive material confidential information about the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination from a person who is an insider under section 131 (including a person under subsection 131(3) or (3.1))?
      `I knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person who gave me the information about the bidder or party to the business combination was an insider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know, or ought you reasonably to have known, that the person who gave you the information was such an insider?
      `I am a person the regulations prescribe as an insider of the bidder or party to the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person that the regulations prescribe as an insider of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination?
      `the percentage that the regulations prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the regulations prescribe for this purpose (as a number between 0 and 1)? The Act leaves this figure to the regulations.
      `I am an affiliate or associate of a person who proposes a take-over bid or a business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an affiliate or associate of a person who proposes to make a take-over bid for, or to enter into a business combination with, the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an insider because I am connected to a person who proposes a take-over bid or a business combination` IF
    `insider within s 131(3.1)` myConnection `the percentage that the regulations prescribe` `I am an affiliate or associate of a person who proposes a take-over bid or a business combination`
    WHERE
        myConnection MEANS `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)` WITH
            `the corporation itself` IS `I am the bidder or party to the business combination itself`
            `an affiliate of the corporation` IS `I am an affiliate of the bidder or party to the business combination`
            `a director or an officer of the corporation` IS `I am a director or an officer of the bidder or party to the business combination`
            `a director or an officer of a person described in paragraph (b), (d) or (f)` IS `I am a director or an officer of an affiliate of the bidder or party to the business combination, of a person holding a large block of its shares, or of a person doing business with it`
            `fraction of the voting rights beneficially owned, controlled or directed, not counting shares held as underwriter in the course of a distribution to the public` IS `the fraction of the voting rights in the bidder or party to the business combination that I own, control or direct`
            `employed or retained by the corporation` IS `I am employed or retained by the bidder or party to the business combination`
            `employed or retained by a person described in paragraph (f)` IS `I am employed or retained by a person doing business with the bidder or party to the business combination`
            `engages in or proposes to engage in any business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation` IS `I engage or propose to engage in business or professional activity with or on behalf of the bidder or party to the business combination`
            `received material confidential information concerning the corporation while a person described in any of paragraphs (a) to (f)` IS `I received material confidential information about the bidder or party to the business combination while I was one of those persons`
            `received material confidential information from a person described in subsection 131(1), (3) or (3.1)` IS `I received material confidential information about the bidder or party to the business combination from an insider`
            `knows or ought reasonably to have known that the person giving the information is such a person` IS `I knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person who gave me the information about the bidder or party to the business combination was an insider`
            `a prescribed person` IS `I am a person the regulations prescribe as an insider of the bidder or party to the business combination`

-- s 131(1), (3), (3.1). A person is an insider with respect to the information if they are an insider under (1), or a deemed insider under (3) who obtained the
-- information from the corporation, or an insider under (3.1).
@ref CBCA s 131(1), (3), (3.1)
@export Am I an insider of the corporation with respect to the confidential information (s 131(1), (3) and (3.1))?
GIVEN `I am the corporation itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the corporation itself?
      `I am an affiliate of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an affiliate of the corporation?
      `I am a director or an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of the corporation?
      `I am a director or an officer of an affiliate of the corporation, of a person holding a large block of its shares, or of a person doing business with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of an affiliate of the corporation, of a person who holds more than the prescribed percentage of its voting shares, or of a person who engages in business or professional activity with it?
      `the fraction of the voting rights in the corporation that I own, control or direct` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the voting rights attached to all the outstanding shares of the corporation do you own, control or direct, alone or together (as a number between 0 and 1, not counting shares held as underwriter during a public distribution)?
      `I am employed or retained by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed or retained by the corporation?
      `I am employed or retained by a person doing business with the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed or retained by a person who engages in business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation?
      `I engage or propose to engage in business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you engage, or propose to engage, in any business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation?
      `I received material confidential information about the corporation while I was one of those persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive material confidential information about the corporation while you were the corporation, an affiliate, a director or officer, a large shareholder, an employee, or someone doing business with it?
      `I received material confidential information about the corporation from an insider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive material confidential information about the corporation from a person who is an insider under section 131 (including a person under subsection 131(3) or (3.1))?
      `I knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person who gave me the information about the corporation was an insider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know, or ought you reasonably to have known, that the person who gave you the information was such an insider?
      `I am a person the regulations prescribe as an insider of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person that the regulations prescribe as an insider of the corporation?
      `the percentage that the regulations prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage do the regulations prescribe for this purpose (as a number between 0 and 1)? The Act leaves this figure to the regulations.
      `I propose to make a take-over bid for securities of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you propose to make a take-over bid (as the regulations define it) for securities of the corporation?
      `I propose to enter into a business combination with the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you propose to enter into a business combination with the corporation?
      `I obtained the information from the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you obtain the information from the corporation?
      `I am the bidder or party to the business combination itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination itself?
      `I am an affiliate of the bidder or party to the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an affiliate of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination?
      `I am a director or an officer of the bidder or party to the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination?
      `I am a director or an officer of an affiliate of the bidder or party to the business combination, of a person holding a large block of its shares, or of a person doing business with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of an affiliate of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination, of a person who holds more than the prescribed percentage of its voting shares, or of a person who engages in business or professional activity with it?
      `the fraction of the voting rights in the bidder or party to the business combination that I own, control or direct` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the voting rights attached to all the outstanding shares of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination do you own, control or direct, alone or together (as a number between 0 and 1, not counting shares held as underwriter during a public distribution)?
      `I am employed or retained by the bidder or party to the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed or retained by the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination?
      `I am employed or retained by a person doing business with the bidder or party to the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed or retained by a person who engages in business or professional activity with or on behalf of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination?
      `I engage or propose to engage in business or professional activity with or on behalf of the bidder or party to the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you engage, or propose to engage, in any business or professional activity with or on behalf of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination?
      `I received material confidential information about the bidder or party to the business combination while I was one of those persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive material confidential information about the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination while you were the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination, an affiliate, a director or officer, a large shareholder, an employee, or someone doing business with it?
      `I received material confidential information about the bidder or party to the business combination from an insider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive material confidential information about the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination from a person who is an insider under section 131 (including a person under subsection 131(3) or (3.1))?
      `I knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person who gave me the information about the bidder or party to the business combination was an insider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know, or ought you reasonably to have known, that the person who gave you the information was such an insider?
      `I am a person the regulations prescribe as an insider of the bidder or party to the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person that the regulations prescribe as an insider of the person who proposes the take-over bid or business combination?
      `I am an affiliate or associate of a person who proposes a take-over bid or a business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an affiliate or associate of a person who proposes to make a take-over bid for, or to enter into a business combination with, the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an insider of the corporation with respect to the confidential information` IF
    `insider with respect to the information within s 131(1), (3) and (3.1)`
        (`insider within s 131(1)` myConnection `the percentage that the regulations prescribe`)
        (`deemed insider within s 131(3)` `I propose to make a take-over bid for securities of the corporation` `I propose to enter into a business combination with the corporation`)
