    WHERE
        myConnection MEANS `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)` WITH
            `the corporation itself` IS `I am the corporation itself`
            `an affiliate of the corporation` IS `I am an affiliate of the corporation`
            `a director or an officer of the corporation` IS `I am a director or an officer of the corporation`
            `a director or an officer of a person described in paragraph (b), (d) or (f)` IS `I am a director or an officer of an affiliate of the corporation, of a person holding a large block of its shares, or of a person doing business with it`
            `fraction of the voting rights beneficially owned, controlled or directed, not counting shares held as underwriter in the course of a distribution to the public` IS `the fraction of the voting rights in the corporation that I own, control or direct`
            `employed or retained by the corporation` IS `I am employed or retained by the corporation`
            `employed or retained by a person described in paragraph (f)` IS `I am employed or retained by a person doing business with the corporation`
            `engages in or proposes to engage in any business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation` IS `I engage or propose to engage in business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation`
            `received material confidential information concerning the corporation while a person described in any of paragraphs (a) to (f)` IS `I received material confidential information about the corporation while I was one of those persons`
            `received material confidential information from a person described in subsection 131(1), (3) or (3.1)` IS `I received material confidential information about the corporation from an insider`
            `knows or ought reasonably to have known that the person giving the information is such a person` IS `I knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person who gave me the information about the corporation was an insider`
            `a prescribed person` IS `I am a person the regulations prescribe as an insider of the corporation`
        myConnectionToBidder MEANS `Connection of a person to a corporation under s 131(1)` WITH
            `the corporation itself` IS `I am the bidder or party to the business combination itself`
            `an affiliate of the corporation` IS `I am an affiliate of the bidder or party to the business combination`
            `a director or an officer of the corporation` IS `I am a director or an officer of the bidder or party to the business combination`
            `a director or an officer of a person described in paragraph (b), (d) or (f)` IS `I am a director or an officer of an affiliate of the bidder or party to the business combination, of a person holding a large block of its shares, or of a person doing business with it`
            `fraction of the voting rights beneficially owned, controlled or directed, not counting shares held as underwriter in the course of a distribution to the public` IS `the fraction of the voting rights in the bidder or party to the business combination that I own, control or direct`
            `employed or retained by the corporation` IS `I am employed or retained by the bidder or party to the business combination`
            `employed or retained by a person described in paragraph (f)` IS `I am employed or retained by a person doing business with the bidder or party to the business combination`
            `engages in or proposes to engage in any business or professional activity with or on behalf of the corporation` IS `I engage or propose to engage in business or professional activity with or on behalf of the bidder or party to the business combination`
            `received material confidential information concerning the corporation while a person described in any of paragraphs (a) to (f)` IS `I received material confidential information about the bidder or party to the business combination while I was one of those persons`
            `received material confidential information from a person described in subsection 131(1), (3) or (3.1)` IS `I received material confidential information about the bidder or party to the business combination from an insider`
            `knows or ought reasonably to have known that the person giving the information is such a person` IS `I knew or ought reasonably to have known that the person who gave me the information about the bidder or party to the business combination was an insider`
            `a prescribed person` IS `I am a person the regulations prescribe as an insider of the bidder or party to the business combination`

-- s 131(4). An insider who purchases or sells a security of the corporation with knowledge of confidential information that, if generally known, might reasonably be
-- expected to affect materially the value of its securities is liable to compensate the seller or purchaser for damages, unless the insider establishes (a) a reasonable belief
-- that the information had been generally disclosed, (b) that the seller or purchaser knew or ought to have known it, or (c) that the trade took place in the prescribed circumstances.
@ref CBCA s 131(4)
@export Must I compensate the person I traded with because I traded on confidential information (s 131(4))?
GIVEN `I am an insider of the corporation for the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an insider of the corporation with respect to the confidential information?
      `I purchased or sold a security of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you purchase or sell a security of the corporation?
      `I had knowledge of the confidential information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have knowledge of the confidential information when you traded?
      `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the information were generally known, might it reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any of the corporation's securities?
      `I can establish that I reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that you reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed?
      `I can establish that the seller or purchaser knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that the person you traded with knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information?
      `I can establish that the trade took place in the prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that the trade took place in circumstances that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I compensate the person I traded with because I traded on confidential information` IF
    `compensation is owed to the counterparty of the trade within s 131(4)`
        (`trade described in s 131(4)` `I am an insider of the corporation for the information` `I purchased or sold a security of the corporation` `I had knowledge of the confidential information` `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities`)
        `I can establish that I reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed` `I can establish that the seller or purchaser knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information` `I can establish that the trade took place in the prescribed circumstances`

-- s 131(4). The same relation seen from the seller or purchaser: the insider who traded with knowledge of material confidential information is liable to compensate them
-- for damages, unless the insider establishes one of the three defences.
@ref CBCA s 131(4)
@export Am I owed compensation by an insider who traded with me on confidential information (s 131(4))?
GIVEN `the person I traded with is an insider of the corporation for the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you traded with an insider of the corporation with respect to the confidential information?
      `the insider purchased from me or sold to me a security of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that person purchase a security of the corporation from you, or sell one to you?
      `the insider had knowledge of the confidential information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that person have knowledge of the confidential information when they traded with you?
      `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities (the other side)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the information were generally known, might it reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any of the corporation's securities?
      `the insider can establish that they reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the insider establish that they reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed?
      `the insider can establish that I knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the insider establish that you knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information?
      `the insider can establish that the trade took place in the prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the insider establish that the trade took place in circumstances that the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I owed compensation by an insider who traded with me on confidential information` IF
    `compensation is owed to the counterparty of the trade within s 131(4)`
        (`trade described in s 131(4)` `the person I traded with is an insider of the corporation for the information` `the insider purchased from me or sold to me a security of the corporation` `the insider had knowledge of the confidential information` `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities (the other side)`)
        `the insider can establish that they reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed` `the insider can establish that I knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information` `the insider can establish that the trade took place in the prescribed circumstances`

-- s 131(5). The insider is accountable to the corporation for any benefit or advantage received or receivable as a result of a trade described in subsection (4), unless the insider
-- establishes the reasonable belief of paragraph (4)(a). Only that one defence applies here.
@ref CBCA s 131(5)
@export Am I accountable to the corporation for the benefit I got from my trade (s 131(5))?
