      `I purchased or sold a security of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you purchase or sell a security of the corporation?
      `I had knowledge of the confidential information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have knowledge of the confidential information when you traded?
      `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the information were generally known, might it reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any of the corporation's securities?
      `I can establish that I reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that you reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I accountable to the corporation for the benefit I got from my trade` IF
    `the insider is accountable to the corporation within s 131(5)`
        (`trade described in s 131(4)` `I am an insider of the corporation for the information` `I purchased or sold a security of the corporation` `I had knowledge of the confidential information` `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities`)
        `I can establish that I reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed`

-- s 131(5). The same relation seen from the corporation, which a director or shareholder asks about: is an insider who traded accountable to it?
@ref CBCA s 131(5)
@export Is an insider who traded accountable to my corporation for the benefit they got (s 131(5))?
GIVEN `the person who traded is an insider of the corporation for the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who traded an insider of the corporation with respect to the confidential information?
      `that person purchased or sold a security of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that person purchase or sell a security of the corporation?
      `that person had knowledge of the confidential information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that person have knowledge of the confidential information when they traded?
      `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities (the other side)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the information were generally known, might it reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any of the corporation's securities?
      `the insider can establish that they reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the insider establish that they reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an insider who traded accountable to my corporation for the benefit they got` IF
    `the insider is accountable to the corporation within s 131(5)`
        (`trade described in s 131(4)` `the person who traded is an insider of the corporation for the information` `that person purchased or sold a security of the corporation` `that person had knowledge of the confidential information` `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities (the other side)`)
        `the insider can establish that they reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed`

-- s 131(6). An insider who discloses confidential information that has not been generally disclosed and that might materially affect the value of the corporation's securities is
-- liable to compensate any person who subsequently sells securities to, or purchases them from, a person that received the information, unless the insider establishes one of the four
-- defences (the third does not help a person described in (3) or (3.1); the fourth is only for such a person).
@ref CBCA s 131(6)
@export Must I compensate someone because I disclosed confidential information (s 131(6))?
GIVEN `I am an insider of the corporation for the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an insider of the corporation with respect to the confidential information?
      `I disclosed confidential information about the corporation to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose confidential information about the corporation to another person?
      `the information has not been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the information not been generally disclosed?
      `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the information were generally known, might it reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any of the corporation's securities?
      `someone subsequently sold securities of the corporation to, or purchased them from, a person who received the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did someone subsequently sell securities of the corporation to, or purchase them from, a person who received the information?
      `I am a person described in subsection 131(3) or (3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person who proposes a take-over bid or business combination, or who is connected to such a person (s 131(3) or (3.1))?
      `I can establish that I reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that you reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed?
      `I can establish that the claimant knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that the person claiming damages knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information?
      `I can establish that the disclosure was necessary in the course of my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that the disclosure was necessary in the course of your business?
      `I can establish that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I compensate someone because I disclosed confidential information` IF
    `compensation is owed to the claimant of the disclosure within s 131(6)`
        (`disclosure described in s 131(6)` `I am an insider of the corporation for the information` `I disclosed confidential information about the corporation to another person` `the information has not been generally disclosed` `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities`)
        `someone subsequently sold securities of the corporation to, or purchased them from, a person who received the information` `I am a person described in subsection 131(3) or (3.1)` `I can establish that I reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed` `I can establish that the claimant knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information` `I can establish that the disclosure was necessary in the course of my business` `I can establish that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination`

