      `the insider can establish that I knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information about the tip` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the insider establish that you knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information?
      `the insider can establish that the disclosure was necessary in the course of their business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the insider establish that the disclosure was necessary in the course of their business?
      `the insider can establish that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the insider establish that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I owed compensation because an insider disclosed confidential information that led to my trade` IF
    `compensation is owed to the claimant of the disclosure within s 131(6)`
        (`disclosure described in s 131(6)` `an insider of the corporation for the information disclosed it` `that insider disclosed confidential information about the corporation to another person` `the information had not been generally disclosed` `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities (the other side)`)
        `I subsequently sold securities of the corporation to, or purchased them from, a person who received the information` `the insider is a person described in subsection 131(3) or (3.1)` `the insider can establish that they reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed` `the insider can establish that I knew, or ought reasonably to have known, the information about the tip` `the insider can establish that the disclosure was necessary in the course of their business` `the insider can establish that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination`

-- s 131(7). The insider is accountable to the corporation for any benefit or advantage received or receivable as a result of a disclosure described in subsection (6),
