@ref CBCA s 131(7)
@export Am I accountable to the corporation for the benefit I got from disclosing confidential information (s 131(7))?
GIVEN `I am an insider of the corporation for the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an insider of the corporation with respect to the confidential information?
      `I disclosed confidential information about the corporation to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you disclose confidential information about the corporation to another person?
      `the information has not been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the information not been generally disclosed?
      `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the information were generally known, might it reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any of the corporation's securities?
      `I am a person described in subsection 131(3) or (3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person who proposes a take-over bid or business combination, or who is connected to such a person (s 131(3) or (3.1))?
      `I can establish that I reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that you reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed?
      `I can establish that the disclosure was necessary in the course of my business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that the disclosure was necessary in the course of your business?
      `I can establish that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you establish that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I accountable to the corporation for the benefit I got from disclosing confidential information` IF
    `the insider is accountable to the corporation for the disclosure within s 131(7)`
        (`disclosure described in s 131(6)` `I am an insider of the corporation for the information` `I disclosed confidential information about the corporation to another person` `the information has not been generally disclosed` `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities`)
        `I am a person described in subsection 131(3) or (3.1)` `I can establish that I reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed` `I can establish that the disclosure was necessary in the course of my business` `I can establish that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination`

-- s 131(7). The same relation seen from the corporation, which a director or shareholder asks about.
@ref CBCA s 131(7)
@export Is an insider who disclosed confidential information accountable to my corporation (s 131(7))?
GIVEN `an insider of the corporation for the information disclosed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who disclosed the information an insider of the corporation with respect to it?
      `that insider disclosed confidential information about the corporation to another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that insider disclose confidential information about the corporation to another person?
      `the information had not been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the information not been generally disclosed?
      `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities (the other side)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the information were generally known, might it reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of any of the corporation's securities?
      `the insider is a person described in subsection 131(3) or (3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the insider a person who proposes a take-over bid or business combination, or who is connected to such a person?
      `the insider can establish that they reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the insider establish that they reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed?
      `the insider can establish that the disclosure was necessary in the course of their business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the insider establish that the disclosure was necessary in the course of their business?
      `the insider can establish that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the insider establish that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is an insider who disclosed confidential information accountable to my corporation` IF
    `the insider is accountable to the corporation for the disclosure within s 131(7)`
        (`disclosure described in s 131(6)` `an insider of the corporation for the information disclosed it` `that insider disclosed confidential information about the corporation to another person` `the information had not been generally disclosed` `the information, if generally known, might reasonably be expected to affect materially the value of the corporation's securities (the other side)`)
        `the insider is a person described in subsection 131(3) or (3.1)` `the insider can establish that they reasonably believed the information had been generally disclosed` `the insider can establish that the disclosure was necessary in the course of their business` `the insider can establish that the disclosure was necessary to effect the take-over bid or the business combination`

-- s 131(8). In assessing damages for a security of a distributing corporation, the court must consider the comparison with the average market price after general disclosure.
@ref CBCA s 131(8)
@export Must the court compare my price with the market price after disclosure (s 131(8))?
GIVEN `the security is a security of a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the security one of a distributing corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the court compare my price with the market price after disclosure` IF
    `the court must consider the comparison with the post-disclosure price within s 131(8)` `the security is a security of a distributing corporation`

-- s 131(8)(a). If the plaintiff is a purchaser, the court must consider the price paid less the average market price over the twenty trading days after general disclosure.
@ref CBCA s 131(8)(a)
@export As a purchaser, what amount must the court consider (s 131(8)(a))?
GIVEN `the price I paid for the security, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What price did you pay for the security, in dollars?
      `the average market price of the security over the twenty trading days after general disclosure, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the average market price of the security over the twenty trading days immediately following general disclosure of the information, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As a purchaser, what amount must the court consider` IS
    `amount the court must consider where the plaintiff is a purchaser within s 131(8)(a)` `the price I paid for the security, in dollars` `the average market price of the security over the twenty trading days after general disclosure, in dollars`

-- s 131(8)(b). If the plaintiff is a seller, the court must consider the average market price over the twenty trading days after general disclosure less the price received.
@ref CBCA s 131(8)(b)
@export As a seller, what amount must the court consider (s 131(8)(b))?
GIVEN `the average market price of the security over the twenty trading days after general disclosure, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the average market price of the security over the twenty trading days immediately following general disclosure of the information, in dollars?
      `the price I received for the security, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What price did you receive for the security, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `As a seller, what amount must the court consider` IS
    `amount the court must consider where the plaintiff is a seller within s 131(8)(b)` `the average market price of the security over the twenty trading days after general disclosure, in dollars` `the price I received for the security, in dollars`

-- s 131(9). If more than one insider is liable for the same transaction or series of transactions, their liability is joint and several, or solidary.
@ref CBCA s 131(9)
@export If several insiders are liable to me, is each liable for the whole (s 131(9))?
GIVEN `the number of insiders liable for the same transaction or series of transactions` IS A NUMBER @desc How many insiders are liable under subsection 131(4) or (6) for the same transaction or series of transactions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If several insiders are liable to me, is each liable for the whole` IF
    `liability is joint and several within s 131(9)` `the number of insiders liable for the same transaction or series of transactions`

-- s 131(10). An action to enforce a right under subsections (4) to (7) may be commenced only within two years after discovery of the facts that gave rise to the cause of action.
@ref CBCA s 131(10)
@export By when must I start my action under section 131 (s 131(10))?
GIVEN `the date I discovered the facts that gave rise to my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you discover the facts that gave rise to your claim?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I start my action under section 131` IS
    `the last day to commence an action within s 131(10)` `the date I discovered the facts that gave rise to my claim`

-- s 131(10). The same time limit, asked of a particular day.
@ref CBCA s 131(10)
@export May I still start my action under section 131 (s 131(10))?
GIVEN `the date I discovered the facts that gave rise to my claim` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you discover the facts that gave rise to your claim?
      `the date I start my action` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you start, or propose to start, your action?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I still start my action under section 131` IF
    `an action may be commenced within s 131(10)` `the date I discovered the facts that gave rise to my claim` `the date I start my action`


§§ `Where and how a shareholders' meeting is held (s 132)`

-- Only if a meeting of shareholders is being planned or has been called.

-- s 132(1). Meetings of shareholders shall be held at the place within Canada provided in the by-laws or, in the absence of such a provision, at the place within Canada that the directors determine.
@ref CBCA s 132(1)
@export Is the place of the meeting lawful (s 132(1))?
GIVEN `the place is within Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place of the meeting within Canada?
      `the by-laws provide a place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws provide a place for meetings of shareholders?
      `the place is the one the by-laws provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place of the meeting the one the by-laws provide?
      `the place is the one the directors determine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place of the meeting the one the directors have determined?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the place of the meeting lawful` IF
    `the place of the meeting complies with s 132(1)` `the place is within Canada` `the by-laws provide a place` `the place is the one the by-laws provide` `the place is the one the directors determine`

-- s 132(2). A meeting may be held at a place outside Canada if the place is specified in the articles or all the shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting agree.
@ref CBCA s 132(2)
@export May the meeting be held outside Canada (s 132(2))?
GIVEN `the place is outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place of the meeting outside Canada?
      `the place is specified in the articles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles specify that place?
      `all the shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting agree that the meeting is to be held at that place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting agree that it is to be held at that place?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the meeting be held outside Canada` IF
    `a meeting may be held outside Canada within s 132(2)` `the place is outside Canada` `the place is specified in the articles` `all the shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting agree that the meeting is to be held at that place`

-- s 132(3). A shareholder who attends a meeting held outside Canada is deemed to have agreed to it, unless they attend for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully held.
@ref CBCA s 132(3)
@export Am I taken to have agreed to a meeting held outside Canada because I attended (s 132(3))?
GIVEN `I attended a meeting of shareholders held outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you attend a meeting of shareholders held outside Canada?
      `I attended for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully held` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you attend for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully held?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I taken to have agreed to a meeting held outside Canada because I attended` IF
    `the shareholder is deemed to have agreed to the meeting being held outside Canada within s 132(3)` `I attended a meeting of shareholders held outside Canada` `I attended for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully held`

-- s 132(4). Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, any person entitled to attend a meeting may participate by telephonic, electronic or other communication facility that permits all participants to communicate adequately, if the corporation makes one available, in accordance with the regulations, if any.
@ref CBCA s 132(4)
@export May I take part in the meeting by telephone or other electronic means (s 132(4))?
GIVEN `I am entitled to attend the meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to attend the meeting of shareholders?
      `the by-laws otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws provide that people may not take part this way?
      `the corporation makes a communication facility available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation make a telephone, electronic or other communication facility available?
      `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the facility let all participants communicate adequately with each other during the meeting?
      `the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your participation in accordance with the regulations, if any?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I take part in the meeting by telephone or other electronic means` IF
    `a person may participate by electronic means within s 132(4)` `I am entitled to attend the meeting of shareholders` `the by-laws otherwise provide` `the corporation makes a communication facility available` `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting` `the participation is in accordance with the regulations, if any`

-- s 132(4). A person participating by such means is deemed for the purposes of the Act to be present at the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 132(4)
@export Am I treated as present at the meeting if I take part by electronic means (s 132(4))?
GIVEN `I participate in the meeting by means of a communication facility under subsection 132(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you taking part in the meeting by a telephonic, electronic or other communication facility, as subsection 132(4) allows?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as present at the meeting if I take part by electronic means` IF
    `a person participating by electronic means is present at the meeting within s 132(4)` `I participate in the meeting by means of a communication facility under subsection 132(4)`

-- s 132(5). If the directors or the shareholders call a meeting, they may determine that it is held entirely by electronic means, if the by-laws so provide, with a facility that lets all participants communicate adequately, in accordance with the regulations, if any.
@ref CBCA s 132(5)
@export May we hold the meeting entirely by electronic means (s 132(5))?
GIVEN `the directors or the shareholders call the meeting pursuant to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directors or the shareholders calling the meeting under the Act?
      `the by-laws so provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws provide for meetings held entirely by electronic means?
      `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the facility let all participants communicate adequately with each other during the meeting?
      `the meeting is held in accordance with the regulations, if any` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting to be held in accordance with the regulations, if any?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we hold the meeting entirely by electronic means` IF
    `the callers may determine that the meeting is held entirely by electronic means within s 132(5)` `the directors or the shareholders call the meeting pursuant to the Act` `the by-laws so provide` `the facility permits all participants to communicate adequately with each other during the meeting` `the meeting is held in accordance with the regulations, if any`


§§ `Calling the annual meeting and special meetings (s 133)`

-- Directors ask when the meeting must be called; shareholders ask whether the directors have kept to the time.

-- s 133(1)(a). The directors shall call an annual meeting not later than eighteen months after the corporation comes into existence. The day it comes into existence is day 0.
@ref CBCA s 133(1)(a)
@export By when must the directors call the first annual meeting (s 133(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the date the corporation comes into existence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation come into existence?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the directors call the first annual meeting` IS
    `the last day to call the first annual meeting within s 133(1)(a)` `the date the corporation comes into existence`

-- s 133(1)(a). The same time limit, asked of the day the directors actually call the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 133(1)(a)
@export Did the directors call the first annual meeting in time (s 133(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the date the corporation comes into existence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation come into existence?
      `the date the directors call the annual meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the directors call the annual meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the directors call the first annual meeting in time` IF
    `the first annual meeting is called in time within s 133(1)(a)` `the date the corporation comes into existence` `the date the directors call the annual meeting`

-- s 133(1)(b). Subsequently, the directors shall call an annual meeting not later than fifteen months after holding the last preceding annual meeting but no later than six months after the end of the corporation's preceding financial year.
-- The earlier of the two days is the last day.
@ref CBCA s 133(1)(b)
@export By when must the directors call the next annual meeting (s 133(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the date the last preceding annual meeting was held` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the last annual meeting held?
      `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation's preceding financial year end?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the directors call the next annual meeting` IS
    `the last day to call a subsequent annual meeting within s 133(1)(b)` `the date the last preceding annual meeting was held` `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended`

-- s 133(1)(b). The same limit, asked of the day the directors actually call the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 133(1)(b)
@export Did the directors call the next annual meeting in time (s 133(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the date the last preceding annual meeting was held` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the last annual meeting held?
      `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation's preceding financial year end?
      `the date the directors call the annual meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the directors call the annual meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the directors call the next annual meeting in time` IF
    `a subsequent annual meeting is called in time within s 133(1)(b)` `the date the last preceding annual meeting was held` `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended` `the date the directors call the annual meeting`

-- s 133(2). The directors may at any time call a special meeting of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 133(2)
@export May the directors call a special meeting whenever they like (s 133(2))?
GIVEN `the persons calling the meeting are the directors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the people calling the meeting the directors of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors call a special meeting whenever they like` IF
    `the directors may call a special meeting at any time within s 133(2)` `the persons calling the meeting are the directors of the corporation`

-- s 133(3). Despite subsection (1), the corporation may apply to the court for an order extending the time for calling an annual meeting.
@ref CBCA s 133(3)
@export May the corporation ask the court for more time to call the annual meeting (s 133(3))?
GIVEN `the applicant is the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant the corporation?
      `the application is for an order extending the time for calling an annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for an order extending the time for calling an annual meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation ask the court for more time to call the annual meeting` IF
    `the corporation may apply to the court to extend the time for calling an annual meeting within s 133(3)` `the applicant is the corporation` `the application is for an order extending the time for calling an annual meeting`


§§ `Record dates and notice of a meeting (ss 134 to 136)`

-- Only when a meeting, a dividend or a liquidation distribution is being planned.

-- s 134(1). The directors may, within the prescribed period, fix in advance a date as the record date for determining shareholders entitled to a dividend, a liquidation distribution, notice of a meeting, a vote at a meeting, or for any other purpose.
@ref CBCA s 134(1)
@export May the directors fix a record date (s 134(1))?
GIVEN `the persons fixing the date are the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the people fixing the date the directors?
      `the date is fixed in advance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the date fixed in advance?
      `the date is fixed within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the date fixed within the period the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors fix a record date` IF
    `the directors may fix a record date within s 134(1)` `the persons fixing the date are the directors` `the date is fixed in advance` `the date is fixed within the prescribed period`

-- s 134(2). If no record date is fixed: for notice of a meeting it is the close of business on the day before the notice is given, or the day of the meeting if no notice is given;
-- for any purpose other than notice or voting it is the close of business on the day the directors pass the resolution. The text gives no default for a vote.
@ref CBCA s 134(2)
@export What is the record date if the directors fix none (s 134(2))?
GIVEN `the purpose of the record date` IS A `Purpose of a record date under s 134(1)` @desc What is the record date for (receiving a dividend, taking part in a liquidation distribution, receiving notice of a meeting, voting at a meeting, or any other purpose)?
      `notice of the meeting is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is notice of the meeting given?
      `the date notice of the meeting is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date is notice of the meeting given?
      `the date the meeting is held` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting held?
      `the date the directors pass the resolution relating to the purpose` IS A DATE @desc On what date do the directors pass the resolution relating to the purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the record date if the directors fix none` IS
    `the record date when none is fixed within s 134(2)` `the purpose of the record date` (IF `notice of the meeting is given` THEN JUST `the date notice of the meeting is given` ELSE NOTHING) `the date the meeting is held` `the date the directors pass the resolution relating to the purpose`

-- s 134(3). If a record date is fixed, notice of it must be given within the prescribed period unless every holder of a share of the class or series affected whose name is in the securities register at the close of business on the day the directors fix the date has waived notice in writing.
@ref CBCA s 134(3)
@export Must notice of the record date be given (s 134(3))?
GIVEN `a record date is fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a record date been fixed?
      `every holder of a share of the class or series affected whose name is set out in the securities register at the close of business on the day the directors fix the record date has waived notice in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has every holder of a share of the class or series affected, whose name is in the securities register at the close of business on the day the directors fix the date, waived notice in writing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must notice of the record date be given` IF
    `notice of the record date must be given within s 134(3)` `a record date is fixed` `every holder of a share of the class or series affected whose name is set out in the securities register at the close of business on the day the directors fix the record date has waived notice in writing`

-- s 134(3). The notice is given by advertisement in a newspaper published or distributed where the corporation has its registered office and where it has a transfer agent or transfers are recorded, and by written notice to each stock exchange in Canada where its shares are listed.
@ref CBCA s 134(3)
@export Has notice of the record date been given as the Act requires (s 134(3))?
GIVEN `the notice is given within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice given within the period the regulations prescribe?
      `there is an advertisement in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office and in each place in Canada where it has a transfer agent or where a transfer of its shares may be recorded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there an advertisement in a newspaper published or distributed where the corporation has its registered office and in each place in Canada where it has a transfer agent or where a transfer of its shares may be recorded?
      `there is written notice to each stock exchange in Canada on which the shares of the corporation are listed for trading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there written notice to each stock exchange in Canada on which the corporation's shares are listed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has notice of the record date been given as the Act requires` IF
    `notice of the record date is given as s 134(3) requires within s 134(3)` `the notice is given within the prescribed period` `there is an advertisement in a newspaper published or distributed in the place where the corporation has its registered office and in each place in Canada where it has a transfer agent or where a transfer of its shares may be recorded` `there is written notice to each stock exchange in Canada on which the shares of the corporation are listed for trading`

-- s 135(1). Notice of the time and place of a meeting shall be sent within the prescribed period to each shareholder entitled to vote at the meeting, each director and the auditor.
@ref CBCA s 135(1)
@export Am I owed notice of the meeting (s 135(1))?
GIVEN `I am a shareholder entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder entitled to vote at the meeting?
      `I am a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the corporation?
      `I am the auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the auditor of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I owed notice of the meeting` IF
    `notice of the meeting is owed to a person within s 135(1)` `I am a shareholder entitled to vote at the meeting` `I am a director` `I am the auditor of the corporation`

-- s 135(1), (1.1). The notice shall be sent within the prescribed period; a corporation that is not a distributing corporation may send it within a shorter period if the articles or by-laws so specify.
@ref CBCA s 135(1), (1.1)
@export Was notice of the meeting sent in time (s 135(1) and (1.1))?
GIVEN `the notice was sent within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice sent within the period the regulations prescribe?
      `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `the articles or by-laws specify a shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles or by-laws specify a shorter period?
      `the notice was sent within the shorter period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice sent within that shorter period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was notice of the meeting sent in time` IF
    `the notice of the meeting was sent in time within s 135(1) and (1.1)` `the notice was sent within the prescribed period` `the corporation is a distributing corporation` `the articles or by-laws specify a shorter period` `the notice was sent within the shorter period`

-- s 135(2). A notice of a meeting is not required to be sent to shareholders who were not registered on the records of the corporation or its transfer agent on the record date.
@ref CBCA s 135(2)
@export Can the corporation leave me off the notice because I was not registered on the record date (s 135(2))?
GIVEN `I was registered on the records of the corporation or its transfer agent on the record date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you registered on the records of the corporation or its transfer agent on the record date?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the corporation leave me off the notice because I was not registered on the record date` IF
    `notice need not be sent to the shareholder within s 135(2)` `I was registered on the records of the corporation or its transfer agent on the record date`

-- s 135(2). Failure to receive a notice does not deprive a shareholder of the right to vote at the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 135(2)
@export Do I keep my right to vote even though I did not receive notice (s 135(2))?
GIVEN `I am entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to vote at the meeting?
      `I received the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you receive the notice?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I keep my right to vote even though I did not receive notice` IF
    `the shareholder keeps the right to vote without having received notice within s 135(2)` `I am entitled to vote at the meeting` `I received the notice`

-- s 135(3). If a meeting is adjourned for less than thirty days it is not necessary, unless the by-laws otherwise provide, to give notice of the adjourned meeting, other than by announcement at the earliest meeting that is adjourned.
@ref CBCA s 135(3)
@export Can the adjourned meeting be announced at the meeting without a fresh notice (s 135(3))?
GIVEN `the days the meeting is adjourned, in aggregate` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days in all is the meeting adjourned?
      `the by-laws provide that notice must be given of an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws provide that notice must be given of an adjourned meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the adjourned meeting be announced at the meeting without a fresh notice` IF
    `notice of the adjourned meeting other than by announcement is unnecessary within s 135(3)` `the days the meeting is adjourned, in aggregate` `the by-laws provide that notice must be given of an adjourned meeting`

-- s 135(4). If a meeting is adjourned by one or more adjournments for an aggregate of thirty days or more, notice of the adjourned meeting shall be given as for an original meeting.
@ref CBCA s 135(4)
@export Must notice of the adjourned meeting be given as for an original meeting (s 135(4))?
GIVEN `the days the meeting is adjourned, in aggregate` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days in all is the meeting adjourned?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must notice of the adjourned meeting be given as for an original meeting` IF
    `notice of the adjourned meeting is required as for an original meeting within s 135(4)` `the days the meeting is adjourned, in aggregate`

-- s 135(4). Unless the meeting is adjourned for an aggregate of more than ninety days, subsection 149(1) (sending a form of proxy) does not apply to the adjourned meeting.
@ref CBCA s 135(4)
@export Does management have to send a new form of proxy for the adjourned meeting (s 135(4))?
GIVEN `the days the meeting is adjourned, in aggregate` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days in all is the meeting adjourned?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does management have to send a new form of proxy for the adjourned meeting` IF
    `subsection 149(1) applies to the adjourned meeting within s 135(4)` `the days the meeting is adjourned, in aggregate`

-- s 135(5). All business at a special meeting, and all business at an annual meeting except consideration of the financial statements, the auditor's report, election of directors and re-appointment of the incumbent auditor, is deemed to be special business.
@ref CBCA s 135(5)
@export Is this business special business (s 135(5))?
GIVEN `the meeting is a special meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting a special meeting of shareholders?
      `the business is the consideration of the financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business the consideration of the financial statements?
      `the business is the consideration of the auditor's report` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business the consideration of the auditor's report?
      `the business is the election of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business the election of directors?
      `the business is the re-appointment of the incumbent auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the business the re-appointment of the incumbent auditor?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this business special business` IF
    `the business is deemed to be special business within s 135(5)` `the meeting is a special meeting of shareholders` `the business is the consideration of the financial statements` `the business is the consideration of the auditor's report` `the business is the election of directors` `the business is the re-appointment of the incumbent auditor`

-- s 135(6). Notice of a meeting at which special business is to be transacted shall state the nature of that business in sufficient detail to permit the shareholder to form a reasoned judgment, and the text of any special resolution to be submitted.
@ref CBCA s 135(6)
@export Does the notice of meeting say what the Act requires about the business (s 135(6))?
GIVEN `special business is to be transacted at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is special business to be transacted at the meeting?
      `the notice states the nature of that business in sufficient detail to permit the shareholder to form a reasoned judgment on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the nature of that business in enough detail for a shareholder to form a reasoned judgment on it?
      `a special resolution is to be submitted to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a special resolution to be submitted to the meeting?
      `the notice states the text of the special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the text of the special resolution?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the notice of meeting say what the Act requires about the business` IF
    `the notice of the meeting has the content s 135(6) requires within s 135(6)` `special business is to be transacted at the meeting` `the notice states the nature of that business in sufficient detail to permit the shareholder to form a reasoned judgment on it` `a special resolution is to be submitted to the meeting` `the notice states the text of the special resolution`

-- s 136. A shareholder or any other person entitled to attend a meeting of shareholders may in any manner waive notice of the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 136
@export May I waive notice of the meeting (s 136)?
GIVEN `I am a shareholder or other person entitled to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder or other person entitled to attend the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I waive notice of the meeting` IF
    `a person may waive notice of the meeting within s 136` `I am a shareholder or other person entitled to attend the meeting`

-- s 136. Attendance at a meeting is a waiver of notice, except where the person attends for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully called.
@ref CBCA s 136
@export Does my attendance at the meeting waive notice (s 136)?
GIVEN `I am a shareholder or other person entitled to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder or other person entitled to attend the meeting?
      `I attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you attend the meeting?
      `I attend for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully called` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you attend for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully called?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my attendance at the meeting waive notice` IF
    `attendance is a waiver of notice within s 136` `I am a shareholder or other person entitled to attend the meeting` `I attend the meeting` `I attend for the express purpose of objecting to the transaction of any business on the grounds that the meeting is not lawfully called`


§§ `Raising a matter at the annual meeting: shareholder proposals (s 137)`

-- Only if you hold, or beneficially own, shares that carry a vote at an annual meeting and want to put a matter to it, or you run a corporation that has received a proposal.

-- s 137(1)(a). Subject to (1.1) and (1.2), a registered holder or beneficial owner of shares that are entitled to be voted at an annual meeting may submit to the corporation notice of any matter that the person proposes to raise at the meeting (a proposal).
@ref CBCA s 137(1)(a)
@export May I submit a proposal to the shareholders (s 137(1)(a))?
GIVEN `I am a registered holder or beneficial owner of shares entitled to be voted at an annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered holder or beneficial owner of shares that are entitled to be voted at an annual meeting of shareholders?
      `the number of outstanding shares I have held or owned for at least the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many outstanding shares of the corporation have you held or owned, as registered holder or beneficial owner, for at least the period the regulations prescribe?
      `the number of outstanding shares my supporters and I have held or owned for at least the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many outstanding shares of the corporation have you and the persons supporting your proposal, taken together, held or owned for at least the period the regulations prescribe (count yourself or not)?
      `I have the support of those persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do those persons support your proposal?
      `the prescribed number of outstanding shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How many outstanding shares do the regulations prescribe as the minimum for submitting a proposal?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I submit a proposal to the shareholders` IF
    `a person may submit a proposal within s 137(1)(a)`
        `I am a registered holder or beneficial owner of shares entitled to be voted at an annual meeting`
        (`the person is eligible to submit a proposal within s 137(1.1)`
            `the number of outstanding shares I have held or owned for at least the prescribed period`
            `the number of outstanding shares my supporters and I have held or owned for at least the prescribed period`
            `I have the support of those persons`
            `the prescribed number of outstanding shares`)

-- s 137(1)(b). The same person may discuss at the meeting any matter in respect of which they would have been entitled to submit a proposal.
@ref CBCA s 137(1)(b)
@export May I discuss a matter at the annual meeting (s 137(1)(b))?
GIVEN `I am a registered holder or beneficial owner of shares entitled to be voted at an annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a registered holder or beneficial owner of shares that are entitled to be voted at an annual meeting of shareholders?
      `the matter is one in respect of which I would have been entitled to submit a proposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter one on which you would have been entitled to submit a proposal?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I discuss a matter at the annual meeting` IF
    `a person may discuss a matter at the meeting within s 137(1)(b)` `I am a registered holder or beneficial owner of shares entitled to be voted at an annual meeting` `the matter is one in respect of which I would have been entitled to submit a proposal`

-- s 137(1.1). To be eligible, a person must be, for at least the prescribed period, the registered holder or beneficial owner of at least the prescribed number of outstanding shares, or have the support of persons who together hold at least that number for that period.
@ref CBCA s 137(1.1)
@export Am I eligible to submit a proposal (s 137(1.1))?
GIVEN `the number of outstanding shares I have held or owned for at least the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many outstanding shares of the corporation have you held or owned, as registered holder or beneficial owner, for at least the period the regulations prescribe?
      `the number of outstanding shares my supporters and I have held or owned for at least the prescribed period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many outstanding shares of the corporation have you and the persons supporting your proposal, taken together, held or owned for at least the period the regulations prescribe (count yourself or not)?
      `I have the support of those persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do those persons support your proposal?
      `the prescribed number of outstanding shares` IS A NUMBER @desc How many outstanding shares do the regulations prescribe as the minimum for submitting a proposal?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible to submit a proposal` IF
    `the person is eligible to submit a proposal within s 137(1.1)` `the number of outstanding shares I have held or owned for at least the prescribed period` `the number of outstanding shares my supporters and I have held or owned for at least the prescribed period` `I have the support of those persons` `the prescribed number of outstanding shares`

-- s 137(1.2). A proposal must be accompanied by the name and address of the person and of the person's supporters, if applicable, and by the number of shares held or owned by the person and the supporters, if applicable, and the date the shares were acquired.
@ref CBCA s 137(1.2)
@export Does my proposal carry the information the Act requires (s 137(1.2))?
GIVEN `I rely on supporters under s 137(1.1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you rely on supporters to be eligible?
      `the proposal is accompanied by my name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your proposal accompanied by your name and address?
      `the proposal is accompanied by the name and address of my supporters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it accompanied by the name and address of your supporters?
      `the proposal is accompanied by the number of shares I hold and the date I acquired them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it accompanied by the number of shares you hold or own and the date you acquired them?
      `the proposal is accompanied by the number of shares my supporters hold and the date they acquired them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it accompanied by the number of shares your supporters hold or own and the date they acquired them?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my proposal carry the information the Act requires` IF
    `the proposal is accompanied by the information s 137(1.2) requires within s 137(1.2)` `I rely on supporters under s 137(1.1)(b)` `the proposal is accompanied by my name and address` `the proposal is accompanied by the name and address of my supporters` `the proposal is accompanied by the number of shares I hold and the date I acquired them` `the proposal is accompanied by the number of shares my supporters hold and the date they acquired them`

-- s 137(1.3). The information provided under (1.2) is not part of the proposal or the supporting statement and does not count toward the prescribed maximum word limit.
@ref CBCA s 137(1.3)
@export How many words of mine count toward the word limit (s 137(1.3))?
GIVEN `the number of words in my proposal` IS A NUMBER @desc How many words are in your proposal?
      `the number of words in my supporting statement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many words are in your supporting statement?
      `the number of words in the information I provided under s 137(1.2)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many words are in the information you gave about yourself and your supporters?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many words of mine count toward the word limit` IS
    `the words that count toward the prescribed maximum within s 137(1.3)` `the number of words in my proposal` `the number of words in my supporting statement` `the number of words in the information I provided under s 137(1.2)`

-- s 137(1.4). If requested by the corporation within the prescribed period, a person who submits a proposal must provide proof, within the prescribed period, that the person meets the requirements of (1.1).
@ref CBCA s 137(1.4)
@export Must I prove that I am eligible to submit a proposal (s 137(1.4))?
GIVEN `the corporation requests proof within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation ask you for proof within the period the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I prove that I am eligible to submit a proposal` IF
    `the person must provide proof of eligibility within s 137(1.4)` `the corporation requests proof within the prescribed period`

-- s 137(1.4). The duty is met by proof, given within the prescribed period, that shows the requirements of (1.1) are met.
@ref CBCA s 137(1.4)
@export Have I met my duty to prove my eligibility (s 137(1.4))?
GIVEN `the corporation requests proof within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation ask you for proof within the period the regulations prescribe?
      `I provide proof within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide proof within the period the regulations prescribe?
      `the proof shows that I meet the requirements of s 137(1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the proof show that you meet the requirements of subsection 137(1.1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met my duty to prove my eligibility` IF
    `the duty to provide proof of eligibility is met within s 137(1.4)` `the corporation requests proof within the prescribed period` `I provide proof within the prescribed period` `the proof shows that I meet the requirements of s 137(1.1)`

-- s 137(5). The corporation is not required to comply with (2) and (3) if the proposal is late, is a personal grievance, does not relate significantly to the business, repeats a proposal the person failed to present or that failed to get the prescribed support, or abuses the section to secure publicity.
@ref CBCA s 137(5)
@export Is the corporation excused from circulating my proposal (s 137(5))?
GIVEN `the proposal is not submitted to the corporation within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your proposal not submitted to the corporation within the period the regulations prescribe?
      `it clearly appears that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it clearly appear that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance against the corporation or its directors, officers or security holders?
      `it clearly appears that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it clearly appear that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation?
      `I failed to present a proposal included in a circular at my request within the prescribed period before this one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, within the prescribed period before the corporation received this proposal, fail to present in person or by proxy a proposal that had been included in a management proxy circular at your request?
      `substantially the same proposal was submitted before and did not receive the prescribed minimum support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was substantially the same proposal submitted to shareholders in a circular for a meeting held within the prescribed period before receipt, and did it fail to receive the prescribed minimum amount of support?
      `the rights conferred by s 137 are being abused to secure publicity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights conferred by section 137 being abused to secure publicity?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation excused from circulating my proposal` IF
    `the corporation is not required to comply with s 137(2) and (3) within s 137(5)` `the proposal is not submitted to the corporation within the prescribed period` `it clearly appears that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance` `it clearly appears that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation` `I failed to present a proposal included in a circular at my request within the prescribed period before this one` `substantially the same proposal was submitted before and did not receive the prescribed minimum support` `the rights conferred by s 137 are being abused to secure publicity`

-- s 137(5.1). The corporation is not required to set out a later proposal of a person who failed to continue to hold the shares up to and including the day of the meeting, if the later meeting is held within the prescribed period after it.
@ref CBCA s 137(5.1)
@export Is the corporation excused from setting out my later proposal because I stopped holding shares (s 137(5.1))?
GIVEN `I failed to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in s 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in subsection 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting?
      `the later meeting is held within the prescribed period following the date of that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the later meeting held within the period the regulations prescribe after the date of that meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation excused from setting out my later proposal because I stopped holding shares` IF
    `the corporation is not required to set out the person's later proposal within s 137(5.1)` `I failed to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in s 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting` `the later meeting is held within the prescribed period following the date of that meeting`

-- s 137(2). A corporation that solicits proxies shall set out the proposal in the management proxy circular or attach it, unless it is excused by (5) or (5.1).
@ref CBCA s 137(2)
@export Must the corporation circulate my proposal in its management proxy circular (s 137(2))?
GIVEN `the corporation solicits proxies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation solicit proxies?
      `a proposal was submitted by a person who may submit it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a proposal submitted to the corporation by a person who may submit it?
      `the proposal is not submitted to the corporation within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your proposal not submitted to the corporation within the period the regulations prescribe?
      `it clearly appears that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it clearly appear that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance against the corporation or its directors, officers or security holders?
      `it clearly appears that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it clearly appear that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation?
      `I failed to present a proposal included in a circular at my request within the prescribed period before this one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, within the prescribed period before the corporation received this proposal, fail to present in person or by proxy a proposal that had been included in a management proxy circular at your request?
      `substantially the same proposal was submitted before and did not receive the prescribed minimum support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was substantially the same proposal submitted to shareholders in a circular for a meeting held within the prescribed period before receipt, and did it fail to receive the prescribed minimum amount of support?
      `the rights conferred by s 137 are being abused to secure publicity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights conferred by section 137 being abused to secure publicity?
      `I failed to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in s 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in subsection 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting?
      `the later meeting is held within the prescribed period following the date of that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the later meeting held within the period the regulations prescribe after the date of that meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation circulate my proposal in its management proxy circular` IF
    `the corporation must circulate the proposal within s 137(2)`
        `the corporation solicits proxies`
        `a proposal was submitted by a person who may submit it`
        (`the corporation is not required to comply with s 137(2) and (3) within s 137(5)`
            `the proposal is not submitted to the corporation within the prescribed period`
            `it clearly appears that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance`
            `it clearly appears that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation`
            `I failed to present a proposal included in a circular at my request within the prescribed period before this one`
            `substantially the same proposal was submitted before and did not receive the prescribed minimum support`
            `the rights conferred by s 137 are being abused to secure publicity`)
        (`the corporation is not required to set out the person's later proposal within s 137(5.1)`
            `I failed to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in s 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting`
            `the later meeting is held within the prescribed period following the date of that meeting`)

-- s 137(2). The duty is met by setting the proposal out in the management proxy circular or attaching it to it.
@ref CBCA s 137(2)
@export Has the corporation done what s 137(2) requires of it for my proposal?
GIVEN `the corporation solicits proxies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation solicit proxies?
      `a proposal was submitted by a person who may submit it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a proposal submitted to the corporation by a person who may submit it?
      `the proposal is not submitted to the corporation within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your proposal not submitted to the corporation within the period the regulations prescribe?
      `it clearly appears that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it clearly appear that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance against the corporation or its directors, officers or security holders?
      `it clearly appears that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it clearly appear that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation?
      `I failed to present a proposal included in a circular at my request within the prescribed period before this one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, within the prescribed period before the corporation received this proposal, fail to present in person or by proxy a proposal that had been included in a management proxy circular at your request?
      `substantially the same proposal was submitted before and did not receive the prescribed minimum support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was substantially the same proposal submitted to shareholders in a circular for a meeting held within the prescribed period before receipt, and did it fail to receive the prescribed minimum amount of support?
      `the rights conferred by s 137 are being abused to secure publicity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights conferred by section 137 being abused to secure publicity?
      `I failed to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in s 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in subsection 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting?
      `the later meeting is held within the prescribed period following the date of that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the later meeting held within the period the regulations prescribe after the date of that meeting?
      `the proposal is set out in the management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proposal set out in the management proxy circular?
      `the proposal is attached to the management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proposal attached to the management proxy circular?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation done what s 137(2) requires of it for my proposal` IF
    `the duty to circulate the proposal is met within s 137(2)`
        (`the corporation must circulate the proposal within s 137(2)`
            `the corporation solicits proxies`
            `a proposal was submitted by a person who may submit it`
            (`the corporation is not required to comply with s 137(2) and (3) within s 137(5)`
                `the proposal is not submitted to the corporation within the prescribed period`
                `it clearly appears that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance`
                `it clearly appears that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation`
                `I failed to present a proposal included in a circular at my request within the prescribed period before this one`
                `substantially the same proposal was submitted before and did not receive the prescribed minimum support`
                `the rights conferred by s 137 are being abused to secure publicity`)
            (`the corporation is not required to set out the person's later proposal within s 137(5.1)`
                `I failed to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in s 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting`
                `the later meeting is held within the prescribed period following the date of that meeting`))
        `the proposal is set out in the management proxy circular`
        `the proposal is attached to the management proxy circular`

-- s 137(3). If the person who submits the proposal so requests, the corporation shall include in or attach to the circular a statement in support, and the person's name and address, within the prescribed word limit together with the proposal.
@ref CBCA s 137(3)
@export Must the corporation include my supporting statement (s 137(3))?
GIVEN `I request a supporting statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask the corporation to include a supporting statement of not more than the prescribed number of words?
      `the corporation solicits proxies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation solicit proxies?
      `a proposal was submitted by a person who may submit it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a proposal submitted to the corporation by a person who may submit it?
      `the proposal is not submitted to the corporation within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your proposal not submitted to the corporation within the period the regulations prescribe?
      `it clearly appears that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it clearly appear that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance against the corporation or its directors, officers or security holders?
      `it clearly appears that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it clearly appear that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation?
      `I failed to present a proposal included in a circular at my request within the prescribed period before this one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, within the prescribed period before the corporation received this proposal, fail to present in person or by proxy a proposal that had been included in a management proxy circular at your request?
      `substantially the same proposal was submitted before and did not receive the prescribed minimum support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was substantially the same proposal submitted to shareholders in a circular for a meeting held within the prescribed period before receipt, and did it fail to receive the prescribed minimum amount of support?
      `the rights conferred by s 137 are being abused to secure publicity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights conferred by section 137 being abused to secure publicity?
      `I failed to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in s 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in subsection 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting?
      `the later meeting is held within the prescribed period following the date of that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the later meeting held within the period the regulations prescribe after the date of that meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation include my supporting statement` IF
    `the corporation must include the supporting statement within s 137(3)`
        `I request a supporting statement`
        (`the corporation must circulate the proposal within s 137(2)`
            `the corporation solicits proxies`
            `a proposal was submitted by a person who may submit it`
            (`the corporation is not required to comply with s 137(2) and (3) within s 137(5)`
                `the proposal is not submitted to the corporation within the prescribed period`
                `it clearly appears that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance`
                `it clearly appears that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation`
                `I failed to present a proposal included in a circular at my request within the prescribed period before this one`
                `substantially the same proposal was submitted before and did not receive the prescribed minimum support`
                `the rights conferred by s 137 are being abused to secure publicity`)
            (`the corporation is not required to set out the person's later proposal within s 137(5.1)`
                `I failed to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in s 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting`
                `the later meeting is held within the prescribed period following the date of that meeting`))

-- s 137(3). The duty is met by including the statement in, or attaching it to, the circular, with the person's name and address.
@ref CBCA s 137(3)
@export Has the corporation done what s 137(3) requires for my supporting statement?
GIVEN `I request a supporting statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you ask the corporation to include a supporting statement of not more than the prescribed number of words?
      `the corporation solicits proxies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation solicit proxies?
      `a proposal was submitted by a person who may submit it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a proposal submitted to the corporation by a person who may submit it?
      `the proposal is not submitted to the corporation within the prescribed period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your proposal not submitted to the corporation within the period the regulations prescribe?
      `it clearly appears that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it clearly appear that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance against the corporation or its directors, officers or security holders?
      `it clearly appears that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it clearly appear that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation?
      `I failed to present a proposal included in a circular at my request within the prescribed period before this one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you, within the prescribed period before the corporation received this proposal, fail to present in person or by proxy a proposal that had been included in a management proxy circular at your request?
      `substantially the same proposal was submitted before and did not receive the prescribed minimum support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was substantially the same proposal submitted to shareholders in a circular for a meeting held within the prescribed period before receipt, and did it fail to receive the prescribed minimum amount of support?
      `the rights conferred by s 137 are being abused to secure publicity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rights conferred by section 137 being abused to secure publicity?
      `I failed to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in s 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in subsection 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting?
      `the later meeting is held within the prescribed period following the date of that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the later meeting held within the period the regulations prescribe after the date of that meeting?
      `the statement is included in the management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your statement included in the management proxy circular?
      `the statement is attached to the management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your statement attached to the management proxy circular?
      `my name and address are included or attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your name and address included or attached?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation done what s 137(3) requires for my supporting statement` IF
    `the duty to include the supporting statement is met within s 137(3)`
        (`the corporation must include the supporting statement within s 137(3)`
            `I request a supporting statement`
            (`the corporation must circulate the proposal within s 137(2)`
                `the corporation solicits proxies`
                `a proposal was submitted by a person who may submit it`
                (`the corporation is not required to comply with s 137(2) and (3) within s 137(5)`
                    `the proposal is not submitted to the corporation within the prescribed period`
                    `it clearly appears that the primary purpose of the proposal is to enforce a personal claim or redress a personal grievance`
                    `it clearly appears that the proposal does not relate in a significant way to the business or affairs of the corporation`
                    `I failed to present a proposal included in a circular at my request within the prescribed period before this one`
                    `substantially the same proposal was submitted before and did not receive the prescribed minimum support`
                    `the rights conferred by s 137 are being abused to secure publicity`)
                (`the corporation is not required to set out the person's later proposal within s 137(5.1)`
                    `I failed to continue to hold or own the number of shares referred to in s 137(1.1) up to and including the day of the meeting`
                    `the later meeting is held within the prescribed period following the date of that meeting`)))
        `the statement is included in the management proxy circular`
        `the statement is attached to the management proxy circular`
        `my name and address are included or attached`

-- s 137(3). The proposal and the statement together must be within the prescribed maximum number of words.
@ref CBCA s 137(3)
@export Is my proposal with its statement within the word limit (s 137(3))?
GIVEN `the words that count toward the prescribed maximum` IS A NUMBER @desc How many words count toward the maximum (the words of your proposal and your supporting statement)?
      `the prescribed maximum number of words` IS A NUMBER @desc What maximum number of words do the regulations prescribe?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my proposal with its statement within the word limit` IF
    `the proposal and the statement are within the word limit within s 137(3)` `the words that count toward the prescribed maximum` `the prescribed maximum number of words`

-- s 137(4). A proposal may include nominations for the election of directors if it is signed by one or more holders of shares representing in the aggregate not less than five per cent of the shares, or five per cent of the shares of a class of shares, entitled to vote at the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 137(4)
@export May my proposal include nominations for directors (s 137(4))?
GIVEN `the proposal is signed by one or more holders of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proposal signed by one or more holders of shares?
      `the fraction of the shares entitled to vote at the meeting that the signers hold` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of all the shares entitled to vote at the meeting do the signers together hold (as a number between 0 and 1)?
      `the fraction of each class of shares entitled to vote at the meeting that the signers hold` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc For each class of shares entitled to vote at the meeting, what fraction of that class do the signers together hold (as numbers between 0 and 1, one for each class)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my proposal include nominations for directors` IF
    `a proposal may include nominations of directors within s 137(4)` `the proposal is signed by one or more holders of shares` `the fraction of the shares entitled to vote at the meeting that the signers hold` `the fraction of each class of shares entitled to vote at the meeting that the signers hold`

-- s 137(6). No corporation or person acting on its behalf incurs any liability by reason only of circulating a proposal or statement in compliance with section 137.
@ref CBCA s 137(6)
@export Is the corporation free of liability for merely circulating a proposal (s 137(6))?
GIVEN `the corporation or a person acting on its behalf circulates a proposal or statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation, or a person acting on its behalf, circulate a proposal or statement?
      `the circulating is in compliance with s 137` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the circulating in compliance with section 137?
      `the liability is claimed by reason only of the circulating` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability claimed by reason only of the circulating?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation free of liability for merely circulating a proposal` IF
    `no liability is incurred by reason only of circulating within s 137(6)` `the corporation or a person acting on its behalf circulates a proposal or statement` `the circulating is in compliance with s 137` `the liability is claimed by reason only of the circulating`

-- s 137(7). If a corporation refuses to include a proposal in a management proxy circular, it shall notify the person submitting it in writing, within the prescribed period, of its intention to omit it and of the reasons for the refusal.
@ref CBCA s 137(7)
@export Must the corporation tell me if it refuses to include my proposal (s 137(7))?
GIVEN `the corporation refuses to include my proposal in a management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation refuse to include your proposal in a management proxy circular?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation tell me if it refuses to include my proposal` IF
    `the corporation must notify the person of the refusal within s 137(7)` `the corporation refuses to include my proposal in a management proxy circular`

-- s 137(7). The notice is in writing, states the intention to omit the proposal and the reasons, and is given within the prescribed period after the day the corporation receives the proposal or the proof of ownership under (1.4).
@ref CBCA s 137(7)
@export Has the corporation notified me of its refusal as the Act requires (s 137(7))?
GIVEN `the corporation refuses to include my proposal in a management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation refuse to include your proposal in a management proxy circular?
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice in writing?
      `the notice states the intention to omit the proposal from the management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the intention to omit the proposal from the management proxy circular?
      `the notice states the reasons for the refusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state the reasons for the refusal?
      `the notice is given within the prescribed period after the day the corporation receives the proposal or the proof of ownership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice given within the period the regulations prescribe after the day the corporation received the proposal or, as the case may be, the proof of ownership?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation notified me of its refusal as the Act requires` IF
    `the duty to notify the person of the refusal is met within s 137(7)`
        (`the corporation must notify the person of the refusal within s 137(7)`
            `the corporation refuses to include my proposal in a management proxy circular`)
        `the notice is in writing`
        `the notice states the intention to omit the proposal from the management proxy circular`
        `the notice states the reasons for the refusal`
        `the notice is given within the prescribed period after the day the corporation receives the proposal or the proof of ownership`

-- s 137(8). A person claiming to be aggrieved by a corporation's refusal to include their proposal may apply to the court.
@ref CBCA s 137(8)
@export May I ask the court for relief because the corporation refused my proposal (s 137(8))?
GIVEN `I submitted the proposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you submit the proposal?
      `I claim to be aggrieved by the corporation's refusal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim to be aggrieved by the corporation's refusal under subsection 137(7)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the court for relief because the corporation refused my proposal` IF
    `a person may apply to the court within s 137(8)` `I submitted the proposal` `I claim to be aggrieved by the corporation's refusal`

-- s 137(9). The corporation or a person claiming to be aggrieved by a proposal may apply to the court for an order permitting the corporation to omit the proposal, and the court may make it if satisfied that subsection (5) applies.
@ref CBCA s 137(9)
@export May the corporation, or a person aggrieved by a proposal, ask the court to let it be omitted (s 137(9))?
GIVEN `the applicant is the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant the corporation?
      `the applicant is a person claiming to be aggrieved by a proposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant a person claiming to be aggrieved by a proposal?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation, or a person aggrieved by a proposal, ask the court to let it be omitted` IF
    `the corporation or an aggrieved person may apply to the court within s 137(9)` `the applicant is the corporation` `the applicant is a person claiming to be aggrieved by a proposal`

-- s 137(9). The court may make an order if satisfied that subsection (5) applies.
@ref CBCA s 137(9)
@export May the court let the corporation omit the proposal (s 137(9))?
GIVEN `an application is made under s 137(9)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made under subsection 137(9)?
      `the court is satisfied that s 137(5) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that subsection 137(5) applies?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court let the corporation omit the proposal` IF
    `the court may make an order on the application within s 137(9)` `an application is made under s 137(9)` `the court is satisfied that s 137(5) applies`

-- s 137(10). An applicant under (8) or (9) shall give the Director notice of the application, and the Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 137(10)
@export Must I give the Director notice of my court application (s 137(10))?
GIVEN `I apply under s 137(8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying under subsection 137(8)?
      `I apply under s 137(9)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying under subsection 137(9)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the Director notice of my court application` IF
    `the applicant must give the Director notice within s 137(10)` `I apply under s 137(8)` `I apply under s 137(9)`

-- s 137(10). The duty is met by giving the Director notice of the application.
@ref CBCA s 137(10)
@export Have I met my duty to notify the Director (s 137(10))?
GIVEN `I apply under s 137(8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying under subsection 137(8)?
      `I apply under s 137(9)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying under subsection 137(9)?
      `I gave the Director notice of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the Director notice of the application?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met my duty to notify the Director` IF
    `the duty to give the Director notice is met within s 137(10)`
        (`the applicant must give the Director notice within s 137(10)`
            `I apply under s 137(8)`
            `I apply under s 137(9)`)
        `I gave the Director notice of the application`

-- s 137(10). The Director is entitled to appear and be heard in person or by counsel on the application.
@ref CBCA s 137(10)
@export Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on my application (s 137(10))?
GIVEN `the application is under s 137(8) or (9)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one under subsection 137(8) or (9)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on my application` IF
    `the Director is entitled to appear and be heard within s 137(10)` `the application is under s 137(8) or (9)`


§§ `Lists of shareholders, quorum and voting at the meeting (ss 138 to 141)`

-- Only when a meeting of shareholders is being held or planned.

-- s 138(1). The corporation shall prepare an alphabetical list of shareholders entitled to receive notice, showing the number of shares held by each: if a record date is fixed under 134(1)(c), not later than ten days after it;
-- if none is fixed, on the record date established under 134(2)(a).
@ref CBCA s 138(1)
@export By when must the corporation prepare the list of shareholders entitled to receive notice (s 138(1))?
GIVEN `a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors fix a record date for receiving notice of the meeting?
      `the record date fixed for receiving notice of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc What record date did they fix for receiving notice?
      `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)` IS A DATE @desc What is the record date established when none is fixed, for receiving notice of the meeting (the day before notice is given, or the day of the meeting if no notice is given)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the corporation prepare the list of shareholders entitled to receive notice` IS
    `the last day to prepare the list of shareholders entitled to receive notice within s 138(1)` (IF `a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)` THEN JUST `the record date fixed for receiving notice of the meeting` ELSE NOTHING) `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)`

-- s 138(1). The list is alphabetical, shows the number of shares held by each shareholder, and is prepared in time.
@ref CBCA s 138(1)
@export Does the list of shareholders entitled to receive notice comply (s 138(1))?
GIVEN `a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors fix a record date for receiving notice of the meeting?
      `the record date fixed for receiving notice of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc What record date did they fix for receiving notice?
      `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)` IS A DATE @desc What is the record date established when none is fixed, for receiving notice of the meeting (the day before notice is given, or the day of the meeting if no notice is given)?
      `the date the list was prepared` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the list prepared?
      `the list is alphabetical` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the list in alphabetical order?
      `the list shows the number of shares held by each shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the list show the number of shares held by each shareholder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the list of shareholders entitled to receive notice comply` IF
    `the list of shareholders entitled to receive notice complies with s 138(1)` (IF `a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)` THEN JUST `the record date fixed for receiving notice of the meeting` ELSE NOTHING) `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)` `the date the list was prepared` `the list is alphabetical` `the list shows the number of shares held by each shareholder`

-- s 138(2), (3). The corporation shall prepare an alphabetical list of shareholders entitled to vote: no later than ten days after the record date for voting if one is fixed; otherwise not later than ten days after the record date fixed for receiving notice, or,
-- if none is fixed, not later than the record date established under 134(2)(a).
@ref CBCA s 138(2), (3)
@export By when must the corporation prepare the list of shareholders entitled to vote (s 138(2) and (3))?
GIVEN `a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors fix a record date for voting at the meeting?
      `the record date fixed for voting at the meeting` IS A DATE @desc What record date did they fix for voting?
      `a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors fix a record date for receiving notice of the meeting?
      `the record date fixed for receiving notice of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc What record date did they fix for receiving notice?
      `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)` IS A DATE @desc What is the record date established when none is fixed, for receiving notice of the meeting (the day before notice is given, or the day of the meeting if no notice is given)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the corporation prepare the list of shareholders entitled to vote` IS
    `the last day to prepare the list of shareholders entitled to vote within s 138(2) and (3)` (IF `a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(d)` THEN JUST `the record date fixed for voting at the meeting` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)` THEN JUST `the record date fixed for receiving notice of the meeting` ELSE NOTHING) `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)`

-- s 138(2), (3). The list is alphabetical, shows the number of shares held by each, and is prepared in time.
@ref CBCA s 138(2), (3)
@export Does the list of shareholders entitled to vote comply (s 138(2) and (3))?
GIVEN `a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors fix a record date for voting at the meeting?
      `the record date fixed for voting at the meeting` IS A DATE @desc What record date did they fix for voting?
      `a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors fix a record date for receiving notice of the meeting?
      `the record date fixed for receiving notice of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc What record date did they fix for receiving notice?
      `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)` IS A DATE @desc What is the record date established when none is fixed, for receiving notice of the meeting (the day before notice is given, or the day of the meeting if no notice is given)?
      `the date the list was prepared` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the list prepared?
      `the list is alphabetical` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the list in alphabetical order?
      `the list shows the number of shares held by each shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the list show the number of shares held by each shareholder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the list of shareholders entitled to vote comply` IF
    `the list of shareholders entitled to vote complies with s 138(2) and (3)` (IF `a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(d)` THEN JUST `the record date fixed for voting at the meeting` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `a record date is fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)` THEN JUST `the record date fixed for receiving notice of the meeting` ELSE NOTHING) `the record date established under paragraph 134(2)(a)` `the date the list was prepared` `the list is alphabetical` `the list shows the number of shares held by each shareholder`

-- s 138(3.1). A shareholder whose name appears on the list is entitled to vote the shares shown opposite their name at the meeting. The text says nothing for a shareholder not on the list.
@ref CBCA s 138(3.1)
@export How many shares may I vote at the meeting (s 138(3.1))?
GIVEN `my name appears on a list prepared under subsection 138(2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your name appear on the list of shareholders entitled to vote?
      `the number of shares shown opposite my name` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares are shown opposite your name on the list?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many shares may I vote at the meeting` IS
    `the shares the shareholder may vote at the meeting within s 138(3.1)` `my name appears on a list prepared under subsection 138(2) or (3)` `the number of shares shown opposite my name`

-- s 138(4). A shareholder may examine the list during usual business hours at the registered office of the corporation or at the place where its central securities register is maintained, and at the meeting for which the list was prepared.
@ref CBCA s 138(4)
@export May I examine the list of shareholders (s 138(4))?
GIVEN `I am a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder?
      `it is during usual business hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it during usual business hours?
      `it is at the registered office of the corporation or at the place where its central securities register is maintained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you at the registered office of the corporation or at the place where its central securities register is maintained?
      `it is at the meeting of shareholders for which the list was prepared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you at the meeting of shareholders for which the list was prepared?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I examine the list of shareholders` IF
    `a shareholder may examine the list within s 138(4)` `I am a shareholder` `it is during usual business hours` `it is at the registered office of the corporation or at the place where its central securities register is maintained` `it is at the meeting of shareholders for which the list was prepared`

-- s 139(1). Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, a quorum of shareholders is present at a meeting if the holders of a majority of the shares entitled to vote at the meeting are present in person or represented by proxy. "Majority" is more than half.
@ref CBCA s 139(1)
@export Is there a quorum of shareholders at the meeting (s 139(1))?
GIVEN `the by-laws provide a different quorum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws provide a quorum other than a majority of the shares entitled to vote?
      `the quorum the by-laws provide is present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the quorum that the by-laws provide present?
      `the number of shares entitled to vote at the meeting held by those present in person or represented by proxy` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares entitled to vote at the meeting are held by those present in person or represented by proxy?
      `the number of shares entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares are entitled to vote at the meeting in all?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is there a quorum of shareholders at the meeting` IF
    `a quorum of shareholders is present within s 139(1)` `the by-laws provide a different quorum` `the quorum the by-laws provide is present` `the number of shares entitled to vote at the meeting held by those present in person or represented by proxy` `the number of shares entitled to vote at the meeting`

-- s 139(2). If a quorum is present at the opening of the meeting, the shareholders present may, unless the by-laws otherwise provide, proceed with the business although a quorum is not present throughout.
@ref CBCA s 139(2)
@export May the meeting go on if people leave and the quorum is lost (s 139(2))?
GIVEN `a quorum is present at the opening of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a quorum present at the opening of the meeting?
      `the by-laws otherwise provide that the meeting may not proceed without a quorum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws provide otherwise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the meeting go on if people leave and the quorum is lost` IF
    `the shareholders present may proceed with the business within s 139(2)` `a quorum is present at the opening of the meeting` `the by-laws otherwise provide that the meeting may not proceed without a quorum`

-- s 139(3). If a quorum is not present at the opening of any meeting, the shareholders present may adjourn the meeting to a fixed time and place but may not transact any other business.
@ref CBCA s 139(3)
@export May the shareholders present adjourn the meeting if there is no quorum (s 139(3))?
GIVEN `a quorum is present at the opening of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a quorum present at the opening of the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the shareholders present adjourn the meeting if there is no quorum` IF
    `the shareholders present may adjourn the meeting to a fixed time and place within s 139(3)` `a quorum is present at the opening of the meeting`

-- s 139(3). The same sentence: without a quorum at the opening, the shareholders present may not transact any other business. The text says nothing on this point when a quorum was present.
@ref CBCA s 139(3)
@export May the shareholders present transact other business if there is no quorum (s 139(3))?
GIVEN `a quorum is present at the opening of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a quorum present at the opening of the meeting?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the shareholders present transact other business if there is no quorum` IS
    `the shareholders present may transact other business within s 139(3)` `a quorum is present at the opening of the meeting`

-- s 139(4). If a corporation has only one shareholder, or only one holder of any class or series of shares, the shareholder present in person or by proxy constitutes a meeting.
@ref CBCA s 139(4)
@export Does a lone shareholder constitute a meeting (s 139(4))?
GIVEN `the corporation has only one shareholder, or only one holder of the class or series of shares in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have only one shareholder, or only one holder of the class or series of shares in question?
      `that shareholder is present in person or by proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that shareholder present in person or by proxy?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a lone shareholder constitute a meeting` IF
    `the shareholder present constitutes a meeting within s 139(4)` `the corporation has only one shareholder, or only one holder of the class or series of shares in question` `that shareholder is present in person or by proxy`

-- s 140(1). Unless the articles otherwise provide, each share of a corporation entitles the holder to one vote at a meeting of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 140(1)
@export How many votes does each share carry (s 140(1))?
GIVEN `the articles provide a number of votes per share other than one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide for a number of votes per share other than one?
      `the votes per share the articles provide` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes per share do the articles provide? (0 if they do not say)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many votes does each share carry` IS
    `the votes each share carries within s 140(1)`
        `the articles provide a number of votes per share other than one`
        (IF `the articles provide a number of votes per share other than one` AND `the votes per share the articles provide` GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST `the votes per share the articles provide` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 140(1). The holder of shares may cast the votes the shares carry.
@ref CBCA s 140(1)
@export How many votes may I cast at the meeting (s 140(1))?
GIVEN `the number of shares I hold` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shares do you hold that are entitled to vote?
      `the articles provide a number of votes per share other than one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide for a number of votes per share other than one?
      `the votes per share the articles provide` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes per share do the articles provide? (0 if they do not say)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How many votes may I cast at the meeting` IS
    `the votes a holder may cast within s 140(1)`
        `the number of shares I hold`
        (`the votes each share carries within s 140(1)`
            `the articles provide a number of votes per share other than one`
            (IF `the articles provide a number of votes per share other than one` AND `the votes per share the articles provide` GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST `the votes per share the articles provide` ELSE NOTHING))

-- s 140(2). If a body corporate or association is a shareholder, the corporation shall recognize any individual authorized by a resolution of the directors or governing body to represent it at meetings of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 140(2)
@export Must the corporation recognize my representative at the meeting (s 140(2))?
GIVEN `the shareholder is a body corporate or association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the shareholder a body corporate or association?
      `the individual is authorized by a resolution of the directors or governing body to represent it at meetings of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the individual authorized by a resolution of the directors or governing body of the shareholder to represent it at meetings of shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation recognize my representative at the meeting` IF
    `the corporation must recognize the individual as the representative within s 140(2)` `the shareholder is a body corporate or association` `the individual is authorized by a resolution of the directors or governing body to represent it at meetings of shareholders`

-- s 140(3). An individual so authorized may exercise on behalf of the body corporate or association all the powers it could exercise if it were an individual shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 140(3)
@export May my representative exercise all my powers at the meeting (s 140(3))?
GIVEN `the individual is authorized under subsection 140(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the individual authorized as the representative of the body corporate or association under subsection 140(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my representative exercise all my powers at the meeting` IF
    `the representative may exercise all the powers of an individual shareholder within s 140(3)` `the individual is authorized under subsection 140(2)`

-- s 140(4). Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, where shares are held jointly and one or more joint holders are present at a meeting, one of them may, in the absence of the others, vote the shares.
@ref CBCA s 140(4)
@export May I vote jointly held shares if the other joint holders are absent (s 140(4))?
GIVEN `the by-laws provide otherwise about joint holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws provide otherwise about the voting of jointly held shares?
      `the shares are held jointly by two or more persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held jointly by two or more persons?
      `the number of those holders present at the meeting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the joint holders are present at the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I vote jointly held shares if the other joint holders are absent` IF
    `one joint holder present may vote the shares in the absence of the others within s 140(4)` `the by-laws provide otherwise about joint holders` `the shares are held jointly by two or more persons` `the number of those holders present at the meeting`

-- s 140(4). If two or more of the joint holders are present, in person or by proxy, they shall vote as one on the shares jointly held by them.
@ref CBCA s 140(4)
@export Must joint holders who are both present vote as one (s 140(4))?
GIVEN `the by-laws provide otherwise about joint holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws provide otherwise about the voting of jointly held shares?
      `the shares are held jointly by two or more persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares held jointly by two or more persons?
      `the number of those holders who are present and who vote` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the joint holders are present, in person or by proxy, and vote?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must joint holders who are both present vote as one` IF
    `the joint holders who vote must vote as one within s 140(4)` `the by-laws provide otherwise about joint holders` `the shares are held jointly by two or more persons` `the number of those holders who are present and who vote`

-- s 141(1). Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, voting at a meeting shall be by show of hands except where a ballot is demanded by a shareholder or proxyholder entitled to vote at the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 141(1)
@export Will the vote be by show of hands (s 141(1))?
GIVEN `the by-laws provide for voting by another means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws provide for voting by some means other than a show of hands?
      `a ballot is demanded by a shareholder or proxyholder entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a shareholder or proxyholder entitled to vote demanded a ballot?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the vote be by show of hands` IF
    `voting is by show of hands within s 141(1)` `the by-laws provide for voting by another means` `a ballot is demanded by a shareholder or proxyholder entitled to vote at the meeting`

-- s 141(2). A shareholder or proxyholder may demand a ballot either before or after any vote by show of hands.
@ref CBCA s 141(2)
@export May I demand a ballot (s 141(2))?
GIVEN `I am a shareholder or proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder or proxyholder?
      `I make the demand before or after a vote by show of hands` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you making the demand before or after a vote by show of hands?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I demand a ballot` IF
    `a ballot may be demanded within s 141(2)` `I am a shareholder or proxyholder` `I make the demand before or after a vote by show of hands`

-- s 141(3). Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, the corporation may make a communication facility available so that a vote can be held entirely by electronic means, in accordance with the regulations, if any.
@ref CBCA s 141(3)
@export May the vote be held entirely by electronic means (s 141(3))?
GIVEN `the by-laws prevent a vote by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws provide that a vote may not be held by electronic means?
      `the corporation makes a communication facility available for the vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation make a communication facility available for the vote?
      `the vote is held in accordance with the regulations, if any` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the vote held in accordance with the regulations, if any?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the vote be held entirely by electronic means` IF
    `a vote may be held entirely by electronic means within s 141(3)` `the by-laws prevent a vote by electronic means` `the corporation makes a communication facility available for the vote` `the vote is held in accordance with the regulations, if any`

-- s 141(4). Unless the by-laws otherwise provide, a person participating in a meeting under subsection 132(4) or (5) and entitled to vote may vote by means of a communication facility the corporation has made available for the purpose, in accordance with the regulations, if any.
@ref CBCA s 141(4)
@export May I vote by electronic means from where I am (s 141(4))?
GIVEN `I participate in the meeting under subsection 132(4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you taking part in the meeting by electronic means under subsection 132(4) or (5)?
      `I am entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to vote at the meeting?
      `the by-laws prevent voting by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the by-laws provide that you may not vote by electronic means?
      `the corporation has made a communication facility available for voting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation made a communication facility available for voting?
      `my vote is cast in accordance with the regulations, if any` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your vote cast in accordance with the regulations, if any?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I vote by electronic means from where I am` IF
    `a participant may vote by the facility within s 141(4)` `I participate in the meeting under subsection 132(4) or (5)` `I am entitled to vote at the meeting` `the by-laws prevent voting by electronic means` `the corporation has made a communication facility available for voting` `my vote is cast in accordance with the regulations, if any`


§§ `Written resolutions and the minutes (s 142)`

-- Only if shareholders are passing a resolution in writing instead of at a meeting.

-- s 142(1)(a). Except where a written statement is submitted by a director under subsection 110(2) or by an auditor under subsection 168(5), a resolution in writing signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it is as valid as if passed at a meeting.
@ref CBCA s 142(1)(a)
@export Is a resolution that every voting shareholder signed as valid as one passed at a meeting (s 142(1)(a))?
GIVEN `a written statement is submitted by a director under subsection 110(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a director submitted a written statement under subsection 110(2) giving reasons for resigning or opposing a proposal?
      `a written statement is submitted by an auditor under subsection 168(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor submitted a written statement under subsection 168(5)?
      `the resolution is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution in writing?
      `the resolution is signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it at a meeting of shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a resolution that every voting shareholder signed as valid as one passed at a meeting` IF
    `a written resolution is as valid as if passed at a meeting within s 142(1)(a)` `a written statement is submitted by a director under subsection 110(2)` `a written statement is submitted by an auditor under subsection 168(5)` `the resolution is in writing` `the resolution is signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on it at a meeting of shareholders`

-- s 142(1)(b). A resolution in writing dealing with all matters required by the Act to be dealt with at a meeting, signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote at that meeting, satisfies all the requirements of the Act relating to meetings of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 142(1)(b)
@export Does a written resolution satisfy the requirement to hold a meeting (s 142(1)(b))?
GIVEN `a written statement is submitted by a director under subsection 110(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a director submitted a written statement under subsection 110(2) giving reasons for resigning or opposing a proposal?
      `a written statement is submitted by an auditor under subsection 168(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor submitted a written statement under subsection 168(5)?
      `the resolution is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution in writing?
      `the resolution deals with all matters required by the Act to be dealt with at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resolution deal with all matters the Act requires to be dealt with at a meeting of shareholders?
      `the resolution is signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote at that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote at that meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a written resolution satisfy the requirement to hold a meeting` IF
    `a written resolution satisfies the requirements relating to meetings within s 142(1)(b)` `a written statement is submitted by a director under subsection 110(2)` `a written statement is submitted by an auditor under subsection 168(5)` `the resolution is in writing` `the resolution deals with all matters required by the Act to be dealt with at a meeting of shareholders` `the resolution is signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote at that meeting`

-- s 142(2). A copy of every resolution referred to in subsection (1) shall be kept with the minutes of the meetings of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 142(2)
@export Must the corporation keep a copy of the written resolution with the minutes (s 142(2))?
GIVEN `the resolution is one referred to in subsection 142(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one referred to in subsection 142(1) (a written resolution signed by all the voting shareholders)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation keep a copy of the written resolution with the minutes` IF
    `the corporation must keep a copy of the resolution with the minutes within s 142(2)` `the resolution is one referred to in subsection 142(1)`

-- s 142(2). The duty is met by keeping a copy with the minutes of the meetings of shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 142(2)
@export Has the corporation kept a copy of the resolution as required (s 142(2))?
GIVEN `the resolution is one referred to in subsection 142(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution one referred to in subsection 142(1) (a written resolution signed by all the voting shareholders)?
      `a copy is kept with the minutes of the meetings of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a copy kept with the minutes of the meetings of shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation kept a copy of the resolution as required` IF
    `the duty to keep a copy of the resolution is met within s 142(2)`
        (`the corporation must keep a copy of the resolution with the minutes within s 142(2)`
            `the resolution is one referred to in subsection 142(1)`)
        `a copy is kept with the minutes of the meetings of shareholders`

-- s 142(3). Unless a ballot is demanded, an entry in the minutes that the chairperson declared a resolution carried or defeated is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof of the fact without proof of the number or proportion of the votes.
@ref CBCA s 142(3)
@export Is the minutes entry proof that the resolution was carried or defeated (s 142(3))?
GIVEN `a ballot is demanded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a ballot demanded?
      `the minutes of the meeting have an entry that the chairperson of the meeting declared a resolution to be carried or defeated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the minutes have an entry that the chairperson declared the resolution carried or defeated?
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence to the contrary?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the minutes entry proof that the resolution was carried or defeated` IF
    `the minutes entry is proof of the declaration within s 142(3)` `a ballot is demanded` `the minutes of the meeting have an entry that the chairperson of the meeting declared a resolution to be carried or defeated` `there is evidence to the contrary`


§§ `Requisitioning a meeting and calling one yourself (s 143)`

-- Only if you and other shareholders want the directors to call a meeting, or the directors have received a requisition.

-- s 143(1). The holders of not less than five per cent of the issued shares of a corporation that carry the right to vote at a meeting sought to be held may requisition the directors to call a meeting of shareholders for the purposes stated in the requisition.
@ref CBCA s 143(1)
@export May we requisition the directors to call a meeting (s 143(1))?
GIVEN `the fraction of the issued shares that carry the right to vote at the meeting sought, held by the requisitioners` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the issued shares that carry the right to vote at the meeting sought do the shareholders making the requisition hold (as a number between 0 and 1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we requisition the directors to call a meeting` IF
    `holders may requisition the directors to call a meeting within s 143(1)` `the fraction of the issued shares that carry the right to vote at the meeting sought, held by the requisitioners`

-- s 143(2). The requisition, which may consist of several documents of like form each signed by one or more shareholders, shall state the business to be transacted and shall be sent to each director and to the registered office of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 143(2)
@export Does our requisition take the form the Act requires (s 143(2))?
GIVEN `the requisition states the business to be transacted at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the requisition state the business to be transacted at the meeting?
      `the requisition is sent to each director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requisition sent to each director?
      `the requisition is sent to the registered office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requisition sent to the registered office of the corporation?
      `if the requisition consists of several documents, they are of like form and each is signed by one or more shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the requisition consists of several documents, are they of like form and is each signed by one or more shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our requisition take the form the Act requires` IF
    `the requisition complies with s 143(2)` `the requisition states the business to be transacted at the meeting` `the requisition is sent to each director` `the requisition is sent to the registered office of the corporation` `if the requisition consists of several documents, they are of like form and each is signed by one or more shareholders`

-- s 143(3). On receiving the requisition, the directors shall call a meeting to transact the business stated in it, unless (a) a record date has been fixed and notice of it given, (b) the directors have already called a meeting and given notice, or (c) the business includes the matters in paragraphs 137(5)(b) to (e).
@ref CBCA s 143(3)
@export Must the directors call the meeting we requisitioned (s 143(3))?
GIVEN `the fraction of the issued shares that carry the right to vote at the meeting sought, held by the requisitioners` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the issued shares that carry the right to vote at the meeting sought do the shareholders making the requisition hold (as a number between 0 and 1)?
      `the requisition states the business to be transacted at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the requisition state the business to be transacted at the meeting?
      `the requisition is sent to each director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requisition sent to each director?
      `the requisition is sent to the registered office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requisition sent to the registered office of the corporation?
      `if the requisition consists of several documents, they are of like form and each is signed by one or more shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the requisition consists of several documents, are they of like form and is each signed by one or more shareholders?
      `a record date has been fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the board fixed a record date for receiving notice of a meeting of shareholders?
      `notice of the record date has been given under subsection 134(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice of that record date been given?
      `the directors have called a meeting of shareholders and have given notice of it under section 135` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors already called a meeting of shareholders and given notice of it?
      `the business stated in the requisition includes matters described in paragraphs 137(5)(b) to (e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the business stated in the requisition include a personal grievance, a matter not significantly related to the business, or a repeat of a proposal that failed (the matters in paragraphs 137(5)(b) to (e))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the directors call the meeting we requisitioned` IF
    `the directors must call the meeting within s 143(3)`
        (`holders may requisition the directors to call a meeting within s 143(1)`
            `the fraction of the issued shares that carry the right to vote at the meeting sought, held by the requisitioners`)
        (`the requisition complies with s 143(2)`
            `the requisition states the business to be transacted at the meeting`
            `the requisition is sent to each director`
            `the requisition is sent to the registered office of the corporation`
            `if the requisition consists of several documents, they are of like form and each is signed by one or more shareholders`)
        `a record date has been fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)`
        `notice of the record date has been given under subsection 134(3)`
        `the directors have called a meeting of shareholders and have given notice of it under section 135`
        `the business stated in the requisition includes matters described in paragraphs 137(5)(b) to (e)`

-- s 143(4). If the directors do not within twenty-one days after receiving the requisition call a meeting, any shareholder who signed the requisition may call the meeting. The day of receipt is day 0.
@ref CBCA s 143(4)
@export By when must the directors call the requisitioned meeting (s 143(4))?
GIVEN `the date the directors received the requisition` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the directors receive the requisition?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the directors call the requisitioned meeting` IS
    `the last day for the directors to call the meeting within s 143(4)` `the date the directors received the requisition`

-- s 143(4). A shareholder who signed the requisition may call the meeting if the directors were required to call it and have not done so within twenty-one days after receiving it.
@ref CBCA s 143(4)
@export May I call the meeting myself because the directors have not (s 143(4))?
GIVEN `I signed the requisition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you sign the requisition?
      `the fraction of the issued shares that carry the right to vote at the meeting sought, held by the requisitioners` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of the issued shares that carry the right to vote at the meeting sought do the shareholders making the requisition hold (as a number between 0 and 1)?
      `the requisition states the business to be transacted at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the requisition state the business to be transacted at the meeting?
      `the requisition is sent to each director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requisition sent to each director?
      `the requisition is sent to the registered office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requisition sent to the registered office of the corporation?
      `if the requisition consists of several documents, they are of like form and each is signed by one or more shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the requisition consists of several documents, are they of like form and is each signed by one or more shareholders?
      `a record date has been fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the board fixed a record date for receiving notice of a meeting of shareholders?
      `notice of the record date has been given under subsection 134(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has notice of that record date been given?
      `the directors have called a meeting of shareholders and have given notice of it under section 135` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors already called a meeting of shareholders and given notice of it?
      `the business stated in the requisition includes matters described in paragraphs 137(5)(b) to (e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the business stated in the requisition include a personal grievance, a matter not significantly related to the business, or a repeat of a proposal that failed (the matters in paragraphs 137(5)(b) to (e))?
      `the date the directors received the requisition` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the directors receive the requisition?
      `the directors have called a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the directors called a meeting?
      `the date the directors called a meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the directors call the meeting?
      `the date I call the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you call the meeting yourself?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I call the meeting myself because the directors have not` IF
    `a shareholder who signed may call the meeting within s 143(4)`
        `I signed the requisition`
        (`the directors must call the meeting within s 143(3)`
            (`holders may requisition the directors to call a meeting within s 143(1)`
                `the fraction of the issued shares that carry the right to vote at the meeting sought, held by the requisitioners`)
            (`the requisition complies with s 143(2)`
                `the requisition states the business to be transacted at the meeting`
                `the requisition is sent to each director`
                `the requisition is sent to the registered office of the corporation`
                `if the requisition consists of several documents, they are of like form and each is signed by one or more shareholders`)
            `a record date has been fixed under paragraph 134(1)(c)`
            `notice of the record date has been given under subsection 134(3)`
            `the directors have called a meeting of shareholders and have given notice of it under section 135`
            `the business stated in the requisition includes matters described in paragraphs 137(5)(b) to (e)`)
        `the date the directors received the requisition`
        (IF `the directors have called a meeting` THEN JUST `the date the directors called a meeting` ELSE NOTHING)
        `the date I call the meeting`

-- s 143(5). A meeting called under this section shall be called as nearly as possible in the manner in which meetings are to be called pursuant to the by-laws, Part XII and Part XIII.
@ref CBCA s 143(5)
@export Is the meeting we called under section 143 called in the manner the Act requires (s 143(5))?
GIVEN `the meeting is called under s 143` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting called under section 143?
      `it is called as nearly as possible in the manner in which meetings are to be called pursuant to the by-laws, this Part and Part XIII` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it called as nearly as possible in the manner in which meetings are to be called under the by-laws, Part XII and Part XIII?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the meeting we called under section 143 called in the manner the Act requires` IF
    `the meeting is called as s 143(5) requires within s 143(5)` `the meeting is called under s 143` `it is called as nearly as possible in the manner in which meetings are to be called pursuant to the by-laws, this Part and Part XIII`

-- s 143(6). Unless the shareholders otherwise resolve at a meeting called under subsection (4), the corporation shall reimburse the shareholders the expenses reasonably incurred by them in requisitioning, calling and holding the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 143(6)
@export Must the corporation reimburse my expenses for requisitioning and calling the meeting (s 143(6))?
GIVEN `a requisition was made under s 143(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a requisition made under subsection 143(1)?
      `the meeting was called by the shareholders under s 143(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the meeting called by the shareholders under subsection 143(4)?
      `the shareholders resolved otherwise at that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the shareholders resolve at that meeting that the corporation should not reimburse the expenses?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation reimburse my expenses for requisitioning and calling the meeting` IF
    `the corporation must reimburse the shareholders' expenses within s 143(6)` `a requisition was made under s 143(1)` `the meeting was called by the shareholders under s 143(4)` `the shareholders resolved otherwise at that meeting`

-- s 143(6). The amount is the expenses reasonably incurred. If the corporation need not reimburse, there is no amount.
@ref CBCA s 143(6)
@export How much must the corporation reimburse me (s 143(6))?
GIVEN `a requisition was made under s 143(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a requisition made under subsection 143(1)?
      `the meeting was called by the shareholders under s 143(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the meeting called by the shareholders under subsection 143(4)?
      `the shareholders resolved otherwise at that meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the shareholders resolve at that meeting that the corporation should not reimburse the expenses?
      `the expenses reasonably incurred by the shareholders in requisitioning, calling and holding the meeting, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What expenses did the shareholders reasonably incur in requisitioning, calling and holding the meeting, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must the corporation reimburse me` IS
    `the amount to reimburse within s 143(6)`
        (`the corporation must reimburse the shareholders' expenses within s 143(6)`
            `a requisition was made under s 143(1)`
            `the meeting was called by the shareholders under s 143(4)`
            `the shareholders resolved otherwise at that meeting`)
        `the expenses reasonably incurred by the shareholders in requisitioning, calling and holding the meeting, in dollars`


§§ `Asking the court for a meeting (s 144)`

-- Only if a meeting cannot practicably be called or held in the usual way.

-- s 144(1). A court, on the application of a director, a shareholder who is entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders or the Director, may order a meeting to be called, held and conducted in the manner the court directs.
@ref CBCA s 144(1)
@export May I ask the court to order a meeting to be called (s 144(1))?
GIVEN `the applicant is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director?
      `the applicant is a shareholder entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders?
      `the applicant is the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Director appointed under the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the court to order a meeting to be called` IF
    `a person may apply to the court for a meeting within s 144(1)` `the applicant is a director` `the applicant is a shareholder entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders` `the applicant is the Director`

-- s 144(1). The court may order the meeting if (a) it is impracticable to call it in time or in the manner required, (b) it is impracticable to conduct it as the Act or by-laws require, or (c) the court thinks for any other reason that it should be called, held and conducted as it directs.
@ref CBCA s 144(1)
@export May the court order the meeting to be called, held and conducted (s 144(1))?
GIVEN `the applicant is a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director?
      `the applicant is a shareholder entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders?
      `the applicant is the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Director appointed under the Act?
      `it is impracticable to call the meeting within the time or in the manner in which those meetings are to be called` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it impracticable to call the meeting within the time or in the manner in which those meetings are to be called?
      `it is impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner required by this Act or the by-laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner the Act or the by-laws require?
      `the court thinks that the meeting should be called, held and conducted within the time or in the manner it directs for any other reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court think, for any other reason, that the meeting should be called, held and conducted within the time or in the manner it directs?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court order the meeting to be called, held and conducted` IF
    `the court may order a meeting to be called, held and conducted within s 144(1)`
        (`a person may apply to the court for a meeting within s 144(1)`
            `the applicant is a director`
            `the applicant is a shareholder entitled to vote at a meeting of shareholders`
            `the applicant is the Director`)
        `it is impracticable to call the meeting within the time or in the manner in which those meetings are to be called`
        `it is impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner required by this Act or the by-laws`
        `the court thinks that the meeting should be called, held and conducted within the time or in the manner it directs for any other reason`

-- s 144(2). Without restricting (1), the court may order that the quorum required by the by-laws or the Act be varied or dispensed with at a meeting called, held and conducted pursuant to section 144.
@ref CBCA s 144(2)
@export May the court vary or dispense with the quorum at that meeting (s 144(2))?
GIVEN `the meeting is called, held and conducted pursuant to s 144` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting called, held and conducted pursuant to a court order under section 144?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court vary or dispense with the quorum at that meeting` IF
    `the court may vary or dispense with the quorum within s 144(2)` `the meeting is called, held and conducted pursuant to s 144`

-- s 144(3). A meeting called, held and conducted pursuant to this section is for all purposes a meeting of shareholders duly called, held and conducted.
@ref CBCA s 144(3)
@export Is a meeting held on the court's order a valid meeting (s 144(3))?
GIVEN `the meeting is called, held and conducted pursuant to s 144` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting called, held and conducted pursuant to a court order under section 144?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a meeting held on the court's order a valid meeting` IF
    `the meeting is for all purposes a meeting duly called, held and conducted within s 144(3)` `the meeting is called, held and conducted pursuant to s 144`


§§ `Disputes about the election or appointment of a director or auditor (s 145)`

-- Only if the election or appointment of a director or auditor is in dispute.

-- s 145(1). A corporation or a shareholder or director may apply to a court to determine any controversy with respect to an election or appointment of a director or auditor of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 145(1)
@export May I ask the court to settle a dispute about an election or appointment of a director or auditor (s 145(1))?
GIVEN `the applicant is the corporation, a shareholder or a director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the corporation, a shareholder or a director?
      `the controversy is with respect to an election or appointment of a director or auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the dispute about an election or appointment of a director or auditor of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the court to settle a dispute about an election or appointment of a director or auditor` IF
    `a person may apply to the court to determine a controversy within s 145(1)` `the applicant is the corporation, a shareholder or a director` `the controversy is with respect to an election or appointment of a director or auditor of the corporation`

-- s 145(2). On an application under this section the court may make any order it thinks fit, including (a) an order restraining a director or auditor whose election or appointment is challenged from acting pending determination, (b) declaring the result, (c) requiring a new election or appointment with directions, (d) determining the voting rights of shareholders and of persons claiming to own shares.
@ref CBCA s 145(2)
@export May the court make this kind of order on my application (s 145(2))?
GIVEN `the application is made under s 145` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made under section 145?
      `the kind of order` IS A `Kind of order under s 145(2)` @desc Which kind of order is in question (restraining a director or auditor from acting pending the decision, declaring the result of the election or appointment, requiring a new election or appointment with directions, determining voting rights, or any other order the court thinks fit)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court make this kind of order on my application` IF
    `the court may make an order of a kind within s 145(2)` `the application is made under s 145` `the kind of order`


§§ `Agreements among shareholders (ss 145.1 and 146)`

-- Only if shareholders have signed, or are asked to sign, a written agreement about how they vote or how the business is run.

-- s 145.1. A written agreement between two or more shareholders may provide that in exercising voting rights the shares held by them shall be voted as provided in the agreement.
@ref CBCA s 145.1
@export May we agree in writing how our shares are voted (s 145.1)?
GIVEN `the agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement in writing?
      `the number of shareholders who are parties to the agreement` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shareholders are parties to the agreement?
      `the agreement provides how the shares held by them are to be voted in exercising voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement provide how the shares they hold are to be voted in exercising voting rights?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we agree in writing how our shares are voted` IF
    `an agreement may bind the shares to be voted as provided within s 145.1` `the agreement is in writing` `the number of shareholders who are parties to the agreement` `the agreement provides how the shares held by them are to be voted in exercising voting rights`

-- s 146(1). An otherwise lawful written agreement among all the shareholders of a corporation, or among all the shareholders and one or more persons who are not shareholders, that restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation is valid.
@ref CBCA s 146(1)
@export Is our shareholders' agreement that restricts the directors valid (s 146(1))?
GIVEN `the agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement in writing?
      `the agreement is otherwise lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement otherwise lawful?
      `all the shareholders of the corporation are parties to the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the shareholders of the corporation parties to the agreement (with or without other persons)?
      `the agreement restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement restrict, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our shareholders' agreement that restricts the directors valid` IF
    `the agreement is valid within s 146(1)` `the agreement is in writing` `the agreement is otherwise lawful` `all the shareholders of the corporation are parties to the agreement` `the agreement restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation`

-- s 146(2). If a person who is the beneficial owner of all the issued shares of a corporation makes a written declaration that restricts the powers of the directors, the declaration is deemed to be a unanimous shareholder agreement.
@ref CBCA s 146(2)
@export Is my written declaration as sole owner treated as a unanimous shareholder agreement (s 146(2))?
GIVEN `I am the beneficial owner of all the issued shares of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the beneficial owner of all the issued shares of the corporation?
      `my declaration is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your declaration in writing?
      `my declaration restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your declaration restrict, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my written declaration as sole owner treated as a unanimous shareholder agreement` IF
    `the declaration is deemed to be a unanimous shareholder agreement within s 146(2)` `I am the beneficial owner of all the issued shares of the corporation` `my declaration is in writing` `my declaration restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation`

-- s 146(1), (2). There is a unanimous shareholder agreement if a valid agreement among all the shareholders under (1) is made, or a single owner of all the shares makes a declaration under (2).
@ref CBCA s 146(1), (2)
@export Is there a unanimous shareholder agreement (s 146(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `the agreement is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement in writing?
      `the agreement is otherwise lawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the agreement otherwise lawful?
      `all the shareholders of the corporation are parties to the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the shareholders of the corporation parties to the agreement (with or without other persons)?
      `the agreement restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the agreement restrict, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation?
      `I am the beneficial owner of all the issued shares of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the beneficial owner of all the issued shares of the corporation?
      `my declaration is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your declaration in writing?
      `my declaration restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your declaration restrict, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is there a unanimous shareholder agreement` IF
    `there is a unanimous shareholder agreement within s 146(1) and (2)`
        (`the agreement is valid within s 146(1)`
            `the agreement is in writing`
            `the agreement is otherwise lawful`
            `all the shareholders of the corporation are parties to the agreement`
            `the agreement restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation`)
        (`the declaration is deemed to be a unanimous shareholder agreement within s 146(2)`
            `I am the beneficial owner of all the issued shares of the corporation`
            `my declaration is in writing`
            `my declaration restricts, in whole or in part, the powers of the directors to manage, or supervise the management of, the business and affairs of the corporation`)

-- s 146(3). A purchaser or transferee of shares subject to a unanimous shareholder agreement is deemed to be a party to the agreement.
@ref CBCA s 146(3)
@export Am I bound by the unanimous shareholder agreement as a buyer of shares (s 146(3))?
GIVEN `I am a purchaser or transferee of shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a purchaser or transferee of shares of the corporation?
      `the shares are subject to a unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares subject to a unanimous shareholder agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I bound by the unanimous shareholder agreement as a buyer of shares` IF
    `the purchaser or transferee is deemed to be a party within s 146(3)` `I am a purchaser or transferee of shares` `the shares are subject to a unanimous shareholder agreement`

-- s 146(4). If notice is not given to a purchaser or transferee of the existence of a unanimous shareholder agreement, they may, no later than 30 days after they become aware of it, rescind the transaction by which they acquired the shares. The day of awareness is day 0.
@ref CBCA s 146(4)
@export By when must I rescind my purchase of shares that turned out to be subject to a unanimous shareholder agreement (s 146(4))?
GIVEN `the date I became aware of the unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you become aware of the unanimous shareholder agreement?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I rescind my purchase of shares that turned out to be subject to a unanimous shareholder agreement` IS
    `the last day to rescind within s 146(4)` `the date I became aware of the unanimous shareholder agreement`

-- s 146(4). The purchaser or transferee may rescind only if no notice of the agreement was given to them, and only within thirty days after they become aware of it.
@ref CBCA s 146(4)
@export May I rescind my purchase because nobody told me about the unanimous shareholder agreement (s 146(4))?
GIVEN `notice of the existence of the agreement was given to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice of the existence of the agreement given to you, in the manner referred to in subsection 49(8) or otherwise?
      `the date I became aware of the unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you become aware of the unanimous shareholder agreement?
      `the date I rescind the transaction` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you rescind the transaction?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I rescind my purchase because nobody told me about the unanimous shareholder agreement` IF
    `the purchaser or transferee may rescind the transaction within s 146(4)` `notice of the existence of the agreement was given to me` `the date I became aware of the unanimous shareholder agreement` `the date I rescind the transaction`

-- s 146(5). To the extent that a unanimous shareholder agreement restricts the powers of the directors, the parties who are given that power to manage have all the rights, powers, duties and liabilities of a director, whether under the Act or otherwise, including any defences available to the directors.
@ref CBCA s 146(5)
@export Do I take on a director's rights, powers, duties and liabilities because the agreement gives me the power to manage (s 146(5))?
GIVEN `the right, power, duty or liability is one the agreement takes from the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the right, power, duty or liability one that the agreement takes away from the directors?
      `I am a party to the agreement who is given the power to manage or supervise the management of the business and affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the agreement who is given the power to manage or supervise the management of the business and affairs of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I take on a director's rights, powers, duties and liabilities because the agreement gives me the power to manage` IF
    `the party has the right, power, duty or liability of a director within s 146(5)` `the right, power, duty or liability is one the agreement takes from the directors` `I am a party to the agreement who is given the power to manage or supervise the management of the business and affairs`

-- s 146(5). The directors are relieved of the same rights, powers, duties and liabilities, including their liabilities under section 119, to the same extent.
@ref CBCA s 146(5)
@export Are the directors relieved of a duty or liability that the agreement gives to the shareholders (s 146(5))?
GIVEN `the right, power, duty or liability is one the agreement takes from the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the right, power, duty or liability one that the agreement takes away from the directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the directors relieved of a duty or liability that the agreement gives to the shareholders` IF
    `the directors are relieved of the right, power, duty or liability within s 146(5)` `the right, power, duty or liability is one the agreement takes from the directors`

-- s 146(6). Nothing in section 146 prevents shareholders from fettering their discretion when exercising the powers of directors under a unanimous shareholder agreement.
@ref CBCA s 146(6)
@export May shareholders who exercise a director's powers under the agreement bind themselves in advance (s 146(6))?
GIVEN `the shareholders exercise the powers of directors under a unanimous shareholder agreement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the shareholders exercise the powers of directors under a unanimous shareholder agreement?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May shareholders who exercise a director's powers under the agreement bind themselves in advance` IF
    `shareholders may fetter their discretion within s 146(6)` `the shareholders exercise the powers of directors under a unanimous shareholder agreement`


§§ `What a proxy is and who is an intermediary (s 147)`

-- Only if you are giving, collecting or holding proxies, or holding shares for someone else.

-- s 147. "Form of proxy": a written or printed form that, on completion and execution (or, in Quebec, signing) by or on behalf of a shareholder, becomes a proxy.
@ref CBCA s 147 form of proxy
@export Is this document a form of proxy (s 147)?
GIVEN `it is a written or printed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a written or printed form?
      `on completion and execution, or in Quebec on signing, by or on behalf of a shareholder it becomes a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On completion and execution (or, in Quebec, signing) by or on behalf of a shareholder, does it become a proxy?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this document a form of proxy` IF
    `form of proxy within s 147` `it is a written or printed form` `on completion and execution, or in Quebec on signing, by or on behalf of a shareholder it becomes a proxy`

-- s 147. "Proxy": a completed and executed (or, in Quebec, signed) form of proxy by means of which a shareholder appoints a proxyholder to attend and act on the shareholder's behalf at a meeting.
@ref CBCA s 147 proxy
@export Is this completed form a proxy (s 147)?
GIVEN `it is a form of proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a form of proxy?
      `it is completed and executed, or in Quebec signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it completed and executed (or, in Quebec, signed)?
      `by means of it a shareholder appoints a proxyholder to attend and act on the shareholder's behalf at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appoint a proxyholder to attend and act on the shareholder's behalf at a meeting of shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this completed form a proxy` IF
    `proxy within s 147` `it is a form of proxy` `it is completed and executed, or in Quebec signed` `by means of it a shareholder appoints a proxyholder to attend and act on the shareholder's behalf at a meeting of shareholders`

-- s 147. "Intermediary": a person who holds a security on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder, and includes brokers and dealers, depositaries, financial institutions, clearing-agency participants, trustees of registered plans, nominees of those, and a person who carries out similar functions and holds a security registered in its name or its nominee's on behalf of another.
@ref CBCA s 147 intermediary
@export Is the person who holds my shares an intermediary (s 147)?
GIVEN `the person holds a security on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person who holds your shares hold a security on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder of it?
      `the person is a securities broker or dealer required to be registered to trade or deal in securities under the laws of any jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a securities broker or dealer required to be registered to trade or deal in securities under the laws of any jurisdiction?
      `the person is a securities depositary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a securities depositary?
      `the person is a financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a financial institution?
      `the person is a securities dealer, trust company, bank or other person on whose behalf a clearing agency or its nominees hold securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In respect of a clearing agency, is the person a securities dealer, trust company, bank or other person (including another clearing agency) on whose behalf the clearing agency or its nominees hold securities of an issuer?
      `the person is a trustee or administrator of a self-administered registered savings or investment plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a trustee or administrator of a self-administered retirement savings plan, retirement income fund, education savings plan or other similar self-administered savings or investment plan registered under the Income Tax Act?
      `the person is a nominee of a person referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (e)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a nominee of a person referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (e) of the definition of intermediary?
      `the person carries out functions similar to those of such individuals or entities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person carry out functions similar to those carried out by the individuals or entities in paragraphs (a) to (e) of the definition?
      `the person holds a security registered in their name or their nominee's name on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person hold a security registered in their name, or in the name of their nominee, on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder of the security?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the person who holds my shares an intermediary` IF
    `intermediary within s 147` `the person holds a security on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder` `the person is a securities broker or dealer required to be registered to trade or deal in securities under the laws of any jurisdiction` `the person is a securities depositary` `the person is a financial institution` `the person is a securities dealer, trust company, bank or other person on whose behalf a clearing agency or its nominees hold securities` `the person is a trustee or administrator of a self-administered registered savings or investment plan` `the person is a nominee of a person referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (e)` `the person carries out functions similar to those of such individuals or entities` `the person holds a security registered in their name or their nominee's name on behalf of another person who is not the registered holder`

-- s 147. "Solicit" or "solicitation" includes (i) a request for a proxy, (ii) a request to execute or not execute a form of proxy or to revoke a proxy, (iii) sending a form of proxy or other communication reasonably calculated to procure, withhold or revoke a proxy, and (iv) sending a form of proxy under section 149; but does not include the seven excluded acts.
-- The word "includes" opens the definition: an act in none of the lists is not decided (fork F-147-solicit).
@ref CBCA s 147 solicit
@export Is what I did a solicitation of proxies (s 147)?
GIVEN `it is a request for a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act a request for a proxy, whether or not accompanied by or included in a form of proxy?
      `it is a request to execute or not to execute, or to sign or not to sign, a form of proxy or to revoke a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a request to execute or not to execute (or, in Quebec, to sign or not to sign) a form of proxy, or to revoke a proxy?
      `it is the sending of a form of proxy or other communication to a shareholder under circumstances reasonably calculated to result in the procurement, withholding or revocation of a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the sending of a form of proxy or other communication to a shareholder under circumstances reasonably calculated to result in the procurement, withholding or revocation of a proxy?
      `it is the sending of a form of proxy to a shareholder under section 149` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the sending of a form of proxy to a shareholder under section 149?
      `it is the sending of a form of proxy in response to an unsolicited request made by or on behalf of a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the sending of a form of proxy in response to an unsolicited request made by or on behalf of a shareholder?
      `it is the performance of administrative acts or professional services on behalf of a person soliciting a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the performance of administrative acts or professional services on behalf of a person soliciting a proxy?
      `it is the sending by an intermediary of the documents referred to in section 153` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the sending by an intermediary of the documents referred to in section 153?
      `it is a solicitation by a person in respect of shares of which the person is the beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a solicitation by a person in respect of shares of which that person is the beneficial owner?
      `it is a public announcement, as prescribed, by a shareholder of how the shareholder intends to vote and the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a public announcement, as prescribed, by a shareholder of how the shareholder intends to vote and the reasons for that decision?
      `it is a communication for the purposes of obtaining the number of shares required for a shareholder proposal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a communication for the purposes of obtaining the number of shares required for a shareholder proposal under subsection 137(1.1)?
      `it is a communication, other than a solicitation by or on behalf of the management, made in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a communication, other than a solicitation by or on behalf of the management of the corporation, made to shareholders in circumstances that may be prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I did a solicitation of proxies` IS
    `solicitation within s 147`
        (`act within the inclusions of solicit within s 147`
            `it is a request for a proxy`
            `it is a request to execute or not to execute, or to sign or not to sign, a form of proxy or to revoke a proxy`
            `it is the sending of a form of proxy or other communication to a shareholder under circumstances reasonably calculated to result in the procurement, withholding or revocation of a proxy`
            `it is the sending of a form of proxy to a shareholder under section 149`)
        (`act within the exclusions of solicit within s 147`
            `it is the sending of a form of proxy in response to an unsolicited request made by or on behalf of a shareholder`
            `it is the performance of administrative acts or professional services on behalf of a person soliciting a proxy`
            `it is the sending by an intermediary of the documents referred to in section 153`
            `it is a solicitation by a person in respect of shares of which the person is the beneficial owner`
            `it is a public announcement, as prescribed, by a shareholder of how the shareholder intends to vote and the reasons`
            `it is a communication for the purposes of obtaining the number of shares required for a shareholder proposal`
            `it is a communication, other than a solicitation by or on behalf of the management, made in prescribed circumstances`)

-- s 147. "Solicitation by or on behalf of the management of a corporation": a solicitation by any person pursuant to a resolution or instructions of, or with the acquiescence of, the directors or a committee of the directors.
@ref CBCA s 147 solicitation by management
@export Is this a solicitation by or on behalf of the management (s 147)?
GIVEN `it is a solicitation by any person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a solicitation by any person?
      `it is pursuant to a resolution or instructions of the directors or a committee of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it pursuant to a resolution or instructions of the directors or a committee of the directors?
      `it is with the acquiescence of the directors or a committee of the directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it with the acquiescence of the directors or a committee of the directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a solicitation by or on behalf of the management` IF
    `solicitation by or on behalf of the management of a corporation within s 147` `it is a solicitation by any person` `it is pursuant to a resolution or instructions of the directors or a committee of the directors` `it is with the acquiescence of the directors or a committee of the directors`


§§ `Appointing, executing and revoking a proxy (s 148)`

-- Only if you are a shareholder who wants to vote by proxy, or a corporation receiving proxies.

-- s 148(1). A shareholder entitled to vote at a meeting may by means of a proxy appoint a proxyholder, or one or more alternate proxyholders, who are not required to be shareholders, to attend and act at the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 148(1)
@export May I appoint a proxyholder to vote for me (s 148(1))?
GIVEN `I am a shareholder entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder entitled to vote at the meeting?
      `the appointment is by means of a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you make the appointment by means of a proxy?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I appoint a proxyholder to vote for me` IF
    `a shareholder may appoint a proxyholder within s 148(1)` `I am a shareholder entitled to vote at the meeting` `the appointment is by means of a proxy`

-- s 148(2). A proxy shall be executed or, in Quebec, signed by the shareholder or by the shareholder's personal representative authorized in writing.
@ref CBCA s 148(2)
@export Is my proxy properly executed (s 148(2))?
GIVEN `the proxy is executed or, in Quebec, signed by the shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proxy executed (or, in Quebec, signed) by the shareholder?
      `the proxy is executed or, in Quebec, signed by the shareholder's personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proxy executed (or, in Quebec, signed) by the shareholder's personal representative?
      `that personal representative is authorized in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that personal representative authorized in writing?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my proxy properly executed` IF
    `the proxy is executed as s 148(2) requires within s 148(2)` `the proxy is executed or, in Quebec, signed by the shareholder` `the proxy is executed or, in Quebec, signed by the shareholder's personal representative` `that personal representative is authorized in writing`

-- s 148(3). A proxy is valid only at the meeting in respect of which it is given or any adjournment of it.
@ref CBCA s 148(3)
@export Is my proxy valid at this meeting (s 148(3))?
GIVEN `the meeting is the meeting in respect of which the proxy is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the meeting in respect of which the proxy was given?
      `the meeting is an adjournment of the meeting in respect of which the proxy is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this an adjournment of the meeting in respect of which the proxy was given?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my proxy valid at this meeting` IF
    `the proxy is valid at the meeting within s 148(3)` `the meeting is the meeting in respect of which the proxy is given` `the meeting is an adjournment of the meeting in respect of which the proxy is given`

-- s 148(4). A shareholder may revoke a proxy by depositing an instrument or act in writing executed (or signed) by the shareholder or the shareholder's authorized personal representative at the registered office up to and including the last business day preceding the day of the meeting, or with the chairman of the meeting on the day, or in any other manner permitted by law.
@ref CBCA s 148(4)
@export Have I revoked my proxy (s 148(4))?
GIVEN `I executed or signed a written instrument or act revoking the proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you (or your authorized personal representative) execute or sign an instrument or act in writing revoking the proxy?
      `I deposited the instrument at the registered office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deposit the instrument at the registered office of the corporation?
      `the date I deposited the instrument` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you deposit it?
      `the last business day preceding the day of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc What is the last business day preceding the day of the meeting, or of the adjournment at which the proxy is to be used?
      `I deposited the instrument with the chairman of the meeting on the day of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you deposit the instrument with the chairman of the meeting on the day of the meeting or of an adjournment of it?
      `I revoked the proxy in any other manner permitted by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you revoke the proxy in any other manner permitted by law?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I revoked my proxy` IF
    `the proxy is revoked within s 148(4)` `I executed or signed a written instrument or act revoking the proxy` (IF `I deposited the instrument at the registered office of the corporation` THEN JUST `the date I deposited the instrument` ELSE NOTHING) `the last business day preceding the day of the meeting` `I deposited the instrument with the chairman of the meeting on the day of the meeting` `I revoked the proxy in any other manner permitted by law`

-- s 148(5). The directors may specify in the notice calling a meeting a time not more than 48 hours, excluding Saturdays and holidays, before the meeting or adjournment before which proxies must be deposited with the corporation or its agent.
@ref CBCA s 148(5)
@export May the directors set a deadline for depositing proxies (s 148(5))?
GIVEN `the time is specified in a notice calling the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the time specified in a notice calling the meeting?
      `the hours, excluding Saturdays and holidays, before the meeting or adjournment at which the time falls` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours, excluding Saturdays and holidays, before the meeting or adjournment does the time fall?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors set a deadline for depositing proxies` IF
    `the directors may specify the time for depositing proxies within s 148(5)` `the time is specified in a notice calling the meeting` `the hours, excluding Saturdays and holidays, before the meeting or adjournment at which the time falls`


§§ `Management's duty to send a form of proxy (s 149)`

-- Directors ask whether the corporation must send a form of proxy; shareholders ask whether they are owed one.

-- s 149(2). The management is not required to send a form of proxy if the corporation is not a distributing corporation and has fifty or fewer shareholders entitled to vote at a meeting, two or more joint holders being counted as one.
@ref CBCA s 149(2)
@export Is the corporation excused from sending me a form of proxy (s 149(2))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `the number of shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting, joint holders counted as one` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shareholders are entitled to vote at the meeting (two or more joint holders counted as one)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation excused from sending me a form of proxy` IF
    `management is not required to send a form of proxy within s 149(2)` `the corporation is a distributing corporation` `the number of shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting, joint holders counted as one`

-- s 149(1). Subject to (2), the management of a corporation shall, concurrently with giving notice of a meeting, send a form of proxy in prescribed form to each shareholder entitled to receive notice of the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 149(1)
@export Must management send me a form of proxy with the notice of the meeting (s 149(1))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `the number of shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting, joint holders counted as one` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shareholders are entitled to vote at the meeting (two or more joint holders counted as one)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must management send me a form of proxy with the notice of the meeting` IF
    `management must send a form of proxy within s 149(1)`
        (`management is not required to send a form of proxy within s 149(2)`
            `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
            `the number of shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting, joint holders counted as one`)

-- s 149(1). The duty is met by sending, concurrently with the notice (the same day), a form of proxy in the prescribed form to each shareholder entitled to receive notice.
@ref CBCA s 149(1)
@export Did management send the form of proxy as the Act requires (s 149(1))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `the number of shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting, joint holders counted as one` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shareholders are entitled to vote at the meeting (two or more joint holders counted as one)?
      `the date the notice of the meeting was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of the meeting given?
      `the date the form of proxy was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the form of proxy sent?
      `the form of proxy is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the form of proxy in the form the regulations prescribe?
      `the form of proxy was sent to each shareholder who is entitled to receive notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent to each shareholder who is entitled to receive notice of the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did management send the form of proxy as the Act requires` IF
    `the duty to send a form of proxy is met within s 149(1)`
        (`management must send a form of proxy within s 149(1)`
            (`management is not required to send a form of proxy within s 149(2)`
                `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
                `the number of shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting, joint holders counted as one`))
        `the date the notice of the meeting was given`
        `the date the form of proxy was sent`
        `the form of proxy is in the prescribed form`
        `the form of proxy was sent to each shareholder who is entitled to receive notice of the meeting`

-- s 149(3). If the management of a corporation fails to comply, without reasonable cause, with subsection (1), the corporation is guilty of an offence.
@ref CBCA s 149(3)
@export Is the corporation guilty of an offence for not sending me a form of proxy (s 149(3))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `the number of shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting, joint holders counted as one` IS A NUMBER @desc How many shareholders are entitled to vote at the meeting (two or more joint holders counted as one)?
      `the management failed to comply with subsection 149(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did management fail to comply with subsection 149(1)?
      `the failure was without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the failure without reasonable cause?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation guilty of an offence for not sending me a form of proxy` IF
    `the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 149(3)`
        (`management must send a form of proxy within s 149(1)`
            (`management is not required to send a form of proxy within s 149(2)`
                `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
                `the number of shareholders entitled to vote at the meeting, joint holders counted as one`))
        `the management failed to comply with subsection 149(1)`
        `the failure was without reasonable cause`

-- s 149(3). The corporation is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars; the ceiling is not the sentence.
@ref CBCA s 149(3) fine
@export What is the most the corporation can be fined for that (s 149(3))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the corporation can be fined for that` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 149(3)`)'s `maximum fine in dollars`

-- s 149(4). Where a corporation commits an offence under (3), any director or officer who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in it is a party to and guilty of the offence.
@ref CBCA s 149(4)
@export Am I guilty of the corporation's offence under s 149(3) as a director or officer (s 149(4))?
GIVEN `the corporation commits an offence under subsection 149(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation commit an offence under subsection 149(3)?
      `I am a director or officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of the corporation?
      `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly authorize, permit or acquiesce in the commission of the offence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of the corporation's offence under s 149(3) as a director or officer` IF
    `a director or officer is a party to and guilty of the offence within s 149(4)` `the corporation commits an offence under subsection 149(3)` `I am a director or officer of the corporation` `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence`

-- s 149(4). Liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both; the ceiling is not the sentence.
@ref CBCA s 149(4) fine
@export What is the most I can be fined as a director or officer under s 149(4)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined as a director or officer under s 149(4)` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 149(4)`)'s `maximum fine in dollars`

-- s 149(4). The same offence: imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months; the ceiling is not the sentence.
@ref CBCA s 149(4) imprisonment
@export What is the longest imprisonment I can face as a director or officer under s 149(4), in months?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment I can face as a director or officer under s 149(4), in months` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 149(4)`)'s `maximum imprisonment in months`

-- s 149(3). The text states no imprisonment for the corporation's offence (a fine only); the answer is "none stated".
@ref CBCA s 149(3) imprisonment
@export What is the longest imprisonment the corporation faces under s 149(3), in months?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment the corporation faces under s 149(3), in months` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 149(3)`)'s `maximum imprisonment in months`


§§ `Circulars when soliciting proxies (ss 150 and 151)`

-- Only if you, or the corporation, are soliciting proxies.

-- s 150(1). A person shall not solicit proxies unless a management proxy circular (for a management solicitation) or a dissident's proxy circular (for any other) in prescribed form is sent to the auditor, to each shareholder whose proxy is solicited, to each director and, for a dissident's circular, to the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 150(1)
@export Have I sent the circular the Act requires before soliciting proxies (s 150(1))?
GIVEN `the solicitation is by or on behalf of the management of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the solicitation by or on behalf of the management of the corporation?
      `a management proxy circular in prescribed form is sent, as an appendix to or a separate document accompanying the notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a management proxy circular in the prescribed form sent, as an appendix to or a separate document accompanying the notice of the meeting?
      `a dissident's proxy circular in prescribed form stating the purposes of the solicitation is sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a dissident's proxy circular in the prescribed form, stating the purposes of the solicitation, sent?
      `the circular is sent to the auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the circular sent to the auditor of the corporation?
      `the circular is sent to each shareholder whose proxy is solicited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it sent to each shareholder whose proxy is solicited?
      `the circular is sent to each director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it sent to each director?
      `the circular is sent to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it sent to the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I sent the circular the Act requires before soliciting proxies` IF
    `the circular required by s 150(1) is sent within s 150(1)` `the solicitation is by or on behalf of the management of the corporation` `a management proxy circular in prescribed form is sent, as an appendix to or a separate document accompanying the notice of the meeting` `a dissident's proxy circular in prescribed form stating the purposes of the solicitation is sent` `the circular is sent to the auditor of the corporation` `the circular is sent to each shareholder whose proxy is solicited` `the circular is sent to each director` `the circular is sent to the corporation`

-- s 150(1), (1.1), (1.2). A person may solicit proxies if the required circular is sent; a person other than management may solicit without a dissident's circular if the proxies of fifteen or fewer shareholders are solicited, or if the solicitation is conveyed by public broadcast, speech or publication in the prescribed circumstances.
@ref CBCA s 150(1), (1.1), (1.2)
@export May I solicit proxies (s 150(1), (1.1) and (1.2))?
GIVEN `the solicitation is by or on behalf of the management of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the solicitation by or on behalf of the management of the corporation?
      `a management proxy circular in prescribed form is sent, as an appendix to or a separate document accompanying the notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a management proxy circular in the prescribed form sent, as an appendix to or a separate document accompanying the notice of the meeting?
      `a dissident's proxy circular in prescribed form stating the purposes of the solicitation is sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a dissident's proxy circular in the prescribed form, stating the purposes of the solicitation, sent?
      `the circular is sent to the auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the circular sent to the auditor of the corporation?
      `the circular is sent to each shareholder whose proxy is solicited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it sent to each shareholder whose proxy is solicited?
      `the circular is sent to each director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it sent to each director?
      `the circular is sent to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it sent to the corporation?
      `the total number of shareholders whose proxies are solicited, joint holders counted as one` IS A NUMBER @desc To how many shareholders in all are you soliciting proxies (two or more joint holders counted as one)?
      `the solicitation is conveyed by public broadcast, speech or publication in the prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the solicitation conveyed by public broadcast, speech or publication in the prescribed circumstances?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I solicit proxies` IF
    `a person may solicit proxies within s 150(1), (1.1) and (1.2)`
        `the solicitation is by or on behalf of the management of the corporation`
        (`the circular required by s 150(1) is sent within s 150(1)`
            `the solicitation is by or on behalf of the management of the corporation`
            `a management proxy circular in prescribed form is sent, as an appendix to or a separate document accompanying the notice of the meeting`
            `a dissident's proxy circular in prescribed form stating the purposes of the solicitation is sent`
            `the circular is sent to the auditor of the corporation`
            `the circular is sent to each shareholder whose proxy is solicited`
            `the circular is sent to each director`
            `the circular is sent to the corporation`)
        `the total number of shareholders whose proxies are solicited, joint holders counted as one`
        `the solicitation is conveyed by public broadcast, speech or publication in the prescribed circumstances`

-- s 150(2). A person required to send a management or dissident's proxy circular shall send concurrently a copy of it to the Director, together with a statement in prescribed form, the form of proxy, any other documents for use in connection with the meeting and, for a management proxy circular, a copy of the notice of meeting.
@ref CBCA s 150(2)
@export Have I sent the Director the copy the Act requires (s 150(2))?
GIVEN `I am required to send a management proxy circular or dissident's proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required to send a management proxy circular or a dissident's proxy circular?
      `the circular is a management proxy circular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the circular a management proxy circular?
      `the date the circular was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the circular sent?
      `the date the copy was sent to the Director` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the copy sent to the Director?
      `the copy is sent with a statement in prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the copy sent with a statement in the prescribed form?
      `the copy is sent with the form of proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent with the form of proxy?
      `the copy is sent with any other documents for use in connection with the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent with any other documents for use in connection with the meeting?
      `the copy is sent with a copy of the notice of meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it sent with a copy of the notice of meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I sent the Director the copy the Act requires` IF
    `the copy to the Director complies with s 150(2)` `I am required to send a management proxy circular or dissident's proxy circular` `the circular is a management proxy circular` `the date the circular was sent` `the date the copy was sent to the Director` `the copy is sent with a statement in prescribed form` `the copy is sent with the form of proxy` `the copy is sent with any other documents for use in connection with the meeting` `the copy is sent with a copy of the notice of meeting`

-- s 150(3). A person who fails to comply with subsections (1) and (2) is guilty of an offence.
@ref CBCA s 150(3)
@export Am I guilty of an offence for soliciting proxies without the circulars (s 150(3))?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with subsection 150(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with subsection 150(1)?
      `I failed to comply with subsection 150(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with subsection 150(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence for soliciting proxies without the circulars` IF
    `a person is guilty of an offence within s 150(3)` `I failed to comply with subsection 150(1)` `I failed to comply with subsection 150(2)`

-- s 150(3). Fine not exceeding five thousand dollars, or imprisonment not exceeding six months, or both; the ceiling is not the sentence.
@ref CBCA s 150(3) fine
@export What is the most I can be fined under s 150(3)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined under s 150(3)` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 150(3)`)'s `maximum fine in dollars`

-- s 150(3). Imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months; the ceiling is not the sentence.
@ref CBCA s 150(3) imprisonment
@export What is the longest imprisonment I can face under s 150(3), in months?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment I can face under s 150(3), in months` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 150(3)`)'s `maximum imprisonment in months`

-- s 150(4). Where a body corporate commits an offence under (3), any director or officer who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in it is a party to and guilty of the offence.
@ref CBCA s 150(4)
@export Am I guilty of my company's offence under s 150(3) as a director or officer (s 150(4))?
GIVEN `the body corporate commits an offence under subsection 150(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the body corporate commit an offence under subsection 150(3)?
      `I am a director or officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or officer of the body corporate?
      `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly authorize, permit or acquiesce in the commission of the offence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of my company's offence under s 150(3) as a director or officer` IF
    `a director or officer of a body corporate is a party to and guilty of the offence within s 150(4)` `the body corporate commits an offence under subsection 150(3)` `I am a director or officer of the body corporate` `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence`

-- s 150(4). Fine not exceeding five thousand dollars, or imprisonment not exceeding six months, or both.
@ref CBCA s 150(4) fine
@export What is the most I can be fined as a director or officer under s 150(4)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined as a director or officer under s 150(4)` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 150(4)`)'s `maximum fine in dollars`

-- s 150(4). Imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months.
@ref CBCA s 150(4) imprisonment
@export What is the longest imprisonment I can face as a director or officer under s 150(4), in months?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment I can face as a director or officer under s 150(4), in months` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 150(4)`)'s `maximum imprisonment in months`

-- s 151(1). On the application of an interested person, the Director may exempt the person, on any terms the Director thinks fit, from any of the requirements of section 149 or subsection 150(1) or 153(1).
@ref CBCA s 151(1)
@export May I ask the Director to exempt me from the proxy requirements (s 151(1))?
GIVEN `I am an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an interested person?
      `the requirement is a requirement of section 149, subsection 150(1) or subsection 153(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement one of section 149, subsection 150(1) or subsection 153(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the Director to exempt me from the proxy requirements` IF
    `the Director may exempt the person within s 151(1)` `I am an interested person` `the requirement is a requirement of section 149, subsection 150(1) or subsection 153(1)`

-- s 151(1). The exemption may have retroactive effect.
@ref CBCA s 151(1)
@export May the Director's exemption have retroactive effect (s 151(1))?
GIVEN `the Director has granted an exemption under subsection 151(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director granted an exemption under subsection 151(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director's exemption have retroactive effect` IF
    `the exemption may have retroactive effect within s 151(1)` `the Director has granted an exemption under subsection 151(1)`


§§ `Acting as a proxyholder (s 152)`

-- Only if you have been appointed proxyholder for a shareholder.

-- s 152(1). A person who solicits a proxy and is appointed proxyholder shall attend in person or cause an alternate proxyholder to attend the meeting and comply with the directions of the shareholder who appointed them.
@ref CBCA s 152(1)
@export Must I attend the meeting and follow the shareholder's directions as proxyholder (s 152(1))?
GIVEN `I solicit a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you solicit the proxy?
      `I am appointed proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you appointed proxyholder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I attend the meeting and follow the shareholder's directions as proxyholder` IF
    `the proxyholder must attend and comply with the directions within s 152(1)` `I solicit a proxy` `I am appointed proxyholder`

-- s 152(1). The duty is met by attending in person or causing an alternate proxyholder to attend, and complying with the shareholder's directions.
@ref CBCA s 152(1)
@export Have I done what s 152(1) requires of me as proxyholder?
GIVEN `I solicit a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you solicit the proxy?
      `I am appointed proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you appointed proxyholder?
      `I attend the meeting in person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you attend the meeting in person?
      `I cause an alternate proxyholder to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cause an alternate proxyholder to attend the meeting?
      `I comply with the directions of the shareholder who appointed me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you comply with the directions of the shareholder who appointed you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I done what s 152(1) requires of me as proxyholder` IF
    `the duty to attend and comply with the directions is met within s 152(1)`
        (`the proxyholder must attend and comply with the directions within s 152(1)`
            `I solicit a proxy`
            `I am appointed proxyholder`)
        `I attend the meeting in person`
        `I cause an alternate proxyholder to attend the meeting`
        `I comply with the directions of the shareholder who appointed me`

-- s 152(2). A proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder has the same rights as the shareholder who appointed them to speak at a meeting in respect of any matter.
@ref CBCA s 152(2)
@export May I speak at the meeting as proxyholder (s 152(2))?
GIVEN `I am a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I speak at the meeting as proxyholder` IF
    `a proxyholder has the shareholder's right to speak within s 152(2)` `I am a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder`

-- s 152(2). A proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder has the same right as the shareholder to vote by way of ballot.
@ref CBCA s 152(2)
@export May I vote by ballot as proxyholder (s 152(2))?
GIVEN `I am a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I vote by ballot as proxyholder` IF
    `a proxyholder has the shareholder's right to vote by ballot within s 152(2)` `I am a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder`

-- s 152(2). A proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder has the same right as the shareholder to vote by a show of hands, except where they have conflicting instructions from more than one shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 152(2)
@export May I vote by show of hands as proxyholder (s 152(2))?
GIVEN `I am a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder?
      `I have conflicting instructions from more than one shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have conflicting instructions from more than one shareholder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I vote by show of hands as proxyholder` IF
    `a proxyholder has the shareholder's right to vote by a show of hands within s 152(2)` `I am a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder` `I have conflicting instructions from more than one shareholder`

-- s 152(3)(a). If the chairperson declares that the votes attached to shares represented by proxy and required to be voted against what will be the decision of the meeting are less than five per cent of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot, then unless a shareholder or proxyholder demands a ballot, the chairperson may conduct the vote by a show of hands.
@ref CBCA s 152(3)(a)
@export May the chairperson take the vote by show of hands despite the proxies (s 152(3)(a))?
GIVEN `the chairperson declares that the votes attached to shares represented by proxy and required to be voted against the decision are less than five per cent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the chairperson declared that the votes attached to shares represented at the meeting by proxy and required to be voted against what will be the decision of the meeting are less than five per cent of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot?
      `the fraction of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot attached to proxy shares required to be voted against the decision` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot is attached to shares represented by proxy and required to be voted against what will be the decision of the meeting (as a number between 0 and 1)?
      `a shareholder or proxyholder demands a ballot` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a shareholder or proxyholder demand a ballot?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the chairperson take the vote by show of hands despite the proxies` IF
    `the chairperson may conduct the vote by a show of hands within s 152(3)(a)` `the chairperson declares that the votes attached to shares represented by proxy and required to be voted against the decision are less than five per cent` `the fraction of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot attached to proxy shares required to be voted against the decision` `a shareholder or proxyholder demands a ballot`

-- s 152(3)(b). In that case a proxyholder or alternate proxyholder may vote in respect of that matter by a show of hands.
@ref CBCA s 152(3)(b)
@export May I, as proxyholder, vote by show of hands when the chairperson allows it (s 152(3)(b))?
GIVEN `the chairperson declares that the votes attached to shares represented by proxy and required to be voted against the decision are less than five per cent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the chairperson declared that the votes attached to shares represented at the meeting by proxy and required to be voted against what will be the decision of the meeting are less than five per cent of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot?
      `the fraction of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot attached to proxy shares required to be voted against the decision` IS A NUMBER @desc What fraction of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot is attached to shares represented by proxy and required to be voted against what will be the decision of the meeting (as a number between 0 and 1)?
      `a shareholder or proxyholder demands a ballot` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a shareholder or proxyholder demand a ballot?
      `I am a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as proxyholder, vote by show of hands when the chairperson allows it` IF
    `a proxyholder may vote by a show of hands within s 152(3)(b)`
        (`the chairperson may conduct the vote by a show of hands within s 152(3)(a)`
            `the chairperson declares that the votes attached to shares represented by proxy and required to be voted against the decision are less than five per cent`
            `the fraction of all the votes that might be cast on the ballot attached to proxy shares required to be voted against the decision`
            `a shareholder or proxyholder demands a ballot`)
        `I am a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder`

-- s 152(4). A proxyholder or alternate proxyholder who without reasonable cause fails to comply with the directions of a shareholder under this section is guilty of an offence.
@ref CBCA s 152(4)
@export Am I guilty of an offence for not following the shareholder's directions as proxyholder (s 152(4))?
GIVEN `I am a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder?
      `I failed to comply with the directions of a shareholder under s 152` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with the directions of a shareholder under section 152?
      `the failure was without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the failure without reasonable cause?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence for not following the shareholder's directions as proxyholder` IF
    `a proxyholder is guilty of an offence within s 152(4)` `I am a proxyholder or an alternate proxyholder` `I failed to comply with the directions of a shareholder under s 152` `the failure was without reasonable cause`

-- s 152(4). Fine not exceeding five thousand dollars, or imprisonment not exceeding six months, or both.
@ref CBCA s 152(4) fine
@export What is the most I can be fined as a proxyholder under s 152(4)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined as a proxyholder under s 152(4)` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 152(4)`)'s `maximum fine in dollars`

-- s 152(4). Imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months.
@ref CBCA s 152(4) imprisonment
@export What is the longest imprisonment I can face as a proxyholder under s 152(4), in months?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment I can face as a proxyholder under s 152(4), in months` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 152(4)`)'s `maximum imprisonment in months`


§§ `Shares held by an intermediary (s 153)`

-- Only if your shares are registered in the name of a broker, bank or other intermediary, or you solicit proxies from such holders.

-- s 153(1). Shares registered in the name of an intermediary or its nominee and not beneficially owned by the intermediary must not be voted unless the intermediary, without delay after receipt, sends a copy of the meeting documents to the beneficial owner and, except when it has received written voting instructions, a written request for instructions.
@ref CBCA s 153(1)
@export May my intermediary vote my shares (s 153(1))?
GIVEN `the shares are registered in the name of an intermediary or its nominee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares registered in the name of an intermediary or its nominee?
      `the shares are not beneficially owned by the intermediary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares not beneficially owned by the intermediary?
      `the intermediary sent a copy of each document to the beneficial owner without delay after receiving it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the intermediary, without delay after receiving each document, send a copy of it to the beneficial owner?
      `the intermediary has received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the intermediary received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner?
      `the intermediary sent the beneficial owner a written request for voting instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the intermediary send the beneficial owner a written request for voting instructions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my intermediary vote my shares` IF
    `the shares may be voted within s 153(1)`
        (`the shares must not be voted unless s 153(1) is met within s 153(1)`
            `the shares are registered in the name of an intermediary or its nominee`
            `the shares are not beneficially owned by the intermediary`)
        `the intermediary sent a copy of each document to the beneficial owner without delay after receiving it`
        `the intermediary has received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner`
        `the intermediary sent the beneficial owner a written request for voting instructions`

-- s 153(2). An intermediary, or a proxyholder appointed by an intermediary, may not vote shares that the intermediary does not beneficially own and that are registered in its name or its nominee's name unless it receives written voting instructions from the beneficial owner.
@ref CBCA s 153(2)
@export Is my intermediary barred from voting my shares without my written instructions (s 153(2))?
GIVEN `the shares are not beneficially owned by the intermediary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares not beneficially owned by the intermediary?
      `the shares are registered in the name of the intermediary or in the name of a nominee of the intermediary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares registered in the name of the intermediary or of a nominee of the intermediary?
      `the intermediary or its proxyholder receives written voting instructions from the beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the intermediary or its proxyholder received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my intermediary barred from voting my shares without my written instructions` IF
    `voting is prohibited within s 153(2)` `the shares are not beneficially owned by the intermediary` `the shares are registered in the name of the intermediary or in the name of a nominee of the intermediary` `the intermediary or its proxyholder receives written voting instructions from the beneficial owner`

-- s 153(3). A person by or on behalf of whom a solicitation is made shall provide, at the request of an intermediary, without delay, at the person's expense, the necessary number of copies of the documents referred to in (1), other than copies of the document requesting voting instructions.
@ref CBCA s 153(3)
@export Must I give an intermediary copies of my solicitation documents (s 153(3))?
GIVEN `a solicitation is made by or on behalf of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a solicitation made by or on your behalf?
      `an intermediary requests copies of the documents referred to in subsection 153(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an intermediary requested copies of the documents referred to in subsection 153(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give an intermediary copies of my solicitation documents` IF
    `the person must provide copies to the intermediary within s 153(3)` `a solicitation is made by or on behalf of me` `an intermediary requests copies of the documents referred to in subsection 153(1)`

-- s 153(3). The duty is met by providing the necessary copies without delay and at the person's expense.
@ref CBCA s 153(3)
@export Have I done what s 153(3) requires about copies?
GIVEN `a solicitation is made by or on behalf of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a solicitation made by or on your behalf?
      `an intermediary requests copies of the documents referred to in subsection 153(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an intermediary requested copies of the documents referred to in subsection 153(1)?
      `I provide the necessary number of copies without delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide the necessary number of copies without delay?
      `I provide them at my expense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you provide them at your own expense?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I done what s 153(3) requires about copies` IF
    `the duty to provide copies is met within s 153(3)`
        (`the person must provide copies to the intermediary within s 153(3)`
            `a solicitation is made by or on behalf of me`
            `an intermediary requests copies of the documents referred to in subsection 153(1)`)
        `I provide the necessary number of copies without delay`
        `I provide them at my expense`

-- s 153(4). An intermediary shall vote or appoint a proxyholder to vote any shares referred to in (1) in accordance with any written voting instructions received from the beneficial owner.
@ref CBCA s 153(4)
@export Must my intermediary vote my shares as I instructed (s 153(4))?
GIVEN `the shares are shares referred to in subsection 153(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares shares referred to in subsection 153(1) (registered in the name of an intermediary and not beneficially owned by it)?
      `the intermediary has received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the intermediary received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my intermediary vote my shares as I instructed` IF
    `the intermediary must vote in accordance with the instructions within s 153(4)` `the shares are shares referred to in subsection 153(1)` `the intermediary has received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner`

-- s 153(4). The duty is met by voting the shares, or appointing a proxyholder to vote them, in accordance with the instructions.
@ref CBCA s 153(4)
@export Has my intermediary done what s 153(4) requires?
GIVEN `the shares are shares referred to in subsection 153(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the shares shares referred to in subsection 153(1) (registered in the name of an intermediary and not beneficially owned by it)?
      `the intermediary has received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the intermediary received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner?
      `the intermediary votes the shares in accordance with the instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the intermediary vote the shares in accordance with the instructions?
      `the intermediary appoints a proxyholder to vote the shares in accordance with the instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the intermediary appoint a proxyholder to vote the shares in accordance with the instructions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my intermediary done what s 153(4) requires` IF
    `the duty to vote in accordance with the instructions is met within s 153(4)`
        (`the intermediary must vote in accordance with the instructions within s 153(4)`
            `the shares are shares referred to in subsection 153(1)`
            `the intermediary has received written voting instructions from the beneficial owner`)
        `the intermediary votes the shares in accordance with the instructions`
        `the intermediary appoints a proxyholder to vote the shares in accordance with the instructions`

-- s 153(5). If a beneficial owner so requests and provides the intermediary with appropriate documentation, the intermediary must appoint the beneficial owner or a nominee of the beneficial owner as proxyholder.
@ref CBCA s 153(5)
@export Must my intermediary appoint me or my nominee as proxyholder if I ask (s 153(5))?
GIVEN `I request that I or my nominee be appointed proxyholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you requested that you, or a nominee of yours, be appointed proxyholder?
      `I provide the intermediary with appropriate documentation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided the intermediary with appropriate documentation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my intermediary appoint me or my nominee as proxyholder if I ask` IF
    `the intermediary must appoint the beneficial owner or a nominee as proxyholder within s 153(5)` `I request that I or my nominee be appointed proxyholder` `I provide the intermediary with appropriate documentation`

-- s 153(6). The failure of an intermediary to comply with this section does not render void any meeting of shareholders or any action taken at the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 153(6)
@export Does my intermediary's failure make the meeting or its decisions void (s 153(6))?
GIVEN `an intermediary failed to comply with section 153` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did an intermediary fail to comply with section 153?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my intermediary's failure make the meeting or its decisions void` IF
    `the failure renders a meeting or an action void within s 153(6)` `an intermediary failed to comply with section 153`

-- s 153(7). Nothing in this section gives an intermediary the right to vote shares that it is otherwise prohibited from voting.
@ref CBCA s 153(7)
@export Does section 153 give my intermediary the right to vote shares it is otherwise barred from voting (s 153(7))?
GIVEN `the intermediary is otherwise prohibited from voting the shares` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the intermediary otherwise prohibited from voting the shares?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 153 give my intermediary the right to vote shares it is otherwise barred from voting` IS
    `s 153 gives the intermediary the right to vote within s 153(7)` `the intermediary is otherwise prohibited from voting the shares`

-- s 153(8). An intermediary who knowingly fails to comply with section 153 is guilty of an offence.
@ref CBCA s 153(8)
@export Is my intermediary guilty of an offence for not complying with section 153 (s 153(8))?
GIVEN `the person is an intermediary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an intermediary?
      `the intermediary failed to comply with section 153` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the intermediary fail to comply with section 153?
      `the intermediary knew that it failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the intermediary know that it failed to comply?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my intermediary guilty of an offence for not complying with section 153` IF
    `an intermediary is guilty of an offence within s 153(8)` `the person is an intermediary` `the intermediary failed to comply with section 153` `the intermediary knew that it failed to comply`

-- s 153(8). Fine not exceeding five thousand dollars, or imprisonment not exceeding six months, or both.
@ref CBCA s 153(8) fine
@export What is the most my intermediary can be fined under s 153(8)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most my intermediary can be fined under s 153(8)` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 153(8)`)'s `maximum fine in dollars`

-- s 153(8). Imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months.
@ref CBCA s 153(8) imprisonment
@export What is the longest imprisonment my intermediary can face under s 153(8), in months?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment my intermediary can face under s 153(8), in months` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 153(8)`)'s `maximum imprisonment in months`

-- s 153(9). If an intermediary that is a body corporate commits an offence under (8), any director or officer who knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in it is a party to and guilty of the offence.
@ref CBCA s 153(9)
@export Am I guilty of my company's offence as a director or officer of an intermediary (s 153(9))?
GIVEN `the intermediary is a body corporate and commits an offence under subsection 153(8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the intermediary a body corporate that commits an offence under subsection 153(8)?
      `I am a director or officer of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or officer of the body corporate?
      `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you knowingly authorize, permit or acquiesce in the commission of the offence?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of my company's offence as a director or officer of an intermediary` IF
    `a director or officer of an intermediary is a party to and guilty of the offence within s 153(9)` `the intermediary is a body corporate and commits an offence under subsection 153(8)` `I am a director or officer of the body corporate` `I knowingly authorized, permitted or acquiesced in the commission of the offence`

-- s 153(9). Fine not exceeding five thousand dollars, or imprisonment not exceeding six months, or both.
@ref CBCA s 153(9) fine
@export What is the most I can be fined as a director or officer of an intermediary under s 153(9)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined as a director or officer of an intermediary under s 153(9)` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 153(9)`)'s `maximum fine in dollars`

-- s 153(9). Imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months.
@ref CBCA s 153(9) imprisonment
@export What is the longest imprisonment I can face as a director or officer of an intermediary under s 153(9), in months?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment I can face as a director or officer of an intermediary under s 153(9), in months` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 153(9)`)'s `maximum imprisonment in months`


§§ `Misleading proxy documents: asking the court (s 154)`

-- Only if a form of proxy, management proxy circular or dissident's proxy circular says something untrue or leaves out something material.

-- s 154(1). If a form of proxy, management proxy circular or dissident's proxy circular contains an untrue statement of a material fact or omits to state a material fact required or necessary to make a statement not misleading, an interested person or the Director may apply to a court.
@ref CBCA s 154(1)
@export May I ask the court to act because a proxy circular is misleading (s 154(1))?
GIVEN `the document contains an untrue statement of a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the form of proxy or circular contain an untrue statement of a material fact?
      `the document omits to state a material fact required in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it omit to state a material fact required in it?
      `the document omits to state a material fact necessary to make a statement in it not misleading in the light of the circumstances in which it was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it omit to state a material fact necessary to make a statement in it not misleading in the light of the circumstances in which it was made?
      `the applicant is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an interested person?
      `the applicant is the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Director appointed under the Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the court to act because a proxy circular is misleading` IF
    `a person may apply to the court within s 154(1)` `the document contains an untrue statement of a material fact` `the document omits to state a material fact required in it` `the document omits to state a material fact necessary to make a statement in it not misleading in the light of the circumstances in which it was made` `the applicant is an interested person` `the applicant is the Director`

-- s 154(1). The court may make any order it thinks fit including (a) restraining the solicitation, the holding of the meeting, or any person from implementing or acting on any resolution passed at the meeting, (b) requiring correction of any form of proxy or circular and a further solicitation, and (c) adjourning the meeting.
@ref CBCA s 154(1)
@export May the court make this kind of order (s 154(1))?
GIVEN `the document contains an untrue statement of a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the form of proxy or circular contain an untrue statement of a material fact?
      `the document omits to state a material fact required in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it omit to state a material fact required in it?
      `the document omits to state a material fact necessary to make a statement in it not misleading in the light of the circumstances in which it was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it omit to state a material fact necessary to make a statement in it not misleading in the light of the circumstances in which it was made?
      `the applicant is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an interested person?
      `the applicant is the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Director appointed under the Act?
      `the kind of order about a proxy document` IS A `Kind of order under s 154(1)` @desc Which kind of order is in question (restraining the solicitation, the holding of the meeting or the acting on any resolution; requiring correction and a further solicitation; adjourning the meeting; or any other order the court thinks fit)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court make this kind of order` IF
    `the court may make an order of a kind within s 154(1)`
        (`a person may apply to the court within s 154(1)`
            `the document contains an untrue statement of a material fact`
            `the document omits to state a material fact required in it`
            `the document omits to state a material fact necessary to make a statement in it not misleading in the light of the circumstances in which it was made`
            `the applicant is an interested person`
            `the applicant is the Director`)
        `the kind of order about a proxy document`

-- s 154(2). An applicant under this section shall give to the Director notice of the application.
@ref CBCA s 154(2)
@export Must I give the Director notice of my application (s 154(2))?
GIVEN `I am an applicant under section 154` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an applicant under section 154?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the Director notice of my application` IF
    `the applicant must give the Director notice within s 154(2)` `I am an applicant under section 154`

-- s 154(2). The duty is met by giving the Director notice of the application.
@ref CBCA s 154(2)
@export Have I met my duty to notify the Director (s 154(2))?
GIVEN `I am an applicant under section 154` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an applicant under section 154?
      `I gave the Director notice of the application under section 154` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the Director notice of the application?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I met my duty to notify the Director (s 154(2))` IF
    `the duty to give the Director notice is met within s 154(2)`
        (`the applicant must give the Director notice within s 154(2)`
            `I am an applicant under section 154`)
        `I gave the Director notice of the application under section 154`

-- s 154(2). The Director is entitled to appear and to be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 154(2)
@export Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on my application (s 154(2))?
GIVEN `the application is under section 154` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one under section 154?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the Director entitled to appear and be heard on my application (s 154(2))` IF
    `the Director is entitled to appear and be heard within s 154(2)` `the application is under section 154`


§§ `The annual financial statements (ss 155 to 158)`

-- Directors ask what must be placed before the shareholders; shareholders ask what they are owed.

-- s 155(1)(a)(i). The statements relate separately to the period that began on the date the corporation came into existence (or, if it has completed a financial year, immediately after the end of the last completed one) and ended not more than six months before the annual meeting.
@ref CBCA s 155(1)(a)(i)
@export Is the first period of the statements the one the Act requires (s 155(1)(a)(i))?
GIVEN `the corporation has completed a financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation completed a financial year?
      `the end of the last completed financial year` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the last completed financial year end?
      `the date the corporation came into existence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation come into existence?
      `the date the period began` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the period covered by the statements begin?
      `the date the period ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the period end?
      `the date of the annual meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the annual meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the first period of the statements the one the Act requires` IF
    `the first period of the statements is as s 155(1)(a)(i) requires within s 155(1)(a)(i)` (IF `the corporation has completed a financial year` THEN JUST `the end of the last completed financial year` ELSE NOTHING) `the date the corporation came into existence` `the date the period began` `the date the period ended` `the date of the annual meeting`

-- s 155(1)(a), (2). The directors shall place before the shareholders prescribed comparative financial statements for the period of (i) and for the immediately preceding financial year; the (ii) statements may be omitted if the reason is set out in the financial statements or in a note to them.
@ref CBCA s 155(1)(a), (2)
@export Are the statements placed before the shareholders the ones the Act requires (s 155(1)(a))?
GIVEN `the statements are the prescribed comparative financial statements and conform to the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the statements the prescribed comparative financial statements, conforming to the prescribed requirements?
      `the statements relate separately to the period of s 155(1)(a)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the statements relate separately to the period described in subparagraph 155(1)(a)(i)?
      `the statements relate separately to the immediately preceding financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the statements relate separately to the immediately preceding financial year?
      `the reason for omitting the statements for the immediately preceding financial year is set out in the financial statements or in a note to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If statements for the preceding financial year are omitted, is the reason set out in the financial statements or in a note to them?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the statements placed before the shareholders the ones the Act requires` IF
    `the statements placed are as s 155(1)(a) requires within s 155(1)(a)` `the statements are the prescribed comparative financial statements and conform to the prescribed requirements` `the statements relate separately to the period of s 155(1)(a)(i)` `the statements relate separately to the immediately preceding financial year` `the reason for omitting the statements for the immediately preceding financial year is set out in the financial statements or in a note to them`

-- s 155(1). The directors shall place before the shareholders at every annual meeting the statements of (a), the report of the auditor, if any, and any further information respecting the financial position and results of operations required by the articles, the by-laws or any unanimous shareholder agreement.
@ref CBCA s 155(1)
@export Have the directors placed everything before the shareholders that s 155(1) requires?
GIVEN `the statements are the prescribed comparative financial statements and conform to the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the statements the prescribed comparative financial statements, conforming to the prescribed requirements?
      `the statements relate separately to the period of s 155(1)(a)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the statements relate separately to the period described in subparagraph 155(1)(a)(i)?
      `the statements relate separately to the immediately preceding financial year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the statements relate separately to the immediately preceding financial year?
      `the reason for omitting the statements for the immediately preceding financial year is set out in the financial statements or in a note to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If statements for the preceding financial year are omitted, is the reason set out in the financial statements or in a note to them?
      `the corporation has an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have an auditor?
      `the report of the auditor is placed before the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor's report placed before the shareholders?
      `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement require further information respecting the financial position and results of operations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement require further information about the financial position and the results of operations?
      `that further information is placed before the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that further information placed before the shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the directors placed everything before the shareholders that s 155(1) requires` IF
    `the directors have complied with s 155(1) within s 155(1)`
        (`the statements placed are as s 155(1)(a) requires within s 155(1)(a)`
            `the statements are the prescribed comparative financial statements and conform to the prescribed requirements`
            `the statements relate separately to the period of s 155(1)(a)(i)`
            `the statements relate separately to the immediately preceding financial year`
            `the reason for omitting the statements for the immediately preceding financial year is set out in the financial statements or in a note to them`)
        `the corporation has an auditor`
        `the report of the auditor is placed before the shareholders`
        `the articles, the by-laws or a unanimous shareholder agreement require further information respecting the financial position and results of operations`
        `that further information is placed before the shareholders`

-- s 156. On the application of a corporation, the Director may exempt it, on any terms the Director thinks fit, from any requirement of section 155 or any of sections 157 to 160 if the Director reasonably believes that the detriment to the corporation outweighs the benefit to the shareholders or, for a distributing corporation, to the public.
-- Whether the Director does is the Director's decision and is not decided here.
@ref CBCA s 156
@export May the corporation ask the Director to exempt it from the financial disclosure requirements (s 156)?
GIVEN `the applicant is the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the applicant the corporation?
      `the requirement is a requirement of section 155 or of any of sections 157 to 160` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement one of section 155 or of any of sections 157 to 160?
      `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `the Director reasonably believes that the detriment that may be caused to the corporation by the requirement outweighs its benefit to the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Director reasonably believe that the detriment the requirement may cause to the corporation outweighs its benefit to the shareholders?
      `the Director reasonably believes that the detriment that may be caused to the corporation by the requirement outweighs its benefit to the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Director reasonably believe that the detriment the requirement may cause to the corporation outweighs its benefit to the public?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation ask the Director to exempt it from the financial disclosure requirements` IF
    `the Director may exempt the corporation within s 156` `the applicant is the corporation` `the requirement is a requirement of section 155 or of any of sections 157 to 160` `the corporation is a distributing corporation` `the Director reasonably believes that the detriment that may be caused to the corporation by the requirement outweighs its benefit to the shareholders` `the Director reasonably believes that the detriment that may be caused to the corporation by the requirement outweighs its benefit to the public`

-- s 157(1). A corporation shall keep at its registered office a copy of the financial statements of each of its subsidiary bodies corporate and of each body corporate the accounts of which are consolidated in its own.
@ref CBCA s 157(1)
@export Must the corporation keep a copy of this body corporate's financial statements at its registered office (s 157(1))?
GIVEN `the body corporate is a subsidiary of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body corporate a subsidiary of the corporation?
      `the accounts of the body corporate are consolidated in the financial statements of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the accounts of the body corporate consolidated in the corporation's financial statements?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation keep a copy of this body corporate's financial statements at its registered office` IF
    `the corporation must keep a copy of the statements within s 157(1)` `the body corporate is a subsidiary of the corporation` `the accounts of the body corporate are consolidated in the financial statements of the corporation`

-- s 157(1). The duty is met by keeping the copy at the registered office.
@ref CBCA s 157(1)
@export Has the corporation kept the copy at its registered office as required (s 157(1))?
GIVEN `the body corporate is a subsidiary of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body corporate a subsidiary of the corporation?
      `the accounts of the body corporate are consolidated in the financial statements of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the accounts of the body corporate consolidated in the corporation's financial statements?
      `a copy is kept at the registered office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a copy kept at the registered office of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation kept the copy at its registered office as required` IF
    `the duty to keep a copy at the registered office is met within s 157(1)`
        (`the corporation must keep a copy of the statements within s 157(1)`
            `the body corporate is a subsidiary of the corporation`
            `the accounts of the body corporate are consolidated in the financial statements of the corporation`)
        `a copy is kept at the registered office of the corporation`

-- s 157(2). A shareholder of a corporation, and the shareholder's personal representative, may on request, during usual business hours, examine the statements referred to in subsection (1) and make extracts from them free of charge, unless the court has barred the right under (3).
@ref CBCA s 157(2)
@export May I examine the subsidiary statements and make extracts free of charge (s 157(2))?
GIVEN `I am a shareholder or the personal representative of a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder, or the personal representative of a shareholder?
      `I request to examine the statements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you ask to examine the statements?
      `it is during the usual business hours of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it during the usual business hours of the corporation?
      `the court has barred my right to examine under subsection 157(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court barred your right to examine them under subsection 157(3)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I examine the subsidiary statements and make extracts free of charge` IF
    `a shareholder may examine the statements and make extracts free of charge within s 157(2)` `I am a shareholder or the personal representative of a shareholder` `I request to examine the statements` `it is during the usual business hours of the corporation` `the court has barred my right to examine under subsection 157(3)`

-- s 157(3). The corporation may, within fifteen days of the request, apply to the court to bar the right to examine. The day of the request is day 0.
@ref CBCA s 157(3)
@export By when may the corporation ask the court to bar my examination (s 157(3))?
GIVEN `the date of the request to examine` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the request to examine made?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when may the corporation ask the court to bar my examination` IS
    `the last day to apply to bar the examination within s 157(3)` `the date of the request to examine`

-- s 157(3). The same fifteen days, asked of the day the corporation applies.
@ref CBCA s 157(3)
@export May the corporation still ask the court to bar my examination (s 157(3))?
GIVEN `the date of the request to examine` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the request to examine made?
      `the date the corporation applies to the court` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the corporation apply to the court?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation still ask the court to bar my examination` IF
    `the corporation may apply to the court within s 157(3)` `the date of the request to examine` `the date the corporation applies to the court`

-- s 157(3). The court may bar the right to examine if the application was made within fifteen days and the court is satisfied that the examination would be detrimental to the corporation or a subsidiary body corporate.
@ref CBCA s 157(3)
@export May the court bar my examination (s 157(3))?
GIVEN `the application was made within fifteen days of the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the application made within fifteen days of the request?
      `the court is satisfied that the examination would be detrimental to the corporation or a subsidiary body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that the examination would be detrimental to the corporation or a subsidiary body corporate?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court bar my examination` IF
    `the court may bar the right to examine within s 157(3)` `the application was made within fifteen days of the request` `the court is satisfied that the examination would be detrimental to the corporation or a subsidiary body corporate`

-- s 157(4). A corporation that applies under (3) shall give the Director and the person asking to examine notice of the application.
@ref CBCA s 157(4)
@export Must the corporation tell me and the Director that it is applying to bar my examination (s 157(4))?
GIVEN `the corporation applies under subsection 157(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation applying under subsection 157(3)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation tell me and the Director that it is applying to bar my examination` IF
    `the corporation must give notice of the application within s 157(4)` `the corporation applies under subsection 157(3)`

-- s 157(4). The duty is met by giving notice of the application to the Director and to the person asking to examine.
@ref CBCA s 157(4)
@export Has the corporation notified me and the Director of its application (s 157(4))?
GIVEN `the corporation applies under subsection 157(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation applying under subsection 157(3)?
      `notice was given to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice given to the Director?
      `notice was given to the person asking to examine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was notice given to the person asking to examine?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation notified me and the Director of its application` IF
    `the duty to give notice of the application is met within s 157(4)`
        (`the corporation must give notice of the application within s 157(4)`
            `the corporation applies under subsection 157(3)`)
        `notice was given to the Director`
        `notice was given to the person asking to examine`

-- s 157(4). The Director and the person asking to examine may appear and be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 157(4)
@export May the Director and I appear and be heard on the corporation's application (s 157(4))?
GIVEN `I am the Director or the person asking to examine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Director, or the person who asked to examine?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director and I appear and be heard on the corporation's application` IF
    `the Director and the person may appear and be heard within s 157(4)` `I am the Director or the person asking to examine`

-- s 158(1). The financial statements shall be approved by the board of directors and evidenced by the signature of one or more directors; a facsimile of the signature may be reproduced.
@ref CBCA s 158(1)
@export Are the statements approved and signed as the Act requires (s 158(1))?
GIVEN `the number of directors who signed the statements manually` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors signed the statements by hand?
      `a facsimile of the signatures is reproduced in the statements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a facsimile of the signatures reproduced in the statements?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Are the statements approved and signed as the Act requires` IF
    `the approval is evidenced as s 158(1) requires within s 158(1)` `the number of directors who signed the statements manually` `a facsimile of the signatures is reproduced in the statements`

-- s 158(2). A corporation shall not issue, publish or circulate copies of the financial statements unless they are approved and signed in accordance with (1) and accompanied by the report of the auditor, if any.
@ref CBCA s 158(2)
@export Is the corporation barred from issuing copies of the statements as they stand (s 158(2))?
GIVEN `the corporation issues, publishes or circulates copies of the statements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation issue, publish or circulate copies of the statements?
      `the number of directors who signed the statements manually` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors signed the statements by hand?
      `a facsimile of the signatures is reproduced in the statements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a facsimile of the signatures reproduced in the statements?
      `the corporation has an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation have an auditor?
      `the statements are accompanied by the report of the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the statements accompanied by the auditor's report?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation barred from issuing copies of the statements as they stand` IF
    `issuing copies is prohibited within s 158(2)`
        `the corporation issues, publishes or circulates copies of the statements`
        (`the condition for issuing copies is met within s 158(2)`
            (`the approval is evidenced as s 158(1) requires within s 158(1)`
                `the number of directors who signed the statements manually`
                `a facsimile of the signatures is reproduced in the statements`)
            `the corporation has an auditor`
            `the statements are accompanied by the report of the auditor`)


§§ `Copies of the financial statements for shareholders and the Director (ss 159 and 160)`

-- Shareholders ask what they are owed before the annual meeting; directors ask what the corporation must send.

-- s 159(1). A corporation shall send a copy of the documents referred to in section 155 to each shareholder, except one who has informed the corporation in writing that they do not want a copy.
@ref CBCA s 159(1)
@export Must the corporation send me a copy of the annual financial statements (s 159(1))?
GIVEN `I have informed the corporation in writing that I do not want a copy of the documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you told the corporation in writing that you do not want a copy of the documents?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation send me a copy of the annual financial statements` IF
    `the corporation must send the documents to the shareholder within s 159(1)` `I have informed the corporation in writing that I do not want a copy of the documents`

-- s 159(1). The copy shall be sent not less than twenty-one days before the annual meeting (or before the signing of a resolution in lieu): on or before the twenty-first day before it.
@ref CBCA s 159(1)
@export By when must the corporation send me the documents (s 159(1))?
GIVEN `the date of the annual meeting, or of the signing of the resolution in lieu of it` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the annual meeting, or the signing of the resolution in lieu of it?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the corporation send me the documents` IS
    `the last day to send the documents to the shareholders within s 159(1)` `the date of the annual meeting, or of the signing of the resolution in lieu of it`

-- s 159(1). The same limit, asked of the day the documents were sent.
@ref CBCA s 159(1)
@export Were the documents sent to me in time (s 159(1))?
GIVEN `the date of the annual meeting, or of the signing of the resolution in lieu of it` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the annual meeting, or the signing of the resolution in lieu of it?
      `the date the documents were sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the documents sent?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Were the documents sent to me in time` IF
    `the documents were sent in time within s 159(1)` `the date of the annual meeting, or of the signing of the resolution in lieu of it` `the date the documents were sent`

-- s 159(2). A corporation that, without reasonable cause, fails to comply with subsection (1) is guilty of an offence.
@ref CBCA s 159(2)
@export Is the corporation guilty of an offence for not sending me the documents (s 159(2))?
GIVEN `the corporation failed to comply with subsection 159(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation fail to comply with subsection 159(1)?
      `the failure was without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the failure without reasonable cause?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation guilty of an offence for not sending me the documents` IF
    `the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 159(2)` `the corporation failed to comply with subsection 159(1)` `the failure was without reasonable cause`

-- s 159(2). Liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars; the ceiling is not the sentence.
@ref CBCA s 159(2) fine
@export What is the most the corporation can be fined under s 159(2)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the corporation can be fined under s 159(2)` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 159(2)`)'s `maximum fine in dollars`

-- s 159(2). The text states no imprisonment for this offence.
@ref CBCA s 159(2) imprisonment
@export What is the longest imprisonment under s 159(2), in months?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment under s 159(2), in months` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 159(2)`)'s `maximum imprisonment in months`

-- s 160(2). A subsidiary corporation is not required to comply with section 160 if the financial statements of its holding corporation are in consolidated or combined form and include the subsidiary's accounts, and are included in the documents the holding corporation sent to the Director in compliance with section 160.
@ref CBCA s 160(2)
@export Is the subsidiary corporation excused from sending the documents to the Director (s 160(2))?
GIVEN `the financial statements of the holding corporation are in consolidated or combined form and include the accounts of the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the holding corporation's financial statements in consolidated or combined form and do they include the subsidiary's accounts?
      `the consolidated or combined statements are included in the documents sent to the Director by the holding corporation in compliance with section 160` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those consolidated or combined statements included in the documents the holding corporation sent to the Director in compliance with section 160?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the subsidiary corporation excused from sending the documents to the Director` IF
    `the subsidiary corporation is not required to comply with s 160 within s 160(2)` `the financial statements of the holding corporation are in consolidated or combined form and include the accounts of the subsidiary` `the consolidated or combined statements are included in the documents sent to the Director by the holding corporation in compliance with section 160`

-- s 160(1). A distributing corporation, any of the issued securities of which remain outstanding and are held by more than one person, shall send a copy of the documents referred to in section 155 to the Director.
@ref CBCA s 160(1)
@export Must the corporation send the financial statements to the Director (s 160(1))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `any of its issued securities remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do any of its issued securities remain outstanding?
      `the number of persons who hold them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons hold them?
      `the financial statements of the holding corporation are in consolidated or combined form and include the accounts of the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the holding corporation's financial statements in consolidated or combined form and do they include the subsidiary's accounts?
      `the consolidated or combined statements are included in the documents sent to the Director by the holding corporation in compliance with section 160` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those consolidated or combined statements included in the documents the holding corporation sent to the Director in compliance with section 160?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation send the financial statements to the Director` IF
    `the corporation must send the documents to the Director within s 160(1)`
        `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
        `any of its issued securities remain outstanding`
        `the number of persons who hold them`
        (`the subsidiary corporation is not required to comply with s 160 within s 160(2)`
            `the financial statements of the holding corporation are in consolidated or combined form and include the accounts of the subsidiary`
            `the consolidated or combined statements are included in the documents sent to the Director by the holding corporation in compliance with section 160`)

-- s 160(1)(a). The copy goes to the Director not less than twenty-one days before each annual meeting, or without delay after a resolution under paragraph 142(1)(b) is signed.
@ref CBCA s 160(1)(a)
@export Were the documents sent to the Director in time for the meeting (s 160(1)(a))?
GIVEN `a resolution under paragraph 142(1)(b) is signed in lieu of the annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a written resolution under paragraph 142(1)(b) signed in lieu of the annual meeting?
      `the date of the annual meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the annual meeting?
      `the date the documents were sent to the Director` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the documents sent to the Director?
      `the documents were sent to the Director without delay after the resolution was signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a resolution was signed in lieu of the meeting, were the documents sent to the Director without delay afterwards?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Were the documents sent to the Director in time for the meeting` IF
    `the documents were sent to the Director in time within s 160(1)(a)` `a resolution under paragraph 142(1)(b) is signed in lieu of the annual meeting` `the date of the annual meeting` `the date the documents were sent to the Director` `the documents were sent to the Director without delay after the resolution was signed`

-- s 160(1)(b). In any event, within fifteen months after the last preceding annual meeting should have been held (or a resolution in lieu signed), but no later than six months after the end of the preceding financial year: the earlier of the two days.
@ref CBCA s 160(1)(b)
@export By when must the documents reach the Director in any event (s 160(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the date the last preceding annual meeting should have been held, or the resolution in lieu should have been signed` IS A DATE @desc On what date should the last preceding annual meeting have been held, or the resolution in lieu have been signed?
      `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation's preceding financial year end?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the documents reach the Director in any event` IS
    `the last day to send the documents to the Director within s 160(1)(b)` `the date the last preceding annual meeting should have been held, or the resolution in lieu should have been signed` `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended`

-- s 160(1)(b). The same limit, asked of the day the documents were sent.
@ref CBCA s 160(1)(b)
@export Were the documents sent to the Director in time in any event (s 160(1)(b))?
GIVEN `the date the last preceding annual meeting should have been held, or the resolution in lieu should have been signed` IS A DATE @desc On what date should the last preceding annual meeting have been held, or the resolution in lieu have been signed?
      `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the corporation's preceding financial year end?
      `the date the documents were sent to the Director` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the documents sent to the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Were the documents sent to the Director in time in any event` IF
    `the documents were sent to the Director in any event in time within s 160(1)(b)` `the date the last preceding annual meeting should have been held, or the resolution in lieu should have been signed` `the date the corporation's preceding financial year ended` `the date the documents were sent to the Director`

-- s 160(3). A corporation that fails to comply with this section is guilty of an offence.
@ref CBCA s 160(3)
@export Is the corporation guilty of an offence for not sending the documents to the Director (s 160(3))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `any of its issued securities remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do any of its issued securities remain outstanding?
      `the number of persons who hold them` IS A NUMBER @desc How many persons hold them?
      `the financial statements of the holding corporation are in consolidated or combined form and include the accounts of the subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the holding corporation's financial statements in consolidated or combined form and do they include the subsidiary's accounts?
      `the consolidated or combined statements are included in the documents sent to the Director by the holding corporation in compliance with section 160` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are those consolidated or combined statements included in the documents the holding corporation sent to the Director in compliance with section 160?
      `the corporation failed to comply with section 160` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation fail to comply with section 160?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the corporation guilty of an offence for not sending the documents to the Director` IF
    `the corporation is guilty of an offence within s 160(3)`
        (`the corporation must send the documents to the Director within s 160(1)`
            `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
            `any of its issued securities remain outstanding`
            `the number of persons who hold them`
            (`the subsidiary corporation is not required to comply with s 160 within s 160(2)`
                `the financial statements of the holding corporation are in consolidated or combined form and include the accounts of the subsidiary`
                `the consolidated or combined statements are included in the documents sent to the Director by the holding corporation in compliance with section 160`))
        `the corporation failed to comply with section 160`

-- s 160(3). Liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars; the ceiling is not the sentence.
@ref CBCA s 160(3) fine
@export What is the most the corporation can be fined under s 160(3)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the corporation can be fined under s 160(3)` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 160(3)`)'s `maximum fine in dollars`

-- s 160(3). The text states no imprisonment for this offence.
@ref CBCA s 160(3) imprisonment
@export What is the longest imprisonment under s 160(3), in months?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment under s 160(3), in months` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 160(3)`)'s `maximum imprisonment in months`


§§ `Who may be the auditor (s 161)`

-- Only if the corporation has, or is choosing, an auditor.

-- s 161(2.1). For the purposes of (2), a business partner of a person includes a shareholder of that person; the ordinary meaning is added to.
@ref CBCA s 161(2.1)
@export Is this person my business partner for the independence rule (s 161(2.1))?
GIVEN `the other is a business partner of the person in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person a business partner in the ordinary sense?
      `the other is a shareholder of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the other person a shareholder of the person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person my business partner for the independence rule` IF
    `a business partner within s 161(2.1)` `the other is a business partner of the person in the ordinary sense` `the other is a shareholder of the person`

-- s 161(2)(b). A person is deemed not independent if they or their business partner (i) is a business partner, director, officer or employee of the corporation or its affiliates, or a business partner of any of their directors, officers or employees; (ii) beneficially owns or controls a material interest in their securities; or (iii) has been a receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator, liquidator or trustee in bankruptcy of the corporation or its affiliates within two years of the proposed appointment.
@ref CBCA s 161(2)(b)
@export Is this person deemed not independent of the corporation (s 161(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the person or their business partner is a business partner, a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation or any of its affiliates, or a business partner of any director, officer or employee of any such corporation or its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person or their business partner a business partner, a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation or any of its affiliates, or a business partner of any director, officer or employee of any such corporation or its affiliates?
      `the person or their business partner beneficially owns or controls, directly or indirectly, a material interest in the securities of the corporation or any of its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person or their business partner beneficially own or control, directly or indirectly, a material interest in the securities of the corporation or any of its affiliates?
      `the person or their business partner has been a receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator, liquidator or trustee in bankruptcy of the corporation or any of its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person or their business partner been a receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator, liquidator or trustee in bankruptcy of the corporation or any of its affiliates?
      `the last day they held that office` IS A DATE @desc On what date did they last hold that office?
      `the date of the proposed appointment as auditor` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the person proposed to be appointed auditor?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person deemed not independent of the corporation` IF
    `the person is deemed not independent within s 161(2)(b)` `the person or their business partner is a business partner, a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation or any of its affiliates, or a business partner of any director, officer or employee of any such corporation or its affiliates` `the person or their business partner beneficially owns or controls, directly or indirectly, a material interest in the securities of the corporation or any of its affiliates` (IF `the person or their business partner has been a receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator, liquidator or trustee in bankruptcy of the corporation or any of its affiliates` THEN JUST `the last day they held that office` ELSE NOTHING) `the date of the proposed appointment as auditor`

-- s 161(1), (2). A person is disqualified from being an auditor if not independent: if they are not independent of the corporation, its affiliates and their directors or officers, as a question of fact, or are deemed not independent by (2)(b). An exemption order under (5) lifts the disqualification.
@ref CBCA s 161(1), (2)
@export Is this person disqualified from being our auditor (s 161(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `the person is independent of the corporation, its affiliates, and the directors or officers of any such corporation or its affiliates, as a question of fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person independent of the corporation, its affiliates, and the directors or officers of any such corporation or its affiliates, as a question of fact?
      `the person or their business partner is a business partner, a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation or any of its affiliates, or a business partner of any director, officer or employee of any such corporation or its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person or their business partner a business partner, a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation or any of its affiliates, or a business partner of any director, officer or employee of any such corporation or its affiliates?
      `the person or their business partner beneficially owns or controls, directly or indirectly, a material interest in the securities of the corporation or any of its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person or their business partner beneficially own or control, directly or indirectly, a material interest in the securities of the corporation or any of its affiliates?
      `the person or their business partner has been a receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator, liquidator or trustee in bankruptcy of the corporation or any of its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person or their business partner been a receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator, liquidator or trustee in bankruptcy of the corporation or any of its affiliates?
      `the last day they held that office` IS A DATE @desc On what date did they last hold that office?
      `the date of the proposed appointment as auditor` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the person proposed to be appointed auditor?
      `an exemption order has been made under subsection 161(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an exemption order under subsection 161(5)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person disqualified from being our auditor` IF
    `a person is disqualified from being an auditor within s 161(1)`
        (`the person is not independent within s 161(2)`
            `the person is independent of the corporation, its affiliates, and the directors or officers of any such corporation or its affiliates, as a question of fact`
            (`the person is deemed not independent within s 161(2)(b)`
                `the person or their business partner is a business partner, a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation or any of its affiliates, or a business partner of any director, officer or employee of any such corporation or its affiliates`
                `the person or their business partner beneficially owns or controls, directly or indirectly, a material interest in the securities of the corporation or any of its affiliates`
                (IF `the person or their business partner has been a receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator, liquidator or trustee in bankruptcy of the corporation or any of its affiliates` THEN JUST `the last day they held that office` ELSE NOTHING)
                `the date of the proposed appointment as auditor`))
        `an exemption order has been made under subsection 161(5)`

-- s 161(3). An auditor who becomes disqualified shall, subject to subsection (5), resign forthwith after becoming aware of the disqualification.
@ref CBCA s 161(3)
@export Must our auditor resign (s 161(3))?
GIVEN `the auditor is disqualified under section 161` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor disqualified under section 161?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must our auditor resign` IF
    `the auditor must resign forthwith within s 161(3)` `the auditor is disqualified under section 161`

-- s 161(3). The duty is met by resigning forthwith ("forthwith" is the person's own judgment).
@ref CBCA s 161(3)
@export Has our auditor done what s 161(3) requires?
GIVEN `the auditor is disqualified under section 161` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor disqualified under section 161?
      `the auditor resigned forthwith after becoming aware of the disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the auditor resign forthwith after becoming aware of the disqualification?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has our auditor done what s 161(3) requires` IF
    `the duty to resign is met within s 161(3)`
        (`the auditor must resign forthwith within s 161(3)`
            `the auditor is disqualified under section 161`)
        `the auditor resigned forthwith after becoming aware of the disqualification`

-- s 161(4). An interested person may apply to a court for an order declaring that an auditor is disqualified and that the office is vacant.
@ref CBCA s 161(4)
@export May I ask the court to declare our auditor disqualified (s 161(4))?
GIVEN `I am an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an interested person?
      `the auditor is disqualified under section 161` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the auditor disqualified under section 161?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the court to declare our auditor disqualified` IF
    `an interested person may apply for a disqualification order within s 161(4)`
        `I am an interested person`
        `the auditor is disqualified under section 161`

-- s 161(5). An interested person may apply to a court for an order exempting an auditor from disqualification.
@ref CBCA s 161(5)
@export May I ask the court to exempt our auditor from disqualification (s 161(5))?
GIVEN `I am an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an interested person?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask the court to exempt our auditor from disqualification` IF
    `an interested person may apply for an exemption order within s 161(5)` `I am an interested person`

-- s 161(5). The court may make an exemption order, on such terms as it thinks fit, if satisfied that an exemption would not unfairly prejudice the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 161(5)
@export May the court exempt our auditor from disqualification (s 161(5))?
GIVEN `an application for an exemption order is made by an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an interested person applied for an exemption order?
      `the court is satisfied that an exemption would not unfairly prejudice the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied that an exemption would not unfairly prejudice the shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court exempt our auditor from disqualification` IF
    `the court may make an exemption order within s 161(5)` `an application for an exemption order is made by an interested person` `the court is satisfied that an exemption would not unfairly prejudice the shareholders`

-- s 161(5). The exemption order may have retrospective effect.
@ref CBCA s 161(5)
@export May the exemption have retrospective effect (s 161(5))?
GIVEN `the court has made an exemption order under subsection 161(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made an exemption order under subsection 161(5)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the exemption have retrospective effect` IF
    `the exemption order may have retrospective effect within s 161(5)` `the court has made an exemption order under subsection 161(5)`


§§ `Appointing, replacing and removing the auditor (ss 162 to 167)`

-- Only when the shareholders are appointing an auditor, or an auditor has resigned, been removed or died.

-- s 162(1). Subject to section 163, the shareholders shall, by ordinary resolution, at the first annual meeting and at each succeeding annual meeting, appoint an auditor to hold office until the close of the next annual meeting.
@ref CBCA s 162(1)
@export Must the shareholders appoint an auditor at the annual meeting (s 162(1))?
GIVEN `it is the first annual meeting of shareholders or a succeeding annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the first annual meeting of shareholders or a succeeding annual meeting?
      `the shareholders have resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the shareholders resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the shareholders appoint an auditor at the annual meeting` IF
    `the shareholders must appoint an auditor within s 162(1)` `it is the first annual meeting of shareholders or a succeeding annual meeting` `the shareholders have resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor`

-- s 162(1). The auditor is appointed by ordinary resolution: a majority of the votes cast by the shareholders who voted. A resolution in writing signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote is as valid as one passed at a meeting under s 142(1)(a), asked about in its own question.
@ref CBCA s 162(1)
@export Has the auditor been validly appointed by ordinary resolution (s 162(1))?
GIVEN `it is the first annual meeting of shareholders or a succeeding annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the first annual meeting of shareholders or a succeeding annual meeting?
      `the shareholders have resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the shareholders resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor?
      `the votes cast in favour of the appointment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favour of the appointment?
      `the votes cast against the appointment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast against the appointment?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the auditor been validly appointed by ordinary resolution` IF
    `the auditor is appointed by ordinary resolution within s 162(1)`
        (`the shareholders must appoint an auditor within s 162(1)`
            `it is the first annual meeting of shareholders or a succeeding annual meeting`
            `the shareholders have resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor`)
        tally
    WHERE
        tally MEANS `Vote tally` WITH
            `votes cast in favour` IS `the votes cast in favour of the appointment`
            `votes cast against` IS `the votes cast against the appointment`
            `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS FALSE

-- s 162(1). The auditor holds office until the close of the next annual meeting.
@ref CBCA s 162(1)
@export Does the auditor still hold office on this date (s 162(1))?
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
      `the date of the close of the next annual meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the next annual meeting close?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the auditor still hold office on this date` IF
    `the appointed auditor holds office within s 162(1)` `the date` `the date of the close of the next annual meeting`

-- s 162(2). An auditor appointed under section 104 is eligible for appointment under subsection (1).
@ref CBCA s 162(2)
@export Is the auditor the directors appointed under section 104 eligible for appointment by the shareholders (s 162(2))?
GIVEN `the auditor was appointed under section 104` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the auditor appointed under section 104?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the auditor the directors appointed under section 104 eligible for appointment by the shareholders` IF
    `the auditor appointed under section 104 is eligible within s 162(2)` `the auditor was appointed under section 104`

-- s 162(3). Despite subsection (1), if an auditor is not appointed at a meeting, the incumbent auditor continues in office until a successor is appointed.
@ref CBCA s 162(3)
@export Does our incumbent auditor stay on if no auditor is appointed at the meeting (s 162(3))?
GIVEN `an auditor is not appointed at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an auditor not appointed at a meeting of shareholders?
      `a successor has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a successor been appointed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does our incumbent auditor stay on if no auditor is appointed at the meeting` IF
    `the incumbent auditor continues in office within s 162(3)` `an auditor is not appointed at a meeting of shareholders` `a successor has been appointed`

-- s 162(4). The remuneration of an auditor may be fixed by ordinary resolution of the shareholders or, if not so fixed, by the directors.
@ref CBCA s 162(4)
@export May the directors fix the auditor's remuneration (s 162(4))?
GIVEN `the remuneration has been fixed by ordinary resolution of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the remuneration been fixed by ordinary resolution of the shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the directors fix the auditor's remuneration` IF
    `the directors may fix the remuneration of the auditor within s 162(4)` `the remuneration has been fixed by ordinary resolution of the shareholders`

-- s 163(1). The shareholders of a corporation that is not a distributing corporation may resolve not to appoint an auditor.
@ref CBCA s 163(1)
@export May we decide not to have an auditor (s 163(1))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we decide not to have an auditor` IF
    `shareholders may resolve not to appoint an auditor within s 163(1)` `the corporation is a distributing corporation`

-- s 163(2), (3). A resolution not to appoint an auditor is valid only until the next succeeding annual meeting, and is not valid unless consented to by all the shareholders, including shareholders not otherwise entitled to vote.
@ref CBCA s 163(2), (3)
@export Is our resolution not to appoint an auditor still valid (s 163)?
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation a distributing corporation?
      `the resolution is consented to by all the shareholders, including shareholders not otherwise entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution consented to by all the shareholders, including shareholders not otherwise entitled to vote?
      `the date` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
      `the date of the next succeeding annual meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the next succeeding annual meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our resolution not to appoint an auditor still valid` IF
    `the resolution not to appoint an auditor is valid within s 163` `the corporation is a distributing corporation` `the resolution is consented to by all the shareholders, including shareholders not otherwise entitled to vote` `the date` `the date of the next succeeding annual meeting`

-- s 164(1). An auditor ceases to hold office when the auditor dies or resigns, or is removed under section 165.
@ref CBCA s 164(1)
@export Has our auditor ceased to hold office (s 164(1))?
GIVEN `the auditor dies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor died?
      `the auditor resigns` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor resigned?
      `the auditor is removed pursuant to section 165` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor been removed under section 165?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has our auditor ceased to hold office` IF
    `the auditor ceases to hold office within s 164(1)` `the auditor dies` `the auditor resigns` `the auditor is removed pursuant to section 165`

-- s 164(2). A resignation of an auditor becomes effective at the time a written resignation is sent to the corporation, or at the time specified in the resignation, whichever is later.
@ref CBCA s 164(2)
@export When does our auditor's resignation take effect (s 164(2))?
GIVEN `the date the written resignation is sent to the corporation` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the written resignation sent to the corporation?
      `the resignation specifies a later time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the resignation specify a date?
      `the date specified in the resignation` IS A DATE @desc What date does the resignation specify?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When does our auditor's resignation take effect` IS
    `the date the resignation becomes effective within s 164(2)` `the date the written resignation is sent to the corporation` (IF `the resignation specifies a later time` THEN JUST `the date specified in the resignation` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 165(1). The shareholders may by ordinary resolution at a special meeting remove the auditor from office, other than an auditor appointed by a court under section 167.
@ref CBCA s 165(1)
@export May the shareholders remove our auditor (s 165(1))?
GIVEN `the resolution is passed at a special meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the resolution passed at a special meeting of shareholders?
      `the votes cast in favour of the removal` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast in favour of removing the auditor?
      `the votes cast against the removal` IS A NUMBER @desc How many votes were cast against removing the auditor?
      `the auditor was appointed by a court under section 167` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the auditor appointed by a court under section 167?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the shareholders remove our auditor` IF
    `the shareholders may remove the auditor within s 165(1)`
        `the resolution is passed at a special meeting of shareholders`
        tally
        `the auditor was appointed by a court under section 167`
    WHERE
        tally MEANS `Vote tally` WITH
            `votes cast in favour` IS `the votes cast in favour of the removal`
            `votes cast against` IS `the votes cast against the removal`
            `signed by all the shareholders entitled to vote on the resolution` IS FALSE

-- s 165(2). A vacancy created by the removal of an auditor may be filled at the meeting at which the auditor is removed.
@ref CBCA s 165(2)
@export May we fill the vacancy at the meeting at which the auditor is removed (s 165(2))?
GIVEN `the vacancy was created by the removal of an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vacancy created by the removal of an auditor?
      `the filling is at the meeting at which the auditor is removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the filling at the meeting at which the auditor is removed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May we fill the vacancy at the meeting at which the auditor is removed` IF
    `the vacancy may be filled at the meeting of removal within s 165(2)` `the vacancy was created by the removal of an auditor` `the filling is at the meeting at which the auditor is removed`

-- s 165(2). If the vacancy is not so filled, it may be filled under section 166.
@ref CBCA s 165(2)
@export If we do not fill the vacancy at the removal meeting, may it be filled under section 166 (s 165(2))?
GIVEN `the vacancy was created by the removal of an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vacancy created by the removal of an auditor?
      `the vacancy was not filled at the meeting at which the auditor was removed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the vacancy not filled at the meeting at which the auditor was removed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `If we do not fill the vacancy at the removal meeting, may it be filled under section 166` IF
    `the vacancy may be filled under section 166 within s 165(2)` `the vacancy was created by the removal of an auditor` `the vacancy was not filled at the meeting at which the auditor was removed`

-- s 166(1). Subject to subsection (3), the directors shall forthwith fill a vacancy in the office of auditor. Subsection (3) lets the articles provide that a vacancy shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 166(1)
@export Must we, the directors, fill the vacancy in the office of auditor (s 166(1))?
GIVEN `there is a vacancy in the office of auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a vacancy in the office of auditor?
      `the articles provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we, the directors, fill the vacancy in the office of auditor` IF
    `the directors must fill the vacancy forthwith within s 166(1)` `there is a vacancy in the office of auditor` `the articles provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders`

-- s 166(1). The duty is met by filling the vacancy forthwith ("forthwith" is the directors' own judgment).
@ref CBCA s 166(1)
@export Have the directors filled the vacancy as required (s 166(1))?
GIVEN `there is a vacancy in the office of auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a vacancy in the office of auditor?
      `the articles provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders?
      `the directors filled the vacancy forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors fill the vacancy forthwith?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the directors filled the vacancy as required` IF
    `the duty to fill the vacancy is met within s 166(1)`
        (`the directors must fill the vacancy forthwith within s 166(1)`
            `there is a vacancy in the office of auditor`
            `the articles provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders`)
        `the directors filled the vacancy forthwith`

-- s 166(3). The articles of a corporation may provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 166(3)
@export May our articles reserve the filling of an auditor vacancy to the shareholders (s 166(3))?
GIVEN `the articles of the corporation provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the articles of the corporation provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our articles reserve the filling of an auditor vacancy to the shareholders` IF
    `the articles may so provide within s 166(3)` `the articles of the corporation provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders`

-- s 166(2). If there is not a quorum of directors, the directors then in office shall, within twenty-one days after a vacancy occurs, call a special meeting of shareholders to fill it. The day the vacancy occurs is day 0.
@ref CBCA s 166(2)
@export By when must the directors in office call a special meeting to fill the vacancy (s 166(2))?
GIVEN `the date the vacancy occurs` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the vacancy occur?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the directors in office call a special meeting to fill the vacancy` IS
    `the last day for the directors in office to call the meeting within s 166(2)` `the date the vacancy occurs`

-- s 166(2). Without a quorum, the directors then in office shall call a special meeting of shareholders to fill the vacancy.
@ref CBCA s 166(2)
@export Must the directors in office call a special meeting to fill the vacancy (s 166(2))?
GIVEN `there is a vacancy in the office of auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a vacancy in the office of auditor?
      `there is not a quorum of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there not a quorum of directors?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the directors in office call a special meeting to fill the vacancy` IF
    `the directors then in office must call a special meeting within s 166(2)` `there is a vacancy in the office of auditor` `there is not a quorum of directors`

-- s 166(2). If the directors fail to call a meeting, or if there are no directors, the meeting may be called by any shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 166(2)
@export May I, as a shareholder, call the meeting to fill the vacancy (s 166(2))?
GIVEN `there are no directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there no directors?
      `there is a vacancy in the office of auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a vacancy in the office of auditor?
      `there is not a quorum of directors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there not a quorum of directors?
      `the date the vacancy occurs` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the vacancy occur?
      `the directors called the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors in office call the meeting?
      `the date the directors called the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date did they call it?
      `the date the shareholder calls the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you call the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I, as a shareholder, call the meeting to fill the vacancy` IF
    `any shareholder may call the meeting within s 166(2)`
        `there are no directors`
        (`the directors then in office must call a special meeting within s 166(2)`
            `there is a vacancy in the office of auditor`
            `there is not a quorum of directors`)
        `the date the vacancy occurs`
        (IF `the directors called the meeting` THEN JUST `the date the directors called the meeting` ELSE NOTHING)
        `the date the shareholder calls the meeting`

-- s 166(4). An auditor appointed to fill a vacancy holds office for the unexpired term of the predecessor.
@ref CBCA s 166(4)
@export When does the term of the auditor appointed to fill the vacancy end (s 166(4))?
GIVEN `the date the predecessor's term of office would have ended` IS A DATE @desc On what date would the predecessor's term of office have ended?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `When does the term of the auditor appointed to fill the vacancy end` IS
    `the date the term of the auditor appointed to fill the vacancy ends within s 166(4)` `the date the predecessor's term of office would have ended`

-- s 167. If a corporation does not have an auditor, the court may, on the application of a shareholder or the Director, appoint and fix the remuneration of an auditor who holds office until one is appointed by the shareholders; but not if the shareholders have resolved under section 163 not to appoint one.
@ref CBCA s 167
@export May the court appoint an auditor for us on my application (s 167)?
GIVEN `the corporation does not have an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation not have an auditor?
      `the applicant is a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a shareholder?
      `the applicant is the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the Director appointed under the Act?
      `the shareholders have resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the shareholders resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the court appoint an auditor for us on my application` IF
    `the court may appoint an auditor and fix the remuneration within s 167` `the corporation does not have an auditor` `the applicant is a shareholder` `the applicant is the Director` `the shareholders have resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor`


§§ `The auditor's rights, the statements and the examination (ss 168 to 170)`

-- Only when the corporation has an auditor.

-- s 168(1). The auditor is entitled to receive notice of every meeting of shareholders and, at the expense of the corporation, to attend and be heard on matters relating to the auditor's duties.
@ref CBCA s 168(1)
@export Must the corporation give the auditor notice of the shareholders' meetings and let them attend (s 168(1))?
GIVEN `the person is the auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the auditor of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation give the auditor notice of the shareholders' meetings and let them attend` IF
    `the auditor is entitled to notice of and to attend and be heard at shareholders' meetings within s 168(1)` `the person is the auditor of the corporation`

-- s 168(1). The auditor attends at the expense of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 168(1)
@export Does the corporation bear the cost of the auditor's attendance at the meeting (s 168(1))?
GIVEN `the person is the auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the auditor of the corporation?
      `the auditor attends a meeting of shareholders on matters relating to the auditor's duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor attend a meeting of shareholders on matters relating to the auditor's duties?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the corporation bear the cost of the auditor's attendance at the meeting` IF
    `the corporation bears the expense of the auditor's attendance within s 168(1)` `the person is the auditor of the corporation` `the auditor attends a meeting of shareholders on matters relating to the auditor's duties`

-- s 168(2). If a director or shareholder, whether or not entitled to vote, gives written notice not less than ten days before a meeting to the auditor or a former auditor, they shall attend the meeting at the expense of the corporation and answer questions relating to their duties as auditor.
@ref CBCA s 168(2)
@export Must the auditor attend the meeting and answer questions because I gave written notice (s 168(2))?
GIVEN `the person is the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation?
      `a director or shareholder gave written notice to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a director or shareholder give written notice to the person?
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the written notice given to the auditor?
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the auditor attend the meeting and answer questions because I gave written notice` IF
    `the auditor or former auditor must attend the meeting within s 168(2)` `the person is the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation` `a director or shareholder gave written notice to the person` `the date the notice was given` `the date of the meeting`

-- s 168(2). The duty is met by attending and answering questions relating to their duties as auditor.
@ref CBCA s 168(2)
@export Has the auditor done what s 168(2) requires?
GIVEN `the person is the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation?
      `a director or shareholder gave written notice to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a director or shareholder give written notice to the person?
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the written notice given to the auditor?
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting?
      `the person attends the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person attend the meeting?
      `the person answers questions relating to their duties as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person answer questions relating to their duties as auditor?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the auditor done what s 168(2) requires` IF
    `the duty to attend and answer questions is met within s 168(2)`
        (`the auditor or former auditor must attend the meeting within s 168(2)`
            `the person is the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation`
            `a director or shareholder gave written notice to the person`
            `the date the notice was given`
            `the date of the meeting`)
        `the person attends the meeting`
        `the person answers questions relating to their duties as auditor`

-- s 168(3). A director or shareholder who sends the notice shall send concurrently a copy to the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 168(3)
@export Have I sent the corporation its copy of my notice to the auditor (s 168(3))?
GIVEN `the date the notice was sent` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you send the notice to the auditor?
      `the date the copy was sent to the corporation` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you send the copy to the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I sent the corporation its copy of my notice to the auditor` IF
    `the copy of the notice to the corporation is sent as s 168(3) requires within s 168(3)` `the date the notice was sent` `the date the copy was sent to the corporation`

-- s 168(4). An auditor or former auditor who fails without reasonable cause to comply with subsection (2) is guilty of an offence.
@ref CBCA s 168(4)
@export Is the auditor guilty of an offence for not attending when I asked (s 168(4))?
GIVEN `the person is the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation?
      `a director or shareholder gave written notice to the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a director or shareholder give written notice to the person?
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the written notice given to the auditor?
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the meeting?
      `the person failed to comply with subsection 168(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person fail to comply with subsection 168(2)?
      `the failure was without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the failure without reasonable cause?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the auditor guilty of an offence for not attending when I asked` IF
    `the auditor or former auditor is guilty of an offence within s 168(4)`
        (`the auditor or former auditor must attend the meeting within s 168(2)`
            `the person is the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation`
            `a director or shareholder gave written notice to the person`
            `the date the notice was given`
            `the date of the meeting`)
        `the person failed to comply with subsection 168(2)`
        `the failure was without reasonable cause`

-- s 168(4). Fine not exceeding five thousand dollars, or imprisonment not exceeding six months, or both; the ceiling is not the sentence.
@ref CBCA s 168(4) fine
@export What is the most our auditor can be fined under s 168(4)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most our auditor can be fined under s 168(4)` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 168(4)`)'s `maximum fine in dollars`

-- s 168(4). Imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months.
@ref CBCA s 168(4) imprisonment
@export What is the longest imprisonment our auditor can face under s 168(4), in months?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment our auditor can face under s 168(4), in months` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 168(4)`)'s `maximum imprisonment in months`

-- s 168(5). The auditor is entitled to submit to the corporation a written statement giving reasons for resigning or for opposing any proposed action or resolution when the auditor resigns, or learns of a meeting called to remove the auditor, of a meeting at which another person is to be appointed to fill the office, or of a meeting at which a section 163 resolution is to be proposed.
@ref CBCA s 168(5)
@export Is our auditor entitled to submit a written statement of reasons (s 168(5))?
GIVEN `the auditor resigns` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor resigned?
      `the auditor receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders called for the purpose of removing the auditor from office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor receive notice of, or otherwise learn of, a meeting of shareholders called for the purpose of removing the auditor from office?
      `the auditor receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of directors or shareholders at which another person is to be appointed to fill the office of auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor receive notice of, or otherwise learn of, a meeting of directors or shareholders at which another person is to be appointed to fill the office of auditor?
      `the auditor receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders at which a resolution referred to in section 163 is to be proposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor receive notice of, or otherwise learn of, a meeting of shareholders at which a resolution referred to in section 163 is to be proposed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our auditor entitled to submit a written statement of reasons` IF
    `the auditor is entitled to submit a statement within s 168(5)` `the auditor resigns` `the auditor receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders called for the purpose of removing the auditor from office` `the auditor receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of directors or shareholders at which another person is to be appointed to fill the office of auditor` `the auditor receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders at which a resolution referred to in section 163 is to be proposed`

-- s 168(5.1)(a). On a proposed replacement of an auditor, through removal or at the end of the auditor's term, the corporation shall make a statement on the reasons for the proposed replacement.
@ref CBCA s 168(5.1)(a)
@export Must the corporation give reasons for replacing the auditor (s 168(5.1)(a))?
GIVEN `an auditor is proposed to be replaced, through removal or at the end of the auditor's term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an auditor proposed to be replaced, through removal or at the end of the auditor's term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation give reasons for replacing the auditor` IF
    `the corporation must make a statement on the reasons for the replacement within s 168(5.1)(a)` `an auditor is proposed to be replaced, through removal or at the end of the auditor's term`

-- s 168(5.1)(b). The proposed replacement auditor may make a statement commenting on those reasons.
@ref CBCA s 168(5.1)(b)
@export May the proposed replacement auditor comment on the corporation's reasons (s 168(5.1)(b))?
GIVEN `an auditor is proposed to be replaced, through removal or at the end of the auditor's term` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an auditor proposed to be replaced, through removal or at the end of the auditor's term?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the proposed replacement auditor comment on the corporation's reasons` IF
    `the proposed replacement auditor may comment within s 168(5.1)(b)` `an auditor is proposed to be replaced, through removal or at the end of the auditor's term`

-- s 168(6). The corporation shall send a copy of the statements without delay to every shareholder entitled to receive notice of a meeting referred to in subsection (1) and to the Director, unless the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150.
@ref CBCA s 168(6)
@export Must the corporation send me a copy of the statements about the auditor's replacement (s 168(6))?
GIVEN `there is a statement under subsection 168(5) or (5.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a statement under subsection 168(5) or (5.1)?
      `the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation send me a copy of the statements about the auditor's replacement` IF
    `the corporation must send a copy of the statements within s 168(6)` `there is a statement under subsection 168(5) or (5.1)` `the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150`

-- s 168(6). The duty is met by sending the copy, without delay, to every shareholder entitled to receive notice of a meeting and to the Director.
@ref CBCA s 168(6)
@export Has the corporation sent the copies as required (s 168(6))?
GIVEN `there is a statement under subsection 168(5) or (5.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a statement under subsection 168(5) or (5.1)?
      `the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150?
      `a copy was sent without delay to every shareholder entitled to receive notice of a meeting referred to in subsection 168(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy sent without delay to every shareholder entitled to receive notice of a meeting referred to in subsection 168(1)?
      `a copy was sent without delay to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a copy sent without delay to the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the corporation sent the copies as required` IF
    `the duty to send a copy of the statements is met within s 168(6)`
        (`the corporation must send a copy of the statements within s 168(6)`
            `there is a statement under subsection 168(5) or (5.1)`
            `the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150`)
        `a copy was sent without delay to every shareholder entitled to receive notice of a meeting referred to in subsection 168(1)`
        `a copy was sent without delay to the Director`

-- s 168(7), (8). No person shall accept appointment as auditor to replace an auditor who has resigned, been removed or whose term has expired or is about to expire until they have requested and received from that auditor a written statement of the circumstances and the reasons for the replacement.
-- Despite (7), a person otherwise qualified may accept if, within fifteen days after making the request, they do not receive a reply. The request day is day 0.
@ref CBCA s 168(7), (8)
@export May I accept appointment as the new auditor now (s 168(7) and (8))?
GIVEN `I am otherwise qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you otherwise qualified to act as auditor?
      `I made a request to the auditor being replaced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you requested from the auditor being replaced a written statement of the circumstances and the reasons for the replacement?
      `the date I made the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the request?
      `I received the written statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received the written statement?
      `the date I received the statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive it?
      `the date I accept the appointment or consent to be appointed` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you accept the appointment or consent to be appointed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I accept appointment as the new auditor now` IF
    `a person may accept the appointment within s 168(7) and (8)`
        `I am otherwise qualified`
        (IF `I made a request to the auditor being replaced` THEN JUST `the date I made the request` ELSE NOTHING)
        (IF `I received the written statement` THEN JUST `the date I received the statement` ELSE NOTHING)
        `the date I accept the appointment or consent to be appointed`

-- s 168(8). The retiring auditor has fifteen days after the request to reply; the request day is day 0 and the fifteenth day after it is the last.
@ref CBCA s 168(8)
@export By when must the retiring auditor reply to my request (s 168(8))?
GIVEN `the date I made the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the request?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the retiring auditor reply to my request` IS
    `the last day for the auditor to reply within s 168(8)` `the date I made the request`

-- s 168(9). Unless subsection (8) applies, an appointment of a person who has not complied with subsection (7) is void.
@ref CBCA s 168(9)
@export Is my appointment as auditor void because I did not first get the retiring auditor's statement (s 168(9))?
GIVEN `I am otherwise qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you otherwise qualified to act as auditor?
      `I made a request to the auditor being replaced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you requested from the auditor being replaced a written statement of the circumstances and the reasons for the replacement?
      `the date I made the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the request?
      `I received the written statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you received the written statement?
      `the date I received the statement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive it?
      `the date I accept the appointment or consent to be appointed` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you accept the appointment or consent to be appointed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my appointment as auditor void because I did not first get the retiring auditor's statement` IF
    `the appointment is void within s 168(9)`
        (`a person may accept the appointment within s 168(7) and (8)`
            `I am otherwise qualified`
            (IF `I made a request to the auditor being replaced` THEN JUST `the date I made the request` ELSE NOTHING)
            (IF `I received the written statement` THEN JUST `the date I received the statement` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the date I accept the appointment or consent to be appointed`)

-- s 169(1). An auditor shall make the examination that is in their opinion necessary to enable them to report on the financial statements required by the Act to be placed before the shareholders, except statements, or the part of them, that relate to the period referred to in subparagraph 155(1)(a)(ii).
@ref CBCA s 169(1)
@export Must our auditor examine these statements (s 169(1))?
GIVEN `the statements are required by this Act to be placed before the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the statements required by the Act to be placed before the shareholders?
      `the statements or the part relate to the period referred to in subparagraph 155(1)(a)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the statements, or the part, relate to the immediately preceding financial year (subparagraph 155(1)(a)(ii))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must our auditor examine these statements` IF
    `the auditor must examine the statements within s 169(1)` `the statements are required by this Act to be placed before the shareholders` `the statements or the part relate to the period referred to in subparagraph 155(1)(a)(ii)`

-- s 169(2) to (4). Despite section 170, an auditor may reasonably rely on the report of an auditor of a body corporate or an unincorporated business whose accounts are included in whole or in part in the corporation's statements; reasonableness is a question of fact; and this applies whether or not the statements are consolidated.
@ref CBCA s 169(2) to (4)
@export May our auditor rely on another auditor's report on a subsidiary's accounts (s 169(2) to (4))?
GIVEN `the accounts of a body corporate or an unincorporated business are included in whole or in part in the financial statements of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the accounts of a body corporate or an unincorporated business included, in whole or in part, in the corporation's financial statements?
      `the reliance on the report of its auditor is reasonable, as a question of fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reliance on the report of its auditor reasonable, as a question of fact?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our auditor rely on another auditor's report on a subsidiary's accounts` IF
    `an auditor may rely on the report of another auditor within s 169(2)` `the accounts of a body corporate or an unincorporated business are included in whole or in part in the financial statements of the corporation` `the reliance on the report of its auditor is reasonable, as a question of fact`

-- s 170(1). On the demand of the auditor, the present or former directors, officers, employees, agents or mandataries of the corporation shall provide any information and explanations and access to records, documents, books, accounts and vouchers of the corporation or any of its subsidiaries that are, in the auditor's opinion, necessary for the examination and report under section 169 and that they are reasonably able to provide.
@ref CBCA s 170(1)
@export Must I give the auditor the information or access the auditor demands (s 170(1))?
GIVEN `the auditor demands it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor demand it?
      `I am a present or former director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a present or former director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary of the corporation?
      `it is information, an explanation, or access to records, documents, books, accounts or vouchers of the corporation or any of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it information, an explanation, or access to records, documents, books, accounts or vouchers of the corporation or any of its subsidiaries?
      `in the opinion of the auditor it is necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the auditor's opinion, is it necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169?
      `I am reasonably able to provide it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you reasonably able to provide it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give the auditor the information or access the auditor demands` IF
    `the person must provide it on the auditor's demand within s 170(1)` `the auditor demands it` `I am a present or former director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary of the corporation` `it is information, an explanation, or access to records, documents, books, accounts or vouchers of the corporation or any of its subsidiaries` `in the opinion of the auditor it is necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169` `I am reasonably able to provide it`

-- s 170(2). On the demand of the auditor, the directors shall obtain from the present or former directors, officers, employees and agents or mandataries of any subsidiary the information and explanations they are reasonably able to provide and that are, in the auditor's opinion, necessary, and furnish them to the auditor.
@ref CBCA s 170(2)
@export Must we, the directors, obtain and furnish the subsidiary's information to the auditor (s 170(2))?
GIVEN `the auditor demands it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor demand it?
      `the information and explanations are those the present or former directors, officers, employees or agents or mandataries of a subsidiary are reasonably able to provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the information and explanations those that the present or former directors, officers, employees or agents or mandataries of a subsidiary are reasonably able to provide?
      `in the opinion of the auditor they are necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the auditor's opinion, are they necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we, the directors, obtain and furnish the subsidiary's information to the auditor` IF
    `the directors must obtain and furnish the information within s 170(2)` `the auditor demands it` `the information and explanations are those the present or former directors, officers, employees or agents or mandataries of a subsidiary are reasonably able to provide` `in the opinion of the auditor they are necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169`

-- s 170(2). The duty is met by obtaining the information and explanations and furnishing them to the auditor.
@ref CBCA s 170(2)
@export Have the directors done what s 170(2) requires?
GIVEN `the auditor demands it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the auditor demand it?
      `the information and explanations are those the present or former directors, officers, employees or agents or mandataries of a subsidiary are reasonably able to provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the information and explanations those that the present or former directors, officers, employees or agents or mandataries of a subsidiary are reasonably able to provide?
      `in the opinion of the auditor they are necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the auditor's opinion, are they necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169?
      `the directors obtained the information and explanations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors obtain the information and explanations?
      `the directors furnished them to the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors furnish them to the auditor?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the directors done what s 170(2) requires` IF
    `the duty to obtain and furnish the information is met within s 170(2)`
        (`the directors must obtain and furnish the information within s 170(2)`
            `the auditor demands it`
            `the information and explanations are those the present or former directors, officers, employees or agents or mandataries of a subsidiary are reasonably able to provide`
            `in the opinion of the auditor they are necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169`)
        `the directors obtained the information and explanations`
        `the directors furnished them to the auditor`

-- s 170(3). A person who in good faith makes an oral or written communication under subsection (1) or (2) is not liable in any civil proceeding arising from having made it.
@ref CBCA s 170(3)
@export Am I free of civil liability for what I tell the auditor in good faith (s 170(3))?
GIVEN `the communication is made in good faith under subsection 170(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the communication in good faith under subsection 170(1) or (2)?
      `the proceeding is a civil proceeding arising from having made the communication` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil proceeding arising from having made the communication?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I free of civil liability for what I tell the auditor in good faith` IF
    `the person is not liable in the civil proceeding within s 170(3)` `the communication is made in good faith under subsection 170(1) or (2)` `the proceeding is a civil proceeding arising from having made the communication`


§§ `The audit committee (s 171)`

-- Directors ask what the committee must look like and do; the audit committee itself only arises in the corporations the Act describes, and any corporation may choose one.

-- s 171(1). Subject to subsection (2), a corporation described in subsection 102(2) shall have an audit committee; any other corporation may. The Director's authorization under (2) lifts the duty.
@ref CBCA s 171(1)
@export Must our corporation have an audit committee (s 171(1))?
GIVEN `the corporation is one described in subsection 102(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation one described in subsection 102(2) (the corporations that must have an audit committee)?
      `the Director has authorized the corporation to dispense with an audit committee under subsection 171(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Director authorized the corporation to dispense with an audit committee under subsection 171(2)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must our corporation have an audit committee` IF
    `the corporation must have an audit committee within s 171(1)` `the corporation is one described in subsection 102(2)` `the Director has authorized the corporation to dispense with an audit committee under subsection 171(2)`

-- s 171(1). Any corporation not described in subsection 102(2) may have an audit committee.
@ref CBCA s 171(1)
@export May our corporation have an audit committee although it is not required to (s 171(1))?
GIVEN `the corporation is one described in subsection 102(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation one described in subsection 102(2) (the corporations that must have an audit committee)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May our corporation have an audit committee although it is not required to` IF
    `a corporation not described in subsection 102(2) may have an audit committee within s 171(1)` `the corporation is one described in subsection 102(2)`

-- s 171(1). An audit committee has not less than three directors, a majority of whom are not officers or employees of the corporation or any of its affiliates. A majority is more than half.
@ref CBCA s 171(1)
@export Is our audit committee composed as the Act requires (s 171(1))?
GIVEN `the number of members of the audit committee` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members does the audit committee have?
      `all the members are directors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are all the members directors of the corporation?
      `the number of members who are not officers or employees of the corporation or any of its affiliates` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members are not officers or employees of the corporation or any of its affiliates?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is our audit committee composed as the Act requires` IF
    `the audit committee is composed as s 171(1) requires within s 171(1)` `the number of members of the audit committee` `all the members are directors of the corporation` `the number of members who are not officers or employees of the corporation or any of its affiliates`

-- s 171(2). The Director may, on the application of a corporation, authorize it to dispense with an audit committee. Whether the Director does is the Director's decision and is not decided here.
@ref CBCA s 171(2)
@export May the Director authorize us to dispense with an audit committee (s 171(2))?
GIVEN `the corporation applies to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation apply to the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director authorize us to dispense with an audit committee` IF
    `the Director may authorize the corporation to dispense with an audit committee within s 171(2)` `the corporation applies to the Director`

-- s 171(2). The Director may, if satisfied that the shareholders will not be prejudiced, permit the corporation to dispense with an audit committee on any reasonable conditions the Director thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 171(2)
@export May the Director permit us to dispense with an audit committee on conditions (s 171(2))?
GIVEN `the corporation applies to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the corporation apply to the Director?
      `the Director is satisfied that the shareholders will not be prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Director satisfied that the shareholders will not be prejudiced?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Director permit us to dispense with an audit committee on conditions` IF
    `the Director may permit the corporation to dispense with an audit committee on conditions within s 171(2)` `the corporation applies to the Director` `the Director is satisfied that the shareholders will not be prejudiced`

-- s 171(3). An audit committee shall review the financial statements of the corporation before such financial statements are approved under section 158. A date carries no time of day, so a review on the day of approval is read as before it (fork F-171-before).
@ref CBCA s 171(3)
@export Did the audit committee review the statements before they were approved (s 171(3))?
GIVEN `the date the audit committee reviewed the financial statements` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the audit committee review the financial statements?
      `the date the financial statements were approved under section 158` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the financial statements approved under section 158?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did the audit committee review the statements before they were approved` IF
    `the audit committee reviewed the statements before they were approved within s 171(3)` `the date the audit committee reviewed the financial statements` `the date the financial statements were approved under section 158`

-- s 171(4). The auditor is entitled to receive notice of every meeting of the audit committee and, at the expense of the corporation, to attend and be heard.
@ref CBCA s 171(4)
@export Must the audit committee give the auditor notice of its meetings and let them attend (s 171(4))?
GIVEN `the person is the auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the auditor of the corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the audit committee give the auditor notice of its meetings and let them attend` IF
    `the auditor is entitled to notice of and to attend and be heard at the committee's meetings within s 171(4)` `the person is the auditor of the corporation`

-- s 171(4). If so requested by a member of the audit committee, the auditor shall attend every meeting of the committee held during the auditor's term of office.
@ref CBCA s 171(4)
@export Must the auditor attend the audit committee's meeting if I ask (s 171(4))?
GIVEN `a member of the audit committee has requested the auditor to attend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a member of the audit committee requested the auditor to attend?
      `the meeting is held during the term of office of the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting held during the term of office of the auditor?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the auditor attend the audit committee's meeting if I ask` IF
    `the auditor must attend the committee's meeting within s 171(4)` `a member of the audit committee has requested the auditor to attend` `the meeting is held during the term of office of the auditor`

-- s 171(5). The auditor or a member of the audit committee may call a meeting of the committee.
@ref CBCA s 171(5)
@export May I call a meeting of the audit committee (s 171(5))?
GIVEN `the person is the auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the auditor of the corporation?
      `the person is a member of the audit committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the audit committee?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I call a meeting of the audit committee` IF
    `a person may call a meeting of the audit committee within s 171(5)` `the person is the auditor of the corporation` `the person is a member of the audit committee`

-- s 171(6). A director or an officer shall forthwith notify the audit committee and the auditor of any error or mis-statement of which they become aware in a financial statement that the auditor or a former auditor has reported on.
@ref CBCA s 171(6)
@export Must I notify the audit committee and the auditor of an error I found in the statements (s 171(6))?
GIVEN `the person is a director or an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of the corporation?
      `the person becomes aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement that the auditor or a former auditor has reported on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement that the auditor or a former auditor has reported on?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I notify the audit committee and the auditor of an error I found in the statements` IF
    `the director or officer must notify the committee and the auditor within s 171(6)` `the person is a director or an officer of the corporation` `the person becomes aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement that the auditor or a former auditor has reported on`

-- s 171(6). The duty is met by notifying the audit committee and the auditor forthwith.
@ref CBCA s 171(6)
@export Have I notified the committee and the auditor as required (s 171(6))?
GIVEN `the person is a director or an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of the corporation?
      `the person becomes aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement that the auditor or a former auditor has reported on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you become aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement that the auditor or a former auditor has reported on?
      `the person notified the audit committee forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the audit committee forthwith?
      `the person notified the auditor forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the auditor forthwith?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I notified the committee and the auditor as required` IF
    `the duty to notify the committee and the auditor is met within s 171(6)`
        (`the director or officer must notify the committee and the auditor within s 171(6)`
            `the person is a director or an officer of the corporation`
            `the person becomes aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement that the auditor or a former auditor has reported on`)
        `the person notified the audit committee forthwith`
        `the person notified the auditor forthwith`

-- s 171(7). An auditor or former auditor who is notified or becomes aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement on which they have reported, if in their opinion it is material, shall inform each director.
@ref CBCA s 171(7)
@export Must the auditor tell each director about a material error (s 171(7))?
GIVEN `the person is the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation?
      `the person is notified or becomes aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement on which they have reported` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been notified of, or become aware of, an error or mis-statement in a financial statement on which they have reported?
      `in the opinion of the person the error or mis-statement is material` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the person's opinion, is the error or mis-statement material?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the auditor tell each director about a material error` IF
    `the auditor or former auditor must inform each director within s 171(7)` `the person is the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation` `the person is notified or becomes aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement on which they have reported` `in the opinion of the person the error or mis-statement is material`

-- s 171(8). When the auditor informs the directors under subsection (7), the directors shall prepare and issue revised financial statements, or otherwise inform the shareholders and, if the corporation is required to comply with section 160, inform the Director in the same manner as it informs the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 171(8)
@export Must we, the directors, act when the auditor tells us of a material error (s 171(8))?
GIVEN `the auditor or former auditor informed the directors of an error or mis-statement under subsection 171(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor or a former auditor informed the directors of an error or mis-statement under subsection 171(7)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we, the directors, act when the auditor tells us of a material error` IF
    `the directors must act on the error or mis-statement within s 171(8)` `the auditor or former auditor informed the directors of an error or mis-statement under subsection 171(7)`

-- s 171(8). The duty is met by preparing and issuing revised statements, or by informing the shareholders and, if section 160 applies to the corporation, the Director in the same manner.
@ref CBCA s 171(8)
@export Have the directors done what s 171(8) requires?
GIVEN `the auditor or former auditor informed the directors of an error or mis-statement under subsection 171(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the auditor or a former auditor informed the directors of an error or mis-statement under subsection 171(7)?
      `the directors prepared and issued revised financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors prepare and issue revised financial statements?
      `the directors otherwise informed the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the directors otherwise inform the shareholders?
      `the corporation is required to comply with section 160` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation required to comply with section 160?
      `the corporation informed the Director of the error or mis-statement in the same manner as it informed the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the corporation inform the Director of the error or mis-statement in the same manner as it informed the shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the directors done what s 171(8) requires` IF
    `the duty of the directors is met within s 171(8)`
        (`the directors must act on the error or mis-statement within s 171(8)`
            `the auditor or former auditor informed the directors of an error or mis-statement under subsection 171(7)`)
        `the directors prepared and issued revised financial statements`
        `the directors otherwise informed the shareholders`
        `the corporation is required to comply with section 160`
        `the corporation informed the Director of the error or mis-statement in the same manner as it informed the shareholders`

-- s 171(9). Every director or officer who knowingly fails to comply with subsection (6) or (8) is guilty of an offence.
@ref CBCA s 171(9)
@export Am I guilty of an offence for knowingly not complying with s 171(6) or (8) (s 171(9))?
GIVEN `the person is a director or an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director or an officer of the corporation?
      `the person failed to comply with subsection 171(6) or (8)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with subsection 171(6) or (8)?
      `the person knew that they failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know that you failed to comply?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I guilty of an offence for knowingly not complying with s 171(6) or (8)` IF
    `a director or officer is guilty of an offence within s 171(9)` `the person is a director or an officer of the corporation` `the person failed to comply with subsection 171(6) or (8)` `the person knew that they failed to comply`

-- s 171(9). Fine not exceeding five thousand dollars, or imprisonment not exceeding six months, or both; the ceiling is not the sentence.
@ref CBCA s 171(9) fine
@export What is the most I can be fined under s 171(9)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined under s 171(9)` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 171(9)`)'s `maximum fine in dollars`

-- s 171(9). Imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months.
@ref CBCA s 171(9) imprisonment
@export What is the longest imprisonment I can face under s 171(9), in months?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest imprisonment I can face under s 171(9), in months` IS
    (`the penalty ceiling within s 171(9)`)'s `maximum imprisonment in months`


§§ `Qualified privilege (s 172)`

-- Only if an auditor or former auditor has made a statement or report under the Act.

-- s 172. Any oral or written statement or report made under the Act by the auditor or a former auditor of a corporation has qualified privilege.
@ref CBCA s 172
@export Does the auditor's statement or report have qualified privilege (s 172)?
GIVEN `it is an oral or written statement or report made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an oral or written statement or report made under this Act?
      `it is made by the auditor or a former auditor of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by the auditor or a former auditor of a corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the auditor's statement or report have qualified privilege` IF
    `the statement or report has qualified privilege within s 172` `it is an oral or written statement or report made under this Act` `it is made by the auditor or a former auditor of a corporation`


§§ `Diversity information (Part XIV.1, s 172.1)`

-- Only for the corporations the regulations prescribe, at their annual meeting.

-- s 172.1(1). The directors of a prescribed corporation shall place before the shareholders at every annual meeting the prescribed information about diversity among the directors and members of senior management.
@ref CBCA s 172.1(1)
@export Must we, the directors, place the diversity information before the shareholders (s 172.1(1))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a prescribed corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation one that the regulations prescribe for this purpose?
      `the meeting is an annual meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting an annual meeting of shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must we, the directors, place the diversity information before the shareholders` IF
    `the directors must place the diversity information before the shareholders within s 172.1(1)` `the corporation is a prescribed corporation` `the meeting is an annual meeting of shareholders`

-- s 172.1(1). The duty is met by placing the prescribed information about diversity among the directors and among the members of senior management before the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 172.1(1)
@export Have the directors placed the diversity information before the shareholders as required (s 172.1(1))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a prescribed corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation one that the regulations prescribe for this purpose?
      `the meeting is an annual meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the meeting an annual meeting of shareholders?
      `the prescribed information about diversity among the directors was placed before the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the prescribed information about diversity among the directors placed before the shareholders?
      `the prescribed information about diversity among the members of senior management was placed before the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the prescribed information about diversity among the members of senior management placed before the shareholders?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have the directors placed the diversity information before the shareholders as required` IF
    `the directors have complied with s 172.1(1)` `the corporation is a prescribed corporation` `the meeting is an annual meeting of shareholders` `the prescribed information about diversity among the directors was placed before the shareholders` `the prescribed information about diversity among the members of senior management was placed before the shareholders`

-- s 172.1(2). The corporation shall provide the information to each shareholder, along with the notice referred to in subsection 135(1) or along with the proxy circular, except a shareholder who has informed the corporation in writing that they do not want to receive it.
@ref CBCA s 172.1(2)
@export Must the corporation give me the diversity information (s 172.1(2))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a prescribed corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation one that the regulations prescribe for this purpose?
      `the shareholder has informed the corporation in writing that they do not want to receive the information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you told the corporation in writing that you do not want to receive the information?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation give me the diversity information` IF
    `the corporation must provide the diversity information to a shareholder within s 172.1(2)` `the corporation is a prescribed corporation` `the shareholder has informed the corporation in writing that they do not want to receive the information`

-- s 172.1(2). The information may be sent along with the notice referred to in subsection 135(1) or made available along with a proxy circular referred to in subsection 150(1).
@ref CBCA s 172.1(2)
@export Was the diversity information given to me in a way the Act allows (s 172.1(2))?
GIVEN `the information was sent along with the notice referred to in subsection 135(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information sent along with the notice of the meeting referred to in subsection 135(1)?
      `the information was made available along with a proxy circular referred to in subsection 150(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information made available along with a proxy circular referred to in subsection 150(1)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the diversity information given to me in a way the Act allows` IF
    `the information was provided in a manner the section allows within s 172.1(2)` `the information was sent along with the notice referred to in subsection 135(1)` `the information was made available along with a proxy circular referred to in subsection 150(1)`

-- s 172.1(3). The corporation shall send the information to the Director concurrently with providing it to the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 172.1(3)
@export Must the corporation send the diversity information to the Director (s 172.1(3))?
GIVEN `the corporation is a prescribed corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation one that the regulations prescribe for this purpose?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the corporation send the diversity information to the Director` IF
    `the corporation must send the diversity information to the Director within s 172.1(3)` `the corporation is a prescribed corporation`

-- s 172.1(3). Concurrently: on the same day it is provided to the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 172.1(3)
@export Was the diversity information sent to the Director at the same time as to the shareholders (s 172.1(3))?
GIVEN `the date the information was provided to the shareholders` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the information provided to the shareholders?
      `the date the information was sent to the Director` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the information sent to the Director?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the diversity information sent to the Director at the same time as to the shareholders` IF
    `the information was sent to the Director concurrently within s 172.1(3)` `the date the information was provided to the shareholders` `the date the information was sent to the Director`
